INSERT INTO `latest_news` VALUES
(125,'Netflix warns of slowdown, expects 26% operating margin in fourth quarter','Netflix shares fell after warning of slowdown in revenue growth.','Netflix, share price, revenue growth, US stocks, NSE','<p>Netflix expects an operating margin of 26% during the fourth quarter. This will be impacted by costs associated with job cuts. A company&#039;s operating margin is a measure of its profitability, indicating the percentage of revenue that remains after deducting operating costs. Operating costs include expenses such as salaries and equipment.</p>\n<p>The job cuts are likely to have a significant impact on the company&#039;s costs. Netflix continues to be a leader in subscribers. The company&#039;s subscriber base is a key indicator of its success. Subscribers are customers who pay for a company&#039;s services, in this case, Netflix&#039;s streaming services. This revenue stream is crucial for the company&#039;s financial performance.</p>\n<p>The fall in Netflix shares is a significant development. It highlights the challenges faced by the company. The revenue growth slowdown is a key concern for investors. Revenue growth refers to the increase in a company&#039;s revenue over a certain period, which can impact its stock price. Stock prices can fluctuate based on various factors, including revenue growth and operating margins.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The slowdown in revenue growth is a key factor to consider. Investors will be watching the company&#039;s performance closely. The operating margin of 26% is a key metric to track. Investors use metrics like operating margin to evaluate a company&#039;s financial health and make informed investment decisions. This information can help investors assess the company&#039;s potential for future growth and profitability.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261021-000224-ertukB.jpg',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/netflix-q3-results-revenue-growth-slowdown-warning-new-content-chief-subscribers-viewership-ratings-share-price-20015654.htm','2026-10-21 00:02:25','2026-10-21 00:02:25',0,10,'active','2026-10-21 00:02:25','2026-10-28 03:01:05'),
(126,'Elon Musk considers merger of SpaceX and Tesla, forms special committees','Elon Musk-led SpaceX exceeded expectations and considers merging with Tesla.','SpaceX, Tesla, Elon Musk, merger, Q3 results','<p>SpaceX has reported strong Q3 results, surpassing expectations. Elon Musk, the leader of the company, highlighted the possibility of merging SpaceX with Tesla. This development is notable, as it could lead to a significant change in the industry. A merger is a business combination where two or more companies combine to form a new entity.</p>\n<p>The idea of a merger between the two companies has been discussed, with the boards of both companies forming special committees. These committees will examine the feasibility and potential benefits of a merger between the two companies. The formation of special committees is a common practice in such situations, allowing for a thorough examination of the proposal.</p>\n<p>The process of exploring a merger involves evaluating various factors, including financial and operational aspects. This evaluation is crucial in determining the potential success of a merger. A special committee is typically composed of independent directors and experts who can provide an objective assessment of the proposal.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The potential merger between SpaceX and Tesla could have significant implications for investors. The merger could lead to increased efficiency and cost savings, potentially benefiting shareholders. Investors will likely be watching this development closely, as it could impact the value of their investments in both companies. As investors consider this news, they may also be looking at the broader context of the companies&#039; operations and the industry as a whole.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261021-000245-axaALP.webp',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/spacex-q3-results-xai-rockets-compute-infra-q1-guidance-elon-musk-tesla-merger-share-price-20015649.htm','2026-10-21 00:02:45','2026-10-21 00:02:45',0,18,'active','2026-10-21 00:02:45','2026-10-27 09:48:53'),
(127,'Wealth managers advise mix for Rs 10 lakh investment amid uncertainty','Wealth managers suggest a mix of equities, debt, and gold. This helps investors allocate a lump sum investment.','investment mix, equity markets, wealth managers, debt, gold','<p>Investors are facing challenges in allocating a lump sum investment due to uncertainty in equity markets. Wealth managers are suggesting a combination of equities, debt, and gold to vary the investment portfolio. A lump sum investment of Rs 10 lakh can be allocated in this manner. Equity markets refer to platforms where company shares are bought and sold.</p>\n<p>Wealth managers are experts who help investors manage their wealth. They provide advice on investment options and strategies. In this case, they are suggesting a mix of investments to minimize risk. Debt investments, such as bonds, typically offer relatively stable returns, although the returns may be lower than those from equities.</p>\n<p>A combination of equities, debt, and gold can provide a balanced investment portfolio. This mix can help investors navigate uncertain market conditions. Gold is often used as a hedge against inflation, meaning its value may increase when prices rise. By including gold in a portfolio, investors can reduce their reliance on a single type of investment.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: this suggested investment mix can help them make informed decisions about allocating their Rs 10 lakh lump sum investment. By diversifying their portfolio, investors can reduce their risk and potentially earn stable returns over time. A well-planned investment strategy can help investors achieve their financial goals, and seeking advice from wealth managers can be a useful step in this process.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261021-003049-HH20qc.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Economic Times','https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/investing-rs-10-lakh-experts-decode-the-right-mix/articleshow/135078375.cms','2026-10-21 00:30:49','2026-10-21 00:30:49',0,24,'active','2026-10-21 00:30:49','2026-10-26 00:33:45'),
(128,'Super Micro Computer Inc Sees Strong Preliminary Sales','AI-related companies\' shares rallied after Super Micro\'s strong preliminary results. This brings relief to investors.','Super Micro Computer, AI stocks, server maker, NSE, Sensex, tech stocks','<p>The shares of AI-related companies have seen a significant increase in after-hours trading. This surge is attributed to the strong preliminary results from Super Micro Computer Inc. A server-maker, Super Micro Computer Inc&#039;s results have spurred relief among investors. After-hours trading refers to the buying and selling of shares after the official trading hours of a stock exchange.</p>\n<p>Super Micro Computer Inc&#039;s preliminary results indicate a positive trend for the company. This trend is expected to have a ripple effect on other AI-related companies. As a result, their shares have also seen an increase in value. Preliminary results are initial reports of a company&#039;s financial performance, which can give investors an idea of the company&#039;s overall health.</p>\n<p>The increase in share value of AI-related companies is a notable development. It will be interesting to see how this trend continues in the coming days. A block deal, which is a transaction where a large number of shares are bought or sold, can also impact the share price of a company.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The rally in AI-related companies&#039; shares is a significant event. Investors will be watching the market closely to see if this relief is sustained. The stock market can be volatile, and investors should be aware of the various factors that can impact share prices.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261021-003143-Hw7DWw.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Mint','https://www.livemint.com/market/ai-stocks-rally-after-super-micro-preliminary-sales-bring-relief-11792535998995.html','2026-10-21 00:31:43','2026-10-21 00:31:43',0,19,'active','2026-10-21 00:31:43','2026-10-27 09:47:47'),
(129,'Bajaj Finance faces margin pressure due to Reserve Bank\'s repo rate hike','Bajaj Finance warned of margin compression due to repo rate hike.','Bajaj Finance, share price, NBFC stocks, NSE, Sensex, Q2 results','<p>Bajaj Finance has issued a warning that margin compression could worsen. The Reserve Bank of India&#039;s repo rate hike is a key factor in this prediction. A repo rate hike is when the central bank increases the rate at which it lends to commercial banks, which can have a ripple effect on the economy.</p>\n<p>The company has also provided an update on its assets under management, or AUM. This is a measure of the total value of assets being managed by a financial institution, giving an idea of its scale of operations. Assets under management is an important metric for financial companies like Bajaj Finance.</p>\n<p>The warning from Bajaj Finance is significant because it indicates potential challenges ahead. The company&#039;s guidance on AUM has been increased, which may have some positive implications. This guidance is important for investors to understand the company&#039;s outlook.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: the potential for margin compression could impact Bajaj Finance&#039;s profitability. Investors will be watching the company&#039;s performance closely in the second half of the financial year to see how it navigates these challenges. As investors assess the situation, they will consider how the repo rate hike and AUM guidance affect the company&#039;s overall financial health.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261021-010132-qxrWFg.jpg',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/bajaj-finance-share-price-q2-result-reaction-fy27-guidance-aum-margin-repo-rate-buy-sell-target-outlook-20015660.htm','2026-10-21 01:01:32','2026-10-21 01:01:32',0,18,'active','2026-10-21 01:01:32','2026-10-25 10:39:32'),
(130,'HDFC Bank sees improvement despite 12-quarter low in NIM in Q2 results','HDFC Bank\'s core operating profit grew and asset quality improved. This could help margins recover.','HDFC Bank, NIM, asset quality, core operating profit, banking stocks','<p>HDFC Bank&#039;s net interest margin, or NIM, fell to a 12-quarter low in the second quarter. However, the bank&#039;s core operating profit grew during this period. A key factor that could help the bank&#039;s margins recover is faster growth in higher-yielding loans. NIM is a measure of the difference between the interest income and interest expense of a bank.</p>\n<p>The bank&#039;s asset quality also showed improvement. This is a positive sign for the bank&#039;s overall financial health. A bank&#039;s asset quality is a measure of the quality of its loans and investments. It indicates the level of risk associated with the bank&#039;s lending activities.</p>\n<p>Faster growth in higher-yielding loans could help the bank increase its interest income. This, in turn, could help the bank&#039;s margins recover from the current low levels. The bank&#039;s ability to grow its higher-yielding loans will be closely watched by investors. Core operating profit is a measure of a company&#039;s profitability from its main business activities.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The improvement in HDFC Bank&#039;s core operating profit and asset quality is a positive sign. Investors will be looking for further signs of recovery in the bank&#039;s margins and asset quality in the coming quarters. A block deal is a type of transaction where a large number of shares are bought or sold, and investors may be watching for such deals in HDFC Bank&#039;s stock to gauge market sentiment.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261021-010232-Gaq8Wi.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Mint','https://www.livemint.com/market/mark-to-market/hdfc-bank-q2-quarterly-results-review-11792465354169.html','2026-10-21 01:02:32','2026-10-21 01:02:32',0,20,'active','2026-10-21 01:02:32','2026-10-28 03:11:17'),
(131,'South Indian Bank share price may reach ₹62, says market analysis','South Indian Bank share price may increase to ₹62.','South Indian Bank, share price, bank stocks, NSE, Sensex, Nifty','<p>The current share price of South Indian Bank is ₹54.31. A share price is the amount of money an investor pays to buy one share of a company. The share price can fluctuate based on market conditions.</p>\n<p>The share price of South Indian Bank is projected to reach a resistance level of ₹62. This is an increase from the current price.</p>\n<p>In the stock market, indices like the NSE and Sensex track the performance of stocks. These indices provide a benchmark for investors to evaluate their investments. The NSE and Sensex are widely followed indicators of the Indian stock market&#039;s overall performance.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The potential rise in South Indian Bank&#039;s share price to a resistance level of ₹62 is noted by market analysis. Investors should consider their own financial goals and risk tolerance before making any investment decisions. It is essential for investors to evaluate their investment options carefully and make informed decisions to achieve their financial objectives, taking into account their individual circumstances and market conditions.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261021-013153-MfV4gq.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Hindu BusinessLine','https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/markets/sensex-nifty50-today-stock-market-live-updates-21st-october-2026/article71604730.ece','2026-10-21 01:31:53','2026-10-21 01:31:53',0,14,'active','2026-10-21 01:31:53','2026-10-27 15:53:06'),
(132,'Raja Venkatraman shares stock picks for October 21 trading session today','Market expert Raja Venkatraman shares stock picks for 21 October. His picks are based on technical outlook.','Raja Venkatraman, stock picks, market expert, NSE, BSE, Sensex','<p>Market expert Raja Venkatraman has shared his stock picks for 21 October. He provides a technical outlook and trade strategy for investors. A technical outlook is an analysis of a stock&#039;s price and volume data to predict future price movements.</p>\n<p>Raja Venkatraman&#039;s analysis is provided for investors looking to make decisions. His expertise in the market relates to the NSE, BSE, and Sensex.</p>\n<p>Raja Venkatraman&#039;s stock picks are based on his analysis of market trends and patterns. He has provided three stocks for 21 October. A trade strategy is a plan outlining how to trade stocks to achieve investment goals.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: Raja Venkatraman&#039;s stock picks can provide insights for investors. Investors can review his analysis and do their own research before making any investment decisions. Investors should always consider their own risk tolerance and investment goals before investing. For these stocks, a support can be identified to manage risk, while a resistance level can be used to identify a potential price point.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261021-013207-XYGYFx.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Mint','https://www.livemint.com/market/stock-market-news/raja-venkatraman-recommends-three-stocks-for-21-october-11792418885645.html','2026-10-21 01:32:08','2026-10-21 01:32:08',0,16,'active','2026-10-21 01:32:08','2026-10-27 09:47:28'),
(133,'Reliance Jio\'s massive ₹30,213 crore IPO opens for public subscription today','Jio Platforms launches its IPO today to raise ₹30,213 crore. The issue is a fresh share sale of 27 crore shares.','Reliance Jio, IPO, share price, telecom stocks, NSE, Sensex','<p>The IPO price band for Jio Platforms has been fixed at ₹1,065 to ₹1,119 per share. This price range will be applicable for the subscription period. An initial public offering, or IPO, is a way for companies to raise capital by issuing shares to the public. The IPO process involves several steps, including filing documents with regulatory authorities and marketing the issue to potential investors.</p>\n<p>Jio Platforms is issuing 27 crore fresh shares through this IPO. The company aims to raise approximately ₹30,213 crore from this issue. A fresh issue of shares means that the company is issuing new shares to raise capital. This capital can be used for various purposes, such as expanding business operations or repaying debt.</p>\n<p>The IPO opening today will allow investors to subscribe to the shares within the specified price band. The price band provides a range for investors to consider when deciding how much to invest. This can help investors make informed decisions about their investments. Investors should review the IPO documents and consider their own financial goals before investing.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The IPO of Jio Platforms is a significant event in the Indian stock market. Investors can now subscribe to the shares within the specified price band, and the issue is expected to have a substantial impact on the market. Investors should carefully review the IPO details and consider their investment options before making a decision, keeping in mind their own risk tolerance and investment objectives.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261021-023031-iAOu2O.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Mint','https://www.livemint.com/market/stock-market-news/reliance-jio-ipo-massive-30-213-cr-issue-opens-for-subscription-today-latest-gmp-review-listing-price-prediction-11792548066016.html','2026-10-21 02:30:31','2026-10-21 02:30:31',0,23,'active','2026-10-21 02:30:31','2026-10-27 23:18:53'),
(134,'SBI Data Leak Claim Raised by CyberPulse','CyberPulse flags alleged SBI data leak, authenticity uncertain. Claim involves customer info.','SBI, data leak, cybersecurity, State Bank of India, banking stocks','<p>A claim of a data leak involving State Bank of India customer information has been flagged by CyberPulse. The cybersecurity account noted an unverified claim by threat actor Siriusim. This claim alleges the exposure of 3.75 lakh records and 2,722 PDFs. Cybersecurity refers to the practice of protecting digital information from unauthorized access.</p>\n<p>The authenticity of the claim remains uncertain. CyberPulse has brought this to attention, but the details have not been verified. A data leak can refer to the unauthorized release of sensitive information, which can have serious consequences. In the digital age, cybersecurity is a critical concern for individuals and organizations.</p>\n<p>The alleged leak involves a significant amount of customer information. The claim includes 3.75 lakh records and 2,722 PDFs. This is a notable amount of data, and its exposure could have significant implications. A threat actor, in this context, is an entity that poses a risk to digital security.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The alleged data leak may be a concern for investors in the banking sector, particularly those with interests in State Bank of India. Investors should be aware of the potential risks and consequences associated with data leaks, as they can impact the reputation and operations of a company. As investors monitor this situation, they should consider the potential impact on their investments and the banking sector as a whole.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261021-023101-IM5i0Q.jpg',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/technology/sbi-data-leak-claim-cyberpulse-alleged-exposure-3-75-lakh-records-2722-pdfs-20015714.htm','2026-10-21 02:31:01','2026-10-21 02:31:01',0,29,'active','2026-10-21 02:31:01','2026-10-28 02:36:17'),
(135,'Sterling and Wilson Settles Kenya Tax Demand of ₹26.5 Crore for ₹2.66 Crore','Sterling and Wilson has settled a Kenya tax demand of ₹26.5 crore for ₹2.66 crore, as the firm returned to profit in the September quarter.','Sterling and Wilson, Kenya tax demand, renewable energy, September quarter, profit, stock market, Indian investors, tax settlement','<p>Sterling and Wilson has officially resolved a tax dispute in Kenya by paying ₹2.66 crore against an initial demand of ₹26.5 crore. This settlement represents a reduction of nearly 90% of the original liability requested by the authorities. The company confirmed that this payment concludes the outstanding tax matter in the region.</p>\n<p>In its recent financial performance report, the renewable energy company announced a return to profitability for the September quarter. This positive bottom-line result was achieved even though the firm recorded lower revenue during the same three-month period. A profit occurs when a business earns more money than it spends on its operational costs and obligations.</p>\n<p>The company continues to manage its international tax liabilities as part of its ongoing global operations. By settling this specific demand for ₹2.66 crore, the firm has cleared a significant financial hurdle that previously stood at ₹26.5 crore. Such settlements are often pursued by corporations to resolve legal uncertainties and reduce the potential impact of long-term tax litigation on their balance sheets.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The resolution of this tax issue provides clarity regarding the company&#039;s financial obligations in Kenya. Investors are currently monitoring how the return to profit in the September quarter, despite lower revenue, influences the overall financial health of the business moving forward. This development highlights the company’s current approach to managing its international tax exposures while focusing on its core renewable energy projects and maintaining its operational stability in the global market.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261022-000300-LmS70h.webp',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/sterling-and-wilson-settles-rs26-5-crore-kenya-tax-demand-for-rs2-66-crore-20016470.htm','2026-10-22 00:03:00','2026-10-22 00:03:00',0,15,'active','2026-10-22 00:03:00','2026-10-26 10:07:58'),
(136,'Indian Rupee Reaches Six-Week High Following Jio IPO Inflows and Weaker Dollar','The Indian rupee rose to 94.46 on Wednesday, marking a six-week high after gaining 46 paise due to foreign inflows linked to the Jio IPO and a weaker dollar.','Indian rupee, Jio IPO, foreign portfolio investment, currency market, dollar index, forex','<p>The Indian rupee reached a six-week high of 94.46 on Wednesday, recording a gain of 46 paise from its previous close. This currency movement was driven by strong foreign portfolio inflows linked to the Jio IPO and a weaker dollar. Foreign portfolio investment refers to the entry of funds from overseas investors into domestic financial assets.</p>\n<p>Market participants noted that the currency shift reflected the immediate impact of capital moving into the domestic market. The strengthening of the rupee occurred alongside a weaker dollar in global trade, which influences the exchange rates of emerging market currencies. A weaker dollar makes other currencies appear more valuable in comparison during international transactions.</p>\n<p>The movement in the exchange rate is a reflection of current liquidity conditions and investor activity related to the specific public offering. Traders continue to monitor how global currency trends and local capital flows interact during periods of high activity. These fluctuations are typical of how the currency market reacts to shifts in supply and demand for foreign currency.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: A stronger rupee can influence the cost of imported goods for companies operating within India. It also affects the returns for foreign investors holding domestic assets when they convert gains back into their home currency. Changes in the exchange rate are a standard factor that market participants track to understand the broader economic environment and its potential impact on different sectors.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261022-003051-U7LztB.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Economic Times','https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/forex/rupee-soars-to-6-week-high-on-jio-ipo-flows-weaker-dollar/articleshow/135103368.cms','2026-10-22 00:30:51','2026-10-22 00:30:51',0,20,'active','2026-10-22 00:30:51','2026-10-26 10:02:15'),
(137,'Bitcoin Outperformed Gold and Equities Over Three Years According to CoinDCX Data','Data from CoinDCX shows Bitcoin delivered 234% returns over three years, while precious metals performed better than cryptocurrencies over one year.','Bitcoin, gold, crypto returns, CoinDCX, investment performance, equity markets, silver, digital assets','<p>Recent data from CoinDCX reveals that Bitcoin provided returns of nearly 234% during the last three years. This performance allowed the digital asset to outperform gold, silver, and various equity market investments within that specific timeframe. An equity is a stock or any other security representing an ownership interest in a company.</p>\n<p>The market trends shifted significantly when looking at the most recent one-year period. During this shorter duration, precious metals such as gold and silver recorded better performance results compared to cryptocurrencies. This change occurred as the value of cryptocurrencies experienced a decline over the past twelve months, moving away from the multi-year trend.</p>\n<p>Investors often track these diverse asset classes to understand how different markets move in relation to one another. While digital assets showed substantial gains over the three-year window, the recent volatility highlights the difference in performance across various time frames. A block deal is a single transaction of a large number of shares at a negotiated price between two institutional investors.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The data highlights that asset performance varies depending on the chosen time horizon. While Bitcoin led over three years, the recent one-year period favored precious metals, showing that market leadership can shift as asset values fluctuate. Investors should observe how these different categories, including equities and commodities, respond to changing market conditions over both long and short periods to better understand their portfolio dynamics.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261022-003208-nnMIHD.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Economic Times','https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/cryptocurrency/crypto-news/stocks-gold-or-crypto-the-last-3-years-returns-have-a-surprising-answer/articleshow/135096080.cms','2026-10-22 00:32:08','2026-10-22 00:32:08',0,47,'active','2026-10-22 00:32:08','2026-10-26 10:00:29'),
(138,'Tech Mahindra Board Announces Bonus Issue of Shares for Company Shareholders','The board of directors at Tech Mahindra has officially declared a bonus issue of shares, sparking discussions about the impact on current stock holdings.','Tech Mahindra, bonus issue, share price, stock market, NSE, BSE, corporate action','<p>The board of directors at Tech Mahindra has officially declared a bonus issue of shares. This corporate action involves the distribution of additional shares to existing shareholders without any extra cost. A bonus issue is a method used by companies to increase the number of outstanding shares in the market by capitalizing reserves.</p>\n<p>Investors are currently evaluating the implications of this announcement regarding their holdings in the company. Market participants often track such developments closely as they alter the equity structure of the firm. While the total value of the company remains the same, the number of shares held by each investor increases proportionally following the distribution.</p>\n<p>The decision by the board follows standard corporate governance procedures for issuing bonus equity. Shareholders typically receive these additional units based on a specific ratio determined by the company management. This process does not involve any cash outflow from the company, as it is funded through the conversion of existing free reserves into paid-up capital.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The bonus issue will result in an increase in the total volume of shares held by individual investors. Because the total market capitalization is spread across more shares, the price per share typically adjusts downward on the ex-bonus date. Investors should monitor official notifications for the record date to determine eligibility for receiving these additional shares. This development remains a point of focus for those tracking the company&#039;s capital allocation.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261022-010109-Wwcuim.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Mint','https://www.livemint.com/market/stock-market-news/tech-mahindra-bonus-issue-a-sweet-deal-or-market-trap-11792582032984.html','2026-10-22 01:01:09','2026-10-22 01:01:09',0,26,'active','2026-10-22 01:01:09','2026-10-26 11:53:28'),
(139,'Bond Yield Rises to 7.44% Following Higher Oil Prices and Global Cues','The benchmark 10-year bond yield hit 7.44% as oil prices climbed. The Reserve Bank of India also rejected all bids at its recent treasury bill auction.','bond yield, 10-year benchmark bond, Reserve Bank of India, treasury bill auction, oil prices, Indian economy, interest rates','<p>The yield on the 10-year benchmark bond has climbed to 7.44% recently. This movement in the debt market follows rising global oil prices and various global cues that have influenced investor sentiment. Bond yields move inversely to bond prices, meaning that as market prices for existing bonds fall, the effective yield for new investors increases.</p>\n<p>The Reserve Bank of India conducted a treasury bill auction recently where it decided to reject all bids submitted by participants. A treasury bill auction is a process where the central bank sells short-term debt instruments to manage liquidity in the financial system. By choosing not to accept any bids, the central bank maintained its current stance regarding the supply of these short-term government securities.</p>\n<p>Market participants are currently monitoring these shifts closely as the cost of borrowing often aligns with government bond yields. These figures are influenced by a variety of macroeconomic factors, including the price of crude oil, which impacts inflation expectations and the overall fiscal situation. Global cues remain a significant driver for how domestic debt instruments are priced during daily trading sessions on the exchanges.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: Changes in benchmark bond yields often serve as a gauge for broader interest rate trends in the economy. When yields rise, it can reflect changing expectations about future monetary policy and inflation. Investors typically watch these fluctuations to understand how the cost of debt might shift for both the government and private sector borrowers in the coming months.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261022-010208-IHBzOI.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Economic Times','https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/bonds/bond-yield-rises-to-7-44-on-higher-oil-prices-global-cues/articleshow/135103005.cms','2026-10-22 01:02:08','2026-10-22 01:02:08',0,21,'active','2026-10-22 01:02:08','2026-10-26 10:22:53'),
(140,'HCL Technologies Share Price Analysis and Market Performance Today','HCL Technologies shares are currently priced at 1,423.85 with potential to reach 1,580. Investors are monitoring these levels amid broader market movements.','HCL Technologies share price, HCL Tech stock, NSE, Sensex, Indian stock market, HCL Technologies analysis, IT sector stocks','<p>The HCL Technologies share price is currently trading at 1,423.85. Market analysts have indicated that the stock price has the potential to rise to a target of 1,580. These figures are being closely tracked by market participants as they observe the movement of the Sensex and Nifty indices throughout the ongoing trading session.</p>\n<p>A block deal occurs when a large number of shares are traded between two parties at a fixed price outside the open market. This mechanism is often used by institutional investors to execute large orders without causing significant volatility in the daily share price of the company.</p>\n<p>Investors frequently monitor these price fluctuations to understand the current sentiment surrounding major IT companies. The performance of individual stocks like HCL Technologies often contributes to the overall movement of the benchmark indices, which reflect the collective performance of the largest companies listed on the Indian stock exchanges.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The current price of 1,423.85 and the target of 1,580 represent specific data points for those tracking the performance of the company. Understanding these price levels helps in observing how individual stocks align with the broader trends observed in the Sensex and Nifty. Market participants often review these figures to remain updated on the latest shifts in stock valuations during live trading sessions. It is important to note that these values are based on current market data and reflect the ongoing activity within the technology sector as it interacts with the wider financial environment.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261022-013122-T8FFNR.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Hindu BusinessLine','https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/markets/sensex-nifty50-today-stock-market-live-updates-22nd-october-2026/article71608127.ece','2026-10-22 01:31:22','2026-10-22 01:31:22',0,76,'active','2026-10-22 01:31:22','2026-10-28 05:04:15'),
(141,'IBM Reports 5% Sales Growth And Raises Annual Software Revenue Outlook For Q3','IBM achieved $17.1 billion in sales for the third quarter, surpassing analyst estimates as software revenue reached $7.8 billion and infrastructure recovered.','IBM, IBM share price, US tech stocks, global IT sector, software revenue, quarterly results, international markets','<p>IBM has officially announced its third-quarter financial results, reporting a 5% increase in total sales reaching $17.1 billion. The company also confirmed an upward revision to its annual software revenue outlook. This performance was driven by a recovery in deferred infrastructure contracts alongside strong gains in the software division, which contributed $7.8 billion to the overall quarterly total.</p>\n<p>The reported figures surpassed the specific expectations previously set by market analysts. Software revenue represents the income generated by a company through the sale of programs and digital applications rather than physical hardware. By achieving these results, the organization has demonstrated a shift in its financial trajectory compared to previous reporting periods.</p>\n<p>The recovery of deferred infrastructure contracts indicates that previously signed deals for computing systems and related services have now been processed. These contracts are legal agreements where clients commit to long-term hardware or support services. The improvement in this specific segment was a primary factor in the company exceeding its projected sales targets for the three-month period.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The updated annual outlook suggests a change in the company’s anticipated financial performance for the remainder of the year. Investors often monitor changes to revenue guidance to understand how a firm views its future demand. While these results reflect the current operational status of the business, they also provide a clear benchmark for how the software and infrastructure segments are performing in the current economic environment.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261022-013213-caQLor.jpg',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/ibm-q3-results-tech-behemoth-records-5-sales-growth-raises-annual-software-revenue-outlook-20016516.htm','2026-10-22 01:32:14','2026-10-22 01:32:14',0,14,'active','2026-10-22 01:32:14','2026-10-26 09:54:01'),
(142,'Motilal Oswal Predicts 35% Upside for Eternal Shares Following Q2 Results','Motilal Oswal forecasts a 35% rise for Eternal shares after Q2 results, while Bernstein notes upside risks to the company\'s 60% growth guidance.','Eternal share price, Motilal Oswal, Bernstein, Q2 results, stock market, Indian investors, growth guidance, equity research','<p>Motilal Oswal has projected that the Eternal share price could increase by 35% following the release of the company&#039;s Q2 results. In a separate assessment, Bernstein has highlighted potential upside risks regarding the financial year 2026-2029 Net Order Value Compounded Annual Growth Rate (CAGR) guidance of over 60% provided by Eternal.</p>\n<p>The CAGR is a financial metric that measures the mean annual growth rate of an investment over a specified period of time longer than one year. These analyst reports focus on the performance indicators and future growth targets disclosed by the firm to the market. While Motilal Oswal has issued a specific price projection, Bernstein has concentrated its analysis on the sustainability of the order value growth targets mentioned for the upcoming fiscal years.</p>\n<p>Investors often track these analyst reports to understand how professional firms interpret the financial data and future outlooks provided by publicly traded companies. These projections are based on the current financial statements and the long-term guidance shared by the management team. Analysts frequently update their models to reflect the latest quarterly performance and the evolving market conditions that might impact the company&#039;s ability to meet its stated goals.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: These analyst updates reflect different perspectives on the growth trajectory and valuation of Eternal following its recent quarterly financial disclosure. Market participants typically observe such revisions to align their own assessments with the latest expert projections regarding the potential movement of the stock price and the underlying business growth targets.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261022-020040-fwkP0v.jpg',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/eternal-share-price-q2-result-reaction-buy-sell-upside-target-blinkit-zomato-growth-outlook-returns-20016533.htm','2026-10-22 02:00:40','2026-10-22 02:00:40',0,28,'active','2026-10-22 02:00:40','2026-10-28 00:39:44'),
(143,'Nifty PSU Bank and Nifty Private Bank Indices Show Strength on Market Charts','Nandish Shah of HDFC Securities indicates that both banking indices show strength, though the Nifty PSU Bank index currently holds a more favourable bias.','Nifty PSU Bank, Nifty Private Bank, HDFC Securities, Nandish Shah, banking indices, NSE, stock market analysis, Indian banking sector','<p>Nandish Shah of HDFC Securities has provided an update on the current technical positioning of the Nifty PSU Bank and Nifty Private Bank indices. According to his analysis, both banking indices show strength on the charts. However, the market bias is currently more favourable for the Nifty PSU Bank index compared to its private sector counterpart.</p>\n<p>Technical analysis involves studying historical price movements and trading volumes to forecast future trends. Investors often use these charts to identify potential momentum shifts within specific sectors of the economy. By evaluating the performance of these indices, market participants can observe how different groups of financial institutions are trending relative to one another in the current environment.</p>\n<p>The Nifty PSU Bank index tracks the performance of public sector banks, while the Nifty Private Bank index monitors the performance of private sector lenders. These indices serve as benchmarks for investors to gauge the health and direction of the banking industry. Monitoring these specific indices provides a clearer picture of how various institutional categories are reacting to ongoing market conditions and shifting investor sentiment.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The assessment by Nandish Shah highlights a technical preference for public sector lenders over private banks based on current chart patterns. Investors who follow technical indicators may use this information to understand the prevailing momentum within the banking sector. Market participants should continue to monitor broader economic data and individual stock performance to make informed decisions regarding their portfolios in the evolving financial landscape.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261022-042511-aRJH7L.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Business Standard','https://www.business-standard.com/markets/news/nifty-psu-vs-private-bank-which-banking-index-looks-stronger-on-charts-126102200199_1.html','2026-10-22 04:25:11','2026-10-22 04:25:11',0,17,'active','2026-10-22 04:25:11','2026-10-26 10:02:51'),
(144,'Meta Reports 26% Revenue Growth And 264% Net Income Jump In Q3','Meta announced a significant rise in Q3 revenue to $64.6 billion. Net income surged as the company reported higher diluted earnings per share for the period.','Meta, Meta revenue, Meta Q3 results, US tech stocks, global markets, stock market, NASDAQ, investing','<p>Meta has officially released its third-quarter financial performance, showing that revenue reached $64.6 billion, representing a 26% increase. During the same period, the company recorded a 264% jump in net income, which rose from the previous figure of $2.71 billion. These financial results highlight the recent monetary activity for the firm during the third quarter.</p>\n<p>The report also detailed changes in shareholder earnings, noting that diluted earnings per share climbed to $3.83. This is a notable shift from the $1.05 reported in the prior period. Diluted earnings per share is a calculation that accounts for all convertible securities that could potentially be exercised, providing a comprehensive view of profitability per share.</p>\n<p>Market participants often track these quarterly disclosures to understand the financial trajectory of international technology corporations. Such reports are typically filed with regulatory authorities to ensure transparency for global stakeholders and institutional investors. These documents provide a standardized breakdown of how a company utilizes its capital and manages its operational costs over a three-month window.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The financial data provided by Meta offers a clear picture of its recent earnings growth and profitability trends. Indian investors tracking global technology trends may review these specific figures to understand how international market conditions influence the broader financial ecosystem. By examining the reported $64.6 billion in revenue and the shift in earnings per share, stakeholders can assess the reported performance metrics against their own financial objectives and portfolio strategies within the global equity space.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261022-042551-5Rhekv.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Hindu BusinessLine','https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/info-tech/meta-q3-revenue-rises-26-to-646-billion-net-income-jumps-264/article71610031.ece','2026-10-22 04:25:51','2026-10-22 04:25:51',0,21,'active','2026-10-22 04:25:51','2026-10-27 16:26:46'),
(145,'Meta Share Price Drops 7.5 Percent Following Revised Capital Spending Outlook','Meta shares fell 7.5% as the firm increased its capital expenditure forecast to $145 billion to support AI, despite beating Q3 revenue expectations.','Meta share price, US stock market, AI investment, Meta Q3 results, tech stocks, global markets, investment news','<p>Meta shares recorded a decline of 7.5% recently, even though the parent company of Facebook reported quarterly revenue that surpassed market expectations. This movement followed the announcement that the firm is raising its capital-spending outlook to as much as $145 billion. Capital expenditure refers to the funds a company uses to acquire, upgrade, and maintain physical assets such as buildings, technology, or equipment.</p>\n<p>The decision to increase spending is specifically linked to the company’s ongoing efforts to advance its artificial intelligence strategy. While the latest quarterly revenue figures were positive, the market reacted to the updated financial guidance regarding future investments. These figures represent a significant adjustment in the expected operational costs for the business moving forward.</p>\n<p>Investors are currently evaluating how this increased investment in AI infrastructure will impact the company&#039;s financial position in the coming periods. The adjustment to the $145 billion figure serves as a primary indicator of the firm&#039;s focus on long-term technological development. Analysts are watching these developments closely to understand the balance between current revenue growth and the high costs associated with new software and hardware initiatives.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The drop in share price highlights how market participants often weigh future spending commitments against current earnings performance. When a company announces a large increase in capital expenditure, investors frequently assess whether the potential long-term benefits of such technology spending justify the immediate impact on the company&#039;s balance sheet and cash flow.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261023-003316-CmUnIy.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Mint','https://www.livemint.com/market/stock-market-news/meta-share-price-stock-slumps-7-5-despite-upbeat-q3-results-why-is-facebook-parent-falling-11792689825393.html','2026-10-23 00:33:17','2026-10-23 00:33:17',0,26,'active','2026-10-23 00:33:17','2026-10-27 12:30:39'),
(146,'Piyush Goyal Invites European Investors to India, Criticizes China Over Jack Ma','Commerce Minister Piyush Goyal invited European businesses to invest in India, highlighting the country\'s predictable business environment and market access.','Piyush Goyal, European investment, India business environment, FDI, Jack Ma, China, trade','<p>Commerce Minister Piyush Goyal has invited European investors to expand their operations in India, emphasizing that the nation provides a transparent and predictable business environment. During his recent interaction, Goyal highlighted that India offers companies reliable access to global markets through various free trade agreements.</p>\n<p>The minister specifically contrasted the Indian approach to business with the situation in China. He made a direct reference to the case of Jack Ma, the founder of Alibaba, to illustrate his point regarding the differences in how countries handle private enterprise and corporate leadership. Goyal suggested that India maintains a system based on fair play and consistent regulatory standards for all participants.</p>\n<p>Foreign Direct Investment, or FDI, refers to an investment made by a firm or individual in one country into business interests located in another country. By promoting these benefits, the government aims to position the domestic economy as a stable destination for international capital seeking long-term growth opportunities outside of traditional markets. This outreach is part of a broader effort to strengthen economic ties with European partners.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: Increased foreign investment can influence the broader economic landscape and domestic industrial growth. Market participants often track government statements regarding international trade and policy stability to gauge the potential for future capital inflows into the country. Investors should monitor how these diplomatic engagements translate into actual policy changes and corporate expansion within the local market over the coming period.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261023-003327-PDomjL.jpg',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/business/goyal-tells-european-investors-india-offers-fair-play-takes-swipe-at-china-over-jack-ma-20017471.htm','2026-10-23 00:33:27','2026-10-23 00:33:27',0,32,'active','2026-10-23 00:33:27','2026-10-27 13:17:34'),
(147,'Indian Rupee Falls Against Dollar As Brent Oil Prices Cross $112 Mark','The Indian rupee saw its first decline in eight sessions as Brent oil prices rose above $112, despite foreign inflows for the Jio Platforms IPO.','Indian rupee, Brent oil, Jio Platforms IPO, currency market, foreign investment, forex','<p>The Indian rupee experienced a decline on Thursday, marking its first drop in eight trading sessions as Brent oil prices climbed to levels above $112. This movement in the currency value occurred simultaneously with foreign portfolio investment inflows linked to the Jio Platforms IPO. An initial public offering, or IPO, is the process by which a private company offers its shares to the public for the first time to raise capital.</p>\n<p>Market participants observed this shift in the currency valuation during the Thursday trading window. The rise in global crude oil prices often impacts the domestic currency, as India imports a significant portion of its oil requirements. Foreign portfolio investment refers to the entry of funds from overseas investors into the domestic financial markets through various instruments.</p>\n<p>The ongoing interest in the Jio Platforms IPO has facilitated foreign capital inflows into the Indian market. These investments represent a notable activity within the broader financial landscape. Such inflows are monitored closely by market observers as they influence the overall liquidity and supply of foreign currency within the domestic banking system.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: Fluctuations in the currency market can influence the cost of imports and domestic inflation levels. Changes in the exchange rate may affect sectors that rely heavily on imported raw materials or those with significant international debt obligations. Investors typically track these currency trends to understand broader macroeconomic shifts that could impact their portfolio performance in the local equity and bond markets over the coming sessions.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261023-010215-jyupTG.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Economic Times','https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/forex/rupee-declines-first-time-in-eight-sessions-as-brent-oil-prices-rise-above-112/articleshow/135130676.cms','2026-10-23 01:02:15','2026-10-23 01:02:15',0,18,'active','2026-10-23 01:02:15','2026-10-26 01:33:57'),
(148,'Tata Motors Revised Offer Could Net Three Iveco Investors €63 Million Gain','Three Iveco investors are positioned for a €63 million gain as Tata Motors pursues a buyout at a revised share price of €14.40.','Tata Motors, Iveco, buyout, share price, international investment, stock market, corporate news, acquisition','<p>Three investors in Iveco stand to receive a combined gain of approximately €63 million following a revised buyout offer from Tata Motors. This financial outcome is based on the updated offer price of €14.40 per share. Beyond this potential gain, these investors are also set to receive an estimated €288 million in extraordinary dividends.</p>\n<p>A buyout occurs when one company acquires a controlling stake in another entity, often involving the purchase of outstanding shares from existing shareholders. The transaction remains a central focus as Tata Motors works to secure the necessary agreements to finalize the acquisition process. These figures represent the current valuation parameters set forth in the ongoing negotiations between the involved parties.</p>\n<p>The total financial impact for the three stakeholders involves both the capital appreciation from the per-share offer price and the additional extraordinary dividend payments. These amounts are calculated based on the specific terms disclosed regarding the revised bid. The process highlights the complexity of international corporate acquisitions and the specific financial benefits that can arise for major shareholders during such transitions.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The development underscores how revised offer prices directly influence the potential returns for existing shareholders during corporate buyouts. Monitoring these specific financial terms is essential for those tracking the progress of this transaction. While the deal remains in motion, the current figures provide a clear picture of the projected gains for the three investors involved in the Iveco acquisition process.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261023-010236-zR32vU.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Mint','https://www.livemint.com/companies/tata-motors-iveco-acquisition-deal-status-shareholders-approval-11792650839298.html','2026-10-23 01:02:36','2026-10-23 01:02:36',0,47,'active','2026-10-23 01:02:36','2026-10-27 23:40:07'),
(149,'Stock Market Outlook for 23 October 2026 Featuring Global Market Cues','On 23 October 2026, GIFT Nifty shows positive momentum as international indices provide cues for the upcoming session in the Indian stock market.','Stock market, GIFT Nifty, Sensex, Nifty, global markets, 23 October 2026, trading','<p>On 23 October 2026, the stock market outlook is influenced by signals from the DJIA, S&amp;P, NASDAQ, GIFT Nifty, Kospi, Nikkei, and Taiwan markets. The GIFT Nifty was trading around the 22,800 level, representing an increase of nearly 165 points or 0.73% compared to the previous close of Nifty futures. These figures provide a baseline for how the Sensex and Nifty might react during the trading session. Futures are financial contracts to buy or sell assets at a set future date.</p>\n<p>International market performance sets the tone for domestic trading activity. The movement in the DJIA, S&amp;P, and NASDAQ often dictates sentiment for stocks globally. Meanwhile, the performance of the Kospi, Nikkei, and Taiwan indices offers insights into the broader Asian market environment. Investors monitor these foreign benchmarks to gauge potential volatility and shifts in liquidity across various sectors before the opening bell.</p>\n<p>Market participants use these regional and global indicators to assess the daily trajectory of major domestic indices. The 0.73% rise in the GIFT Nifty suggests that external factors are exerting pressure on local futures. By tracking the 22,800 level, traders attempt to identify support and resistance zones for the day.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The current data reflects a snapshot of global sentiment that may influence local price action. Monitoring these international cues helps in understanding the broader market context during the 23 October 2026 session.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261023-013040-mgXd2k.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Mint','https://www.livemint.com/market/stock-market-news/stock-market-outlook-today-23-oct-sensex-nifty-prediction-djia-s-p-nasdaq-gift-nifty-kospi-nikkei-taiwan-11792716174246.html','2026-10-23 01:30:40','2026-10-23 01:30:40',0,66,'active','2026-10-23 01:30:40','2026-10-28 03:10:38'),
(150,'Fusion CX Shares Listed at 5.54 Percent Premium on the NSE Exchange','Fusion CX shares began trading at ₹305 on the NSE, marking a 5.54% premium over the issue price of ₹289. The stock eventually closed at ₹289.65.','Fusion CX, Fusion CX share price, NSE, stock market, IPO listing, Indian stock market','<p>Fusion CX shares officially commenced trading on the National Stock Exchange at a price of ₹305. This debut price represents a premium of 5.54% when compared to the established issue price of ₹289 per share. By the conclusion of the trading session, the stock price settled at ₹289.65. An initial public offering, or IPO, is the process by which a private company offers its shares to the public for the first time.</p>\n<p>The listing process on the NSE allows investors to trade company shares throughout the day during market hours. The movement from the opening price to the final closing price reflects the intraday trading activity observed by market participants. Investors typically monitor these opening movements to gauge the immediate reception of a new stock following its issuance.</p>\n<p>Trading volume on the exchange provides liquidity for those looking to buy or sell their holdings after the initial offering period ends. Market participants track these figures to understand how the supply and demand dynamics influence the price of the security on its inaugural day. This data is recorded by the exchange to ensure transparency for all public investors.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The listing performance highlights the gap between the set issue price and the price determined by market forces. Shareholders should note the closing price of ₹289.65 as a reference point for future sessions. Monitoring such price fluctuations is a standard practice for those observing the performance of newly listed entities in the current financial environment.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261023-020103-7ZXWO5.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Economic Times','https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/fusion-cx-debuts-at-5-5-premium/articleshow/135131473.cms','2026-10-23 02:01:03','2026-10-23 02:01:03',0,24,'active','2026-10-23 02:01:03','2026-10-28 04:59:30'),
(151,'Zetwerk Shares Surge Over 5 Percent During Trading Debut on NSE','Zetwerk shares began trading on the NSE at ₹159.25, marking a rise of over 5% from the initial public offering price of ₹151 per share.','Zetwerk share price, NSE listing, IPO debut, stock market, Zetwerk IPO, Indian stock market, NSE','<p>Zetwerk shares officially started trading on the National Stock Exchange today following a successful initial public offering that raised $518 million. The stock opened at a price of ₹159.25, which represents a gain of more than 5% when compared to the company’s original issue price of ₹151 per share. An initial public offering is the process by which a private company offers its shares to the public for the first time to raise capital.</p>\n<p>The market performance of Zetwerk during its debut session reflects the initial investor interest following the completion of the $518 million public issue. Investors closely monitor these opening day price movements to determine the immediate valuation of the company as established by the broader market participants on the exchange.</p>\n<p>The trading activity on the NSE remained steady as the stock maintained its position above the issue price of ₹151 throughout the early hours of the session. Market participants are now observing the price action to identify a potential support level or a resistance level for the stock as it continues to trade in the open market environment.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The debut performance of Zetwerk provides data on how the market values the company relative to its $518 million IPO price. While the stock rose over 5% from the ₹151 issue price to reach ₹159.25, market participants should continue to track the daily trading volume and price fluctuations to assess the ongoing liquidity of the shares on the exchange.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261023-050444-kFpStz.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Hindu BusinessLine','https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/markets/stock-markets/indias-zetwerk-rises-over-5-in-trading-debut-after-518-million-ipo/article71614554.ece','2026-10-23 05:04:44','2026-10-23 05:04:44',0,19,'active','2026-10-23 05:04:44','2026-10-27 06:01:03'),
(152,'Sorbh Gupta of Bajaj Asset Management Recommends Five-Year SIP Horizon for Smallcap Investors','Sorbh Gupta of Bajaj Asset Management Limited suggests a five-year SIP investment horizon for those looking at smallcap exposure amid current market volatility.','Sorbh Gupta, Bajaj Asset Management, smallcap stocks, SIP, investment strategy, market volatility, Indian mutual funds','<p>In a recent discussion with Kshitij Anand, Sorbh Gupta, Head of Equity at Bajaj Asset Management Limited, addressed the current state of equity markets. He noted that investors interested in smallcap exposure should consider a five-year SIP horizon to navigate ongoing market volatility. A Systematic Investment Plan, or SIP, is a method where investors contribute a fixed amount of money at regular intervals into a mutual fund scheme.</p>\n<p>The conversation focused on the challenges posed by fluctuating conditions and how a disciplined approach might assist participants. By extending the timeframe for investments, individuals may better manage risks associated with short-term price swings in smaller companies. This strategy emphasizes the importance of staying invested over a longer period rather than attempting to time the market movements.</p>\n<p>Smallcap stocks represent shares of companies with smaller market capitalizations, which are often subject to higher price fluctuations compared to larger firms. Gupta highlighted that the five-year duration is a relevant consideration for those building their portfolios in this specific category. His commentary provides a perspective on managing expectations when dealing with assets that experience frequent changes in valuation.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The suggestion to adopt a five-year SIP horizon serves as a reminder that long-term commitment is a way to handle volatility. Investors should evaluate their personal risk tolerance and financial goals before deciding if smallcap exposure aligns with their overall strategy in the current market environment.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261023-050452-wLwFbA.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Economic Times','https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/expert-view/etmarkets-smart-talk-smallcap-investors-should-consider-a-five-year-sip-horizon-amid-volatility-sorbh-gupta/articleshow/135134298.cms','2026-10-23 05:04:52','2026-10-23 05:04:52',0,22,'active','2026-10-23 05:04:52','2026-10-27 11:41:50'),
(153,'IT Stocks Rally as Nifty IT Index Climbs Over 3 Percent Today','IT stocks including TCS, Infosys, HCL Tech, and Wipro rose sharply today as the Nifty IT index gained 3.3 percent following strong September-quarter results.','TCS share price, Infosys share, HCL Tech stock, Wipro share, Nifty IT index, Indian IT stocks, NSE, stock market news','<p>Shares of major Indian technology firms including TCS, Infosys, HCL Tech, and Wipro saw a significant surge during today’s trading session. The Nifty IT index climbed by 3.3 percent, marking a notable jump of 22 percent from its low point recorded in July. This upward movement reflects a positive trend within the technology sector as trading progressed throughout the day.</p>\n<p>The rally in these technology stocks follows the release of September-quarter results. These financial disclosures were stronger than market participants had previously anticipated. The reported data has helped to reduce various concerns regarding the current demand for information technology services. Furthermore, the results addressed ongoing discussions surrounding the potential impact of artificial intelligence disruption on the operations of these major firms.</p>\n<p>Indices like the Nifty IT represent a basket of stocks from a specific sector, allowing investors to track the performance of that industry as a whole. By monitoring these benchmarks, market participants observe how specific segments of the economy react to corporate earnings. The recent performance indicates a shift in sentiment for these specific companies after their latest financial updates were made public.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The recent price movement in the IT sector highlights how quarterly performance reports influence market sentiment. Investors often watch these indices to gauge sector health, while keeping an eye on a resistance level or support when evaluating their positions in individual technology stocks during periods of increased market activity.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261023-051323-72crZ8.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Mint','https://www.livemint.com/market/stock-market-news/top-stocks-to-buy-it-stocks-soar-tcs-infosys-hcl-tech-wipro-nifty-it-up-over-3-today-jumps-22-from-july-low-11792729456440.html','2026-10-23 05:13:23','2026-10-23 05:13:23',0,61,'active','2026-10-23 05:13:23','2026-10-28 04:39:00'),
(154,'Sensex Drops Over 400 Points and Nifty Falls Below 22,500 Amid Market Volatility','The Indian stock market saw sharp declines as Sensex and Nifty dropped while small and midcap indices fell by up to 3% due to rising global oil prices.','Sensex, Nifty, Indian stock market, smallcap, midcap, oil prices, Dalal Street','<p>The Indian stock market witnessed a sharp decline today as the Sensex dropped over 400 points and the Nifty fell below 22,500. This downward trend was further intensified as small and midcap indices plunged by up to 3%. These indices represent the performance of companies with smaller market capitalizations compared to the large-cap stocks found in the main benchmarks.</p>\n<p>The current market movement follows a period where oil prices have soared globally. When crude oil prices rise, it often impacts the trade deficit and inflation levels within the domestic economy, which can influence investor sentiment across various sectors. Market participants are closely monitoring these shifts as they navigate the recent pressure on broader indices.</p>\n<p>Investors often look at these indices to gauge the health of the overall market. A block deal is a single transaction of a large number of shares between two parties, often conducted outside the open market to prevent price volatility. While the main indices are seeing significant downturns, the performance of the smaller stocks indicates a broader retreat across the various segments of the exchange.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The current volatility highlights the importance of monitoring global commodity trends and their impact on local market benchmarks. Traders often track these price movements to identify a potential support level or a resistance level for their portfolios. Maintaining a disciplined approach remains essential when dealing with sudden fluctuations in the equity market, as external economic factors continue to influence daily trading activity on Dalal Street.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261023-051331-o7K3rk.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Economic Times','https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/sensex-drops-over-400-points-nifty-below-22500-while-small-midcap-indices-plunge-up-to-3-what-lies-ahead-for-dalal-street/articleshow/135134693.cms','2026-10-23 05:13:31','2026-10-23 05:13:31',0,23,'active','2026-10-23 05:13:31','2026-10-27 10:32:13'),
(155,'Godrej Properties Reports 62% Drop in Q2FY27 Net Profit to ₹154 Crore','Godrej Properties saw its Q2FY27 net profit decline by 62% to ₹154 crore, even as total income grew by 38% compared to the previous year.','Godrej Properties, Q2FY27 results, real estate stocks, NSE, Indian stock market, quarterly earnings, property developer, investment news','<p>Godrej Properties announced its financial results for the second quarter of the fiscal year 2027, reporting a net profit of ₹154 crore. This figure represents a 62% decline compared to the same period in the previous year. Despite the drop in bottom-line profitability, the company recorded a 38% year-on-year increase in its total income.</p>\n<p>The company noted that these quarterly figures were influenced by specific operational factors. While the net profit saw a significant contraction, the business achieved record first-half bookings. Additionally, the firm experienced higher cash collections during this period, which served to offset the impact of the weaker quarterly earnings performance reported for the current quarter.</p>\n<p>A quarterly result is a financial report released by a company every three months to provide updates on its revenue, expenses, and overall profit or loss. Investors monitor these disclosures to track the operational efficiency and financial health of the firm over a specific timeframe. The data provided reflects the performance of the entity during the three-month duration ending in the second quarter of the fiscal year.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The financial data shows a divergence between the yearly income growth of 38% and the 62% net profit decline. Market participants often track these metrics to evaluate how management handles operational expenses and revenue generation. The company remains focused on its bookings and cash collection cycles as key performance indicators for its upcoming fiscal activities.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261024-000324-tkJnQe.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Business Standard','https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/godrej-properties-q2fy27-results-net-profit-falls-62-to-154-crore-126102400024_1.html','2026-10-24 00:03:24','2026-10-24 00:03:24',0,18,'active','2026-10-24 00:03:24','2026-10-27 06:28:13'),
(156,'Commerce Ministry and EEPC India Plan Engineering Exports Growth to $250 Billion by 2030','The Commerce Ministry and EEPC India are collaborating on a strategy to increase engineering exports to $250 billion by the year 2030.','Engineering exports, Commerce Ministry, EEPC India, export roadmap, Indian trade, manufacturing','<p>The Commerce Ministry and EEPC India recently held discussions to establish a comprehensive roadmap aimed at increasing engineering exports to $250 billion by 2030. This initiative focuses on enhancing the presence of Indian engineering goods within the global marketplace. The target reflects a strategic effort to scale up the sector&#039;s contribution to the national economy over the next several years.</p>\n<p>Officials are exploring ways to leverage existing free trade agreements to provide exporters with better market access. A free trade agreement is a pact between two or more nations to reduce barriers to imports and exports among them. By removing these hurdles, the government intends to make Indian engineering products more competitive against international alternatives.</p>\n<p>The proposed roadmap also prioritizes improved access to essential raw materials for domestic manufacturers. Ensuring a steady and affordable supply of these inputs is considered vital for maintaining production schedules and export volumes. The discussions between the ministry and the council highlighted the need for closer cooperation between the industry and the government to address logistical and supply chain challenges effectively.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The focus on reaching the $250 billion target suggests a long-term emphasis on export-oriented engineering firms. Investors should monitor how these policy changes influence the operational costs and global market reach of companies within this sector. While the roadmap outlines clear goals for 2030, the actual performance of engineering stocks will depend on how successfully these government initiatives are implemented and adopted by the industry participants.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261024-000428-XXhZZd.jpg',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/business/india-engineering-exports-250-billion-target-2030-20018424.htm','2026-10-24 00:04:28','2026-10-24 00:04:28',0,17,'active','2026-10-24 00:04:28','2026-10-27 11:32:34'),
(157,'Sebi Directs Avadhut Sathe Trading Academy and Founder to Refund Rs 546.17 Crore','The market regulator has ordered Avadhut Sathe Trading Academy and its founder to return funds collected from participants for various programs.','Sebi, Avadhut Sathe Trading Academy, Avadhut Sathe, investor protection, market regulator, financial fraud, refund order','<p>On Friday, the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Sebi) issued a formal directive requiring Avadhut Sathe Trading Academy Pvt Ltd (ASTAPL) and its founder, Avadhut Sathe, to refund Rs 546.17 crore. This amount was collected by the entity from various participants for programs. The regulator has mandated that these funds be returned to the individuals who paid for these services.</p>\n<p>The order follows a regulatory review of the academy’s operations regarding the collection of fees from the public. Sebi, which acts as the primary watchdog for the Indian securities market, ensures that entities operating within the financial ecosystem adhere to established legal frameworks. The watchdog maintains oversight to protect participants from unauthorized financial activities.</p>\n<p>The directive highlights the regulatory stance on entities that collect large sums from the public under the guise of training services. By ordering a refund of Rs 546.17 crore, the authority aims to address the interests of those who participated in the academy&#039;s offerings. The academy and Avadhut Sathe must now comply with the instructions provided by the regulator to settle these obligations.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: This development serves as a reminder to verify the registration status of any entity offering financial training or investment-related services. Investors should exercise caution when transferring funds to private academies and ensure they understand the legal standing of the organization. Checking official regulatory databases can help in identifying entities that may be operating outside the scope of authorized financial activities.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261024-003101-rLO7xA.webp',NULL,NULL,'Business Standard','https://www.business-standard.com/markets/news/sebi-orders-avadhut-sathe-trading-academy-and-its-founder-to-refund-546-cr-126102301645_1.html','2026-10-24 00:31:01','2026-10-24 00:31:01',0,40,'active','2026-10-24 00:31:01','2026-10-27 08:17:27'),
(158,'Sebi Relaxes Call Recording Rules for Research Analysts Interacting With Institutional Investors','The market regulator Sebi eased the mandatory call recording requirement for research analysts to lower the compliance burden for market participants.','Sebi, research analysts, institutional investors, compliance, stock market, market regulator, Indian stock market','<p>On Friday, the market regulator Sebi announced a relaxation regarding the mandatory requirement for research analysts to maintain recordings of their interactions with institutional investors. This policy adjustment is intended to reduce the compliance burden for entities operating within the financial sector. A compliance burden refers to the administrative costs and efforts firms must undertake to adhere to regulatory requirements.</p>\n<p>The regulator has modified the existing framework to streamline operations for research analysts. This change specifically addresses the previous obligation to record conversations held with institutional clients. By adjusting these mandates, the authority aims to create a more efficient environment for market participants while maintaining oversight. These rules apply to registered research analysts who provide insights to large-scale institutional investors.</p>\n<p>This move follows ongoing efforts by the regulator to simplify operational procedures for various market intermediaries. The decision reflects a shift in how the authority manages documentation standards for professional interactions. While specific procedural details were updated, the core objective remains the balancing of regulatory transparency with operational ease. The market regulator continues to review various mandates to ensure that the regulatory framework remains relevant to the current needs of the financial industry.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: This regulatory change may simplify the workflow for research firms, potentially allowing for more focused analysis. Investors should note that while compliance requirements have been eased, the regulator maintains its supervision over market activities to ensure overall fairness and transparency in financial dealings.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261024-003111-FFjTEz.webp',NULL,NULL,'Business Standard','https://www.business-standard.com/markets/news/sebi-eases-call-recording-mandate-for-research-analysts-dealing-with-funds-126102301112_1.html','2026-10-24 00:31:11','2026-10-24 00:31:11',0,80,'active','2026-10-24 00:31:11','2026-10-28 03:51:20'),
(159,'Apple India Revenue Surges 32 Percent To Exceed ₹1 Trillion In FY26','Apple India reported revenue of Rs 1,04,607 crore for FY26, marking a 32 per cent growth as per data from intelligence firm Tofler.','Apple India, Tofler, FY26 revenue, Indian technology sector, Apple revenue growth, NSE, business news','<p>Market intelligence firm Tofler has released financial documentation indicating that Apple India achieved a revenue growth of 32 per cent during the fiscal year 2026. According to these filings, the company reached a total revenue figure of Rs 1,04,607 crore, successfully crossing the ₹1 trillion milestone for the period.</p>\n<p>This financial data provides a specific look at the revenue trajectory of the company within the Indian market. Such information is derived from regulatory filings and official company reports that are processed by research agencies to track the performance of corporate entities. Revenue is the total income generated by the sale of goods or services related to a company&#039;s primary operations.</p>\n<p>The report highlights the specific financial performance metrics for the mentioned period without providing further details on operational expenses or net profit margins. The document shared by Tofler serves as the primary source for these figures, confirming the 32 per cent increase over the previous fiscal cycle. Investors often monitor these official filings to understand the scale of operations for major multinational corporations operating within the country.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The reported revenue growth to Rs 1,04,607 crore offers a clear view of the company&#039;s financial scale in India for FY26. While this data reflects past performance, market participants typically analyze such figures to gauge the market presence of the firm. There is no resistance level or support mentioned regarding the stock performance in this report. This information is provided for educational purposes only and does not constitute financial advice.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261024-010038-YDVqq1.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Business Standard','https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/apple-india-revenue-grows-32-to-cross-1-trillion-mark-in-fy26-tofler-126102301658_1.html','2026-10-24 01:00:38','2026-10-24 01:00:38',0,44,'active','2026-10-24 01:00:38','2026-10-28 01:43:43'),
(160,'ASSOCHAM Projects India Exports To Germany To Exceed $50 Billion By 2030','ASSOCHAM reports that India’s exports to Germany may surpass $50 billion by 2030, following a 41% rise in bilateral trade to $31 billion in FY26.','ASSOCHAM, India Germany trade, exports, bilateral trade, FY26, engineering sector, pharma stocks, Indian economy','<p>According to recent data from ASSOCHAM, India’s exports to Germany are projected to surpass $50 billion by 2030. This forecast follows a 41% rise in bilateral merchandise trade since FY18, reaching $31 billion in FY26. Merchandise trade refers to the physical import and export of goods between two nations.</p>\n<p>The report highlights that a potential India-EU FTA and deeper industrial cooperation are expected to boost opportunities across engineering, pharma, and textiles. An FTA, or Free Trade Agreement, is a pact between countries to reduce barriers to imports and exports.</p>\n<p>As trade relations between the two nations deepen, the scope for industrial collaboration is set to expand. This cooperation is expected to facilitate better market access and technological exchanges, strengthening economic ties between India and Germany. The focus remains on leveraging these bilateral frameworks to boost total trade volumes.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The projected increase in trade suggests growth for companies in engineering, pharmaceutical, and textile sectors. Investors should monitor progress on the India-EU FTA, as trade policies often influence the resistance level for stocks linked to international exports. These trends reflect shifts in global trade that may impact the future performance of export-oriented industries listed on the domestic exchanges. Such developments are important for tracking the long-term outlook of companies involved in cross-border commerce and global supply chains.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261024-010135-EajMdg.jpg',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/business/indias-exports-to-germany-could-cross-50-billion-by-2030-assocham-20018410.htm','2026-10-24 01:01:35','2026-10-24 01:01:35',0,18,'active','2026-10-24 01:01:35','2026-10-26 19:56:18'),
(161,'Midcap and Smallcap Stocks Experience Sharp Declines Over Recent Trading Week','Indian midcap and smallcap indices recorded their steepest weekly drops in 20 months, falling by 5.6% and 7.3% respectively amid global market pressures.','midcap stocks, smallcap stocks, stock market crash, NSE, BSE, market volatility, Indian equity market, index performance','<p>Midcap and smallcap stocks recorded their worst weekly losses in 20 months, with the indices falling 5.6% and 7.3%, respectively. These declines occurred during a tumultuous week as rising crude prices and geopolitical tensions rattled markets. A stock market index is a collection of shares representing a specific segment of the market, used to track overall performance.</p>\n<p>The sharp downward movement in these categories reflects broader investor sentiment during a period of uncertainty. As international oil prices climbed, the increased cost of energy impacted various industries, leading to a negative reaction across the exchange. Geopolitical tensions further contributed to the volatility, creating a challenging environment for traders and institutional participants throughout the trading sessions.</p>\n<p>Market participants closely monitored the indices as selling pressure intensified across the midcap and smallcap segments. This period of correction highlights how sensitive these specific stocks are to external macroeconomic factors and global instability. The indices serve as benchmarks for the broader market, and their performance often influences the overall mood of the domestic exchanges.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The recent volatility suggests that market participants should remain cautious during periods of global instability. A resistance level for these indices may be difficult to determine while crude oil prices and geopolitical risks remain elevated. Monitoring these trends is important for those tracking the performance of smaller companies in the current economic climate, as fluctuations in global markets frequently dictate the short-term direction of domestic equity prices.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261024-013028-4vIq26.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Business Standard','https://www.business-standard.com/markets/news/tumultuous-week-midcaps-and-smallcaps-suffer-worst-losses-in-20-months-126102301443_1.html','2026-10-24 01:30:28','2026-10-24 01:30:28',0,31,'active','2026-10-24 01:30:28','2026-10-28 00:29:49'),
(162,'EAAA India Alternatives Raises Rs 360 Crore From Anchor Investors Ahead Of IPO','EAAA India Alternatives secured Rs 360 crore from anchor investors ahead of its public issue scheduled to open for subscription on October 26.','EAAA India Alternatives, IPO, anchor investors, public subscription, share market, stock market news, Indian IPOs','<p>EAAA India Alternatives has successfully collected Rs 360 crore from anchor investors ahead of its initial public offering. The company has officially scheduled its IPO to open for public subscription on October 26. An IPO is the process through which a private company offers its shares to the public for the first time to raise capital.</p>\n<p>Anchor investors are institutional buyers who are invited to subscribe to shares before the issue opens to the general public to instill confidence. By securing these funds, the company has completed a significant step in its pre-listing process. This move allows the firm to demonstrate institutional interest in its upcoming public offering before the retail subscription phase begins.</p>\n<p>The funds raised from these anchor investors form a portion of the total capital the company aims to generate through the market. Market participants often track these pre-IPO developments to gauge the appetite of large financial institutions for new listings. The company will now proceed with the public phase of the offering as per the announced timeline.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The participation of anchor investors provides a signal regarding the valuation and demand for the shares before the public subscription window opens. Investors typically monitor these allotments to understand the institutional sentiment surrounding the issue. This phase serves as a precursor to the wider market participation that will follow when the subscription period commences on October 26 for all categories of investors.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261024-013033-6AGd8J.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Economic Times','https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/ipos/fpos/eaaa-india-alternatives-mops-up-rs-360-crore-from-anchor-investors-ipo-opens-on-oct-26/articleshow/135150980.cms','2026-10-24 01:30:33','2026-10-24 01:30:33',0,46,'active','2026-10-24 01:30:33','2026-10-28 04:13:47'),
(163,'BPCL Reports 21.45% Drop In Q2 FY27 Net Profit Due To Fuel Pricing','Bharat Petroleum Corporation Limited has announced a 21.45% decline in its Q2 FY27 consolidated net profit, citing losses from fuel sales as the reason.','BPCL, BPCL share price, Q2 FY27 results, Bharat Petroleum, NSE, Indian stock market, oil marketing companies, quarterly earnings','<p>Bharat Petroleum Corporation Limited has officially released its financial results for the second quarter of the current fiscal year. The company recorded a 21.45% drop in its consolidated net profit for Q2 FY27. This financial outcome follows a period where the firm faced operational challenges related to the pricing of its products. A consolidated profit represents the combined earnings of a parent company and its subsidiaries.</p>\n<p>The management of Bharat Petroleum Corporation Limited has attributed this decline in profitability to losses incurred during the sale of petrol and diesel. These fuel pricing issues have directly impacted the bottom line of the company during the three-month period. Such earnings reports are released by listed companies to provide transparency to shareholders regarding their periodic financial health and operational performance.</p>\n<p>Investors often monitor these quarterly updates to understand how external economic factors, such as fuel pricing, influence the profitability of oil marketing entities. The current figures reflect the specific impact of these pricing constraints on the company&#039;s performance during the stated timeframe. Understanding these financial metrics is essential for tracking the fiscal trajectory of large-scale industrial corporations operating within the energy sector.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The reported 21.45% decline in net profit provides a clear look at the financial state of Bharat Petroleum Corporation Limited. While the market reacts to these results, stakeholders often monitor the stock for a support level or a resistance level to gauge future price movements based on these official figures.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261024-060033-bwd0HJ.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Economic Times','https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/earnings/bpcl-reports-21-45-drop-in-q2-fy27-net-profit-attributes-losses-to-fuel-pricing-issues/articleshow/135161389.cms','2026-10-24 06:00:33','2026-10-24 06:00:33',0,23,'active','2026-10-24 06:00:33','2026-10-27 07:52:06'),
(164,'Dr. Reddy\'s Labs Reports 36% Profit Decline While Welcoming New Trade Margin Rules','Dr. Reddy\'s Labs saw a 36% drop in second quarter PAT for FY2027. The company views the new trade margin regulations as a positive development.','Dr. Reddy\'s Labs, DRL share price, Q2 results, pharmaceutical sector, NSE, stock market news, Indian pharma stocks','<p>Dr. Reddy&#039;s Labs has released its financial results for the second quarter of FY2027, reporting a 36% dip in profit after tax. The company confirmed that its revenue also experienced a downturn during this period. Despite these declining financial metrics, the management expressed support for the recently introduced trade margin regulations. These government-mandated caps on trade margins are designed to regulate the price markups applied at various stages of the pharmaceutical supply chain.</p>\n<p>The pharmaceutical sector in India is navigating a changing regulatory environment as authorities balance affordability with industry sustainability. Trade margins refer to the difference between the price at which a manufacturer sells a product and the price paid by the end consumer. By capping these margins, regulators aim to control the final retail cost of essential medications for patients across the country.</p>\n<p>The company remains focused on its operational strategies following these results. While the bottom line has been impacted by the recent quarterly performance, the leadership team continues to monitor market conditions. Investors track these filings to understand how regulatory changes and market demand influence the financial health of major pharmaceutical entities listed on the stock exchanges.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The 36% decrease in PAT highlights current challenges. Market participants may observe the stock’s movement relative to its support levels. Future price shifts will be evaluated against the resistance level as the company adapts to the new margin framework.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261024-060042-4T3Pff.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Economic Times','https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/earnings/drl-says-cap-on-trade-margins-a-positive-posts-36-dip-in-q2-pat/articleshow/135161325.cms','2026-10-24 06:00:42','2026-10-24 06:00:42',0,29,'active','2026-10-24 06:00:42','2026-10-28 03:21:09'),
(165,'Q2 Results Today: Kotak Mahindra Bank, AU Small Finance Bank and Other Companies Report Earnings','Several major companies are scheduled to release their financial results for the September quarter on 24th October 2026.','Kotak Mahindra Bank, AU Small Finance Bank, IDFC First Bank, JK Cement, Netweb Tech, Q2 results, NSE, BSE','<p>On 24th October 2026, a series of companies are set to disclose their financial performance for the second quarter. The list of firms scheduled to announce their September quarter earnings includes Kotak Mahindra Bank, AU Small Finance Bank, IDFC First Bank, JK Cement, Netweb Tech, Castrol India, Kajaria Ceramics, and Bharat Coking Coal. Quarterly results provide a periodic snapshot of a company’s financial health, including its revenue and profit figures for the three-month period.</p>\n<p>Investors are closely monitoring these updates as they assess the operational performance of these entities across the banking, manufacturing, and technology sectors. The announcements are expected to be released throughout the trading session. Financial results are mandatory reports that public companies must file to ensure transparency and provide stakeholders with updated information regarding their income and expenses.</p>\n<p>Market participants often watch these disclosures to gauge how individual companies have navigated the economic environment during the recent quarter. As these firms release their data, analysts and traders will evaluate the figures against previous performance metrics. Earnings reports serve as a primary tool for market participants to understand the fiscal trajectory of a business.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The upcoming announcements from Kotak Mahindra Bank, AU Small Finance Bank, IDFC First Bank, JK Cement, Netweb Tech, Castrol India, Kajaria Ceramics, and Bharat Coking Coal on 24th October 2026 may lead to volatility in their respective share prices as the market reacts to the disclosed financial data.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261024-060054-X0POGW.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Hindu BusinessLine','https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/money-and-banking/q2-results-today-live-updates-kotak-mahindra-bank-au-small-finance-bank-idfc-first-bank-jk-cement-netweb-tech-castrol-india-kajaria-ceramics-bharat-coking-coal-company-results-24-october-2026/article71618989.ece','2026-10-24 06:00:54','2026-10-24 06:00:54',0,32,'active','2026-10-24 06:00:54','2026-10-27 06:14:21'),
(166,'MK Sons Fine Jewels Announces ₹275 Crore IPO Opening Next Week','MK Sons Fine Jewels has scheduled its ₹275 crore initial public offering for next week, with anchor investor bidding set for October 27.','MK Sons Fine Jewels IPO, upcoming IPO, share market, stock market news, anchor investors, IPO dates, Indian stock market, primary market','<p>MK Sons Fine Jewels has announced that its initial public offering, valued at ₹275 crore, will open for subscription next week. The company confirmed that the bidding process for anchor investors is scheduled to take place on October 27. This specific date precedes the official opening of the issue for retail and other investor categories by one day. An initial public offering is a process where a private company offers its shares to the public for the first time.</p>\n<p>The offering represents a significant event as the company enters the primary market to secure funds. Investors looking to participate in the subscription should note the specific sequence of dates provided for the different categories of bidders. The transition from anchor bidding to the general public opening is a standard procedure in the timeline of such public issues. This structured approach ensures that institutional participation is recorded before the broader market involvement.</p>\n<p>Market participants are currently tracking the upcoming schedule to align their portfolios with the timeline of this ₹275 crore offering. The company has finalized these dates to streamline the application process for all interested parties. Proper planning regarding the application window is essential for those intending to participate in the bidding process during the designated period next week.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: This IPO allows individuals and institutions to acquire equity in the company during the subscription window. Participants should review the official prospectus to understand the details before submitting applications through their brokers.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261025-000225-lfFDk6.webp',NULL,NULL,'Mint','https://www.livemint.com/market/ipo/upcoming-ipo-mk-sons-fine-jewels-rs-275-cr-opening-next-week-company-profile-key-dates-share-price-band-and-more-11792858838153.html','2026-10-25 00:02:25','2026-10-25 00:02:25',0,39,'active','2026-10-25 00:02:25','2026-10-28 05:26:10'),
(167,'Utssav CZ Gold Jewels Approves 1:1 Bonus Share Issue for Shareholders','Utssav CZ Gold Jewels Ltd has officially approved a 1:1 bonus share issue, which will double its paid-up equity share capital to Rs 49.996 crore.','Utssav CZ Gold Jewels, bonus issue, equity capital, stock market, Indian investors, corporate action, NSE','<p>The board of directors at Utssav CZ Gold Jewels Ltd has formally approved a 1:1 bonus share issue. This corporate action is set to double the company’s paid-up equity share capital to Rs 49.996 crore. The implementation of this decision remains subject to necessary approvals from shareholders and other regulatory requirements. A bonus issue is a corporate action where a company distributes additional shares to existing holders.</p>\n<p>This announcement follows the recent board meeting where the proposal for the bonus issue was evaluated and cleared. The company aims to increase its total equity base through this distribution process. By issuing one new share for every existing share held, the company will adjust its capital structure accordingly. This procedure is commonly used by firms to increase the liquidity of their shares in the secondary market.</p>\n<p>Investors should note that the final execution of this bonus issue depends on the completion of all required formalities. The company has communicated that the increase to Rs 49.996 crore is the intended outcome of this specific capital adjustment. No further details regarding the timeline for the record date or the distribution process were mentioned in the initial announcement released by the firm.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The approval of a 1:1 bonus issue indicates a change in the equity capital structure of Utssav CZ Gold Jewels Ltd. While the total paid-up equity share capital will reach Rs 49.996 crore, the move essentially increases the number of outstanding shares without requiring any additional cash investment from the existing shareholders.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261025-000359-me7i5c.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Business Standard','https://www.business-standard.com/markets/news/utssav-cz-gold-jewels-approves-1-1-bonus-issue-to-double-equity-capital-126102400806_1.html','2026-10-25 00:03:59','2026-10-25 00:03:59',0,18,'active','2026-10-25 00:03:59','2026-10-27 19:35:17'),
(168,'Four Stocks Under ₹200 Featuring High Dividend Yields for Indian Investors','Indian Oil Corporation, PTC India, Central Bank of India, and PTL Enterprises currently trade below ₹200 while offering notable dividend yields.','IOCL share price, PTC India stock, Central Bank of India, PTL Enterprises, dividend stocks, NSE, Indian stock market, high yield shares','<p>Indian Oil Corporation, PTC India, Central Bank of India, and PTL Enterprises are currently identified as stocks priced under ₹200 that offer dividend yields of 5.5%, 19%, 2.53%, and 6.25% respectively. These figures represent the annual return on a share price through dividend payments. Investors often monitor these metrics to assess the income potential of their holdings relative to the current market valuation of the equity.</p>\n<p>The market price of these four entities remains below the ₹200 threshold, which serves as a psychological or technical marker for many market participants. A dividend yield is calculated by dividing the annual dividend per share by the price per share of the stock. By evaluating these specific yields, market participants can observe how much cash flow these companies generate for shareholders based on their current trading levels on the stock exchange.</p>\n<p>Technical analysts sometimes monitor stocks near specific price points to determine potential support, which is a price level where a stock has historically had difficulty falling below. While these four companies show varying yields, they all remain within the sub-₹200 price category. The performance of these shares is subject to market fluctuations and the specific dividend policies adopted by the board of directors of each respective company during the fiscal year.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: These figures highlight the dividend income potential for shares priced below ₹200. It is important to note that dividends are not guaranteed and depend on the financial decisions made by the management of each individual firm.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261025-003144-X8cUsd.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Mint','https://www.livemint.com/market/stock-market-news/high-dividend-low-price-4-stocks-under-rs-200-with-high-yield-iocl-ptc-india-central-bank-ptl-enterprises-11792860259451.html','2026-10-25 00:31:44','2026-10-25 00:31:44',0,33,'active','2026-10-25 00:31:44','2026-10-27 15:50:15'),
(169,'Utssav CZ Gold Jewels Announces 1:1 Bonus Issue After 413% Annual Returns','Utssav CZ Gold Jewels board approved a 1:1 bonus issue of 2,49,98,000 shares, doubling its paid-up equity capital for shareholders.','Utssav CZ Gold Jewels, bonus shares, stock market, NSE, jewellery stocks, equity capital, corporate action','<p>The board of directors at Utssav CZ Gold Jewels has officially approved a 1:1 bonus issue. This corporate action involves the distribution of 2,49,98,000 new shares to existing shareholders, which will effectively double the company’s current paid-up equity capital. The implementation of this issuance remains subject to receiving all necessary regulatory and shareholder approvals. A bonus issue is a corporate action where a company distributes additional shares to existing shareholders for free based on their current holdings.</p>\n<p>The announcement follows a period in which the stock delivered 413% returns over the past year. By issuing these additional shares, the company aims to adjust its equity structure. The specific record date, which determines which shareholders are eligible to receive the bonus shares, will be announced by the firm in due course. Investors typically monitor these dates closely to ensure they are on the register of members to qualify for the allotment.</p>\n<p>Market participants are now tracking the administrative timeline for the distribution of these securities. Once the process is finalized, the new shares will be credited to the demat accounts of eligible investors. This move increases the total number of outstanding shares while keeping the overall value of the company&#039;s equity capital stable.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: A bonus issue increases the number of shares held by an investor without requiring any cash investment, though the price per share typically adjusts downward. Holders should verify their eligibility and monitor for the official record date to confirm their participation in the equity distribution.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261025-003247-vCNKXC.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Mint','https://www.livemint.com/market/stock-market-news/413-returns-in-1-year-gold-jewellery-stock-offers-bonus-shares-do-you-own-check-ratio-record-date-11792858197650.html','2026-10-25 00:32:47','2026-10-25 00:32:47',0,31,'active','2026-10-25 00:32:47','2026-10-27 23:03:27'),
(170,'Setco Automotive Reports ₹203.61 Crore Profit and Announces Lava Cast Merger Plan','Setco Automotive posted a ₹203.61 crore profit for the April–June 2026 quarter as revenue grew by 12.3%, alongside plans to merge with Lava Cast.','Setco Automotive, Lava Cast, quarterly results, corporate merger, stock market news, Indian automotive sector, financial performance, NSE','<p>Setco Automotive reported a consolidated profit of ₹203.61 crore for the April–June 2026 quarter, moving from a loss in the previous year. Alongside these financial results, the company announced plans for a merger with Lava Cast to reduce costs. During this same quarter, the firm recorded a revenue increase of 12.3%.</p>\n<p>These figures represent the performance of the business over the three-month period ending in June 2026. A merger is a corporate strategy where two companies combine their operations, assets, and liabilities into a single entity to improve efficiency. This specific action involving Lava Cast is intended to help the company streamline its total expenditures.</p>\n<p>Investors should note the shift in profitability compared to the previous year. The data provided covers the consolidated earnings of the firm, which includes the financial activities of its various subsidiaries. As the company moves toward the proposed integration of its business units, market participants will be observing how these structural changes impact the financial health of the organization.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The transition to a profit of ₹203.61 crore and the announcement of the Lava Cast merger represent significant developments for the company. While the revenue growth of 12.3% indicates a positive trend in operations, the long-term impact of the merger on cost reduction remains to be seen. Market participants often track such corporate restructuring events to assess future stability and efficiency potential within the business.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261025-010111-smZXcY.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Hindu BusinessLine','https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/companies/setco-automotive-swings-to-20361-crore-profit-plans-lava-cast-merger-to-cut-costs/article71620201.ece','2026-10-25 01:01:11','2026-10-25 01:01:11',0,23,'active','2026-10-25 01:01:11','2026-10-27 20:28:47'),
(171,'Zetwerk IPO: Kae Capital, Accel, Peak XV and Lightspeed Monetise ₹1,215 Crore Stake','Investors Kae Capital, Accel, Peak XV and Lightspeed are set to realise ₹1,215 crore through the upcoming Zetwerk IPO at a price of ₹151 per share.','Zetwerk IPO, Kae Capital, Accel, Peak XV, Lightspeed, Indian stock market, IPO news','<p>Kae Capital, Accel, Peak XV and Lightspeed are preparing to monetise their holdings in the Zetwerk IPO. These investors are set to realise a total of ₹1,215 crore through this offering. The transaction is being executed at an issue price of ₹151 per share, representing the valuation at which these entities are liquidating their positions. An Initial Public Offering, or IPO, is the process by which a private company offers its shares to the public for the first time on a stock exchange.</p>\n<p>The investors involved in this transaction previously accumulated their stakes in the company at prices significantly lower than the current issue price of ₹151 per share. This move allows these venture capital firms to exit or reduce their existing holdings as the company transitions into the public markets. These firms have been long-term backers of the business prior to this public offering event.</p>\n<p>Market participants are closely observing the pricing dynamics as these specific investors offload their equity. The total realisation of ₹1,215 crore reflects the current valuation assessment for the business. All transaction details remain tied to the fixed issue price of ₹151 per share as specified in the offering documents. Investors often track such exits to gauge the sentiment of early-stage backers regarding the company’s valuation.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The exit of these major investors provides liquidity for the participants involved in the sale. Market observers should note the resistance level of ₹151 per share, which serves as the benchmark price for this public offering.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261025-010130-panxbg.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Hindu BusinessLine','https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/markets/zetwerk-ipo-kae-capital-accel-peak-xv-and-lightspeed-set-to-realise-1215-crore/article71620691.ece','2026-10-25 01:01:30','2026-10-25 01:01:30',0,38,'active','2026-10-25 01:01:30','2026-10-28 04:14:10'),
(172,'Lumax Auto Technologies Reports 57.5% Profit Growth and New Manesar Facility Expansion','Lumax Auto Technologies saw a 57.5% rise in Q2 FY27 profit alongside revenue growth of 34.5% as it announces a new mechatronics plant in Manesar.','Lumax Auto Technologies, Q2 results, stock market, NSE, automobile sector, manufacturing, earnings, investor update','<p>Lumax Auto Technologies announced its financial performance for Q2 FY27, reporting a net profit increase of 57.5% compared to the previous year. During this same period, the company recorded a revenue growth of 34.5%. Additionally, the firm revealed plans to establish a new mechatronics manufacturing facility located in Manesar, which aims to achieve a turnover of ₹500 crore. Earnings reports provide a summary of a company&#039;s financial health over a specific three-month period.</p>\n<p>The management confirmed that this investment into the Manesar plant is intended to expand their production capabilities. This new site will focus on mechatronics, a field combining mechanical, electronic, and software engineering. A manufacturing plant is a facility where raw materials are processed into finished goods for sale.</p>\n<p>The company continues to monitor its operational efficiency as it integrates these new production goals into its existing business framework. Shareholders often track these updates to understand how capital expenditure might influence future financial statements. Market participants look at such announcements to gauge the direction of the firm&#039;s infrastructure development and its capacity to meet rising demand in the automotive sector.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The financial results reflect the current performance of the business, while the announcement of the new facility provides insight into future revenue targets. Investors should observe how the ₹500 crore turnover goal for the Manesar plant aligns with the firm&#039;s long-term financial strategy. Monitoring these developments helps in understanding the company&#039;s growth trajectory and its commitment to scaling operations in the competitive automotive industry.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261025-020205-Qyccyp.jpg',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/lumax-auto-share-price-q2-results-profit-manesar-plant-targets-rs-500-crore-turnover-20018622.htm','2026-10-25 02:02:05','2026-10-25 02:02:05',0,23,'active','2026-10-25 02:02:05','2026-10-28 00:07:16'),
(173,'IDBI Bank Sale: Employees Service Conditions To Remain Unchanged Says DIPAM Secretary','DIPAM Secretary Arunish Chawla says IDBI Bank staff and pensioners have nothing to fear regarding the ₹52,878 crore deal involving Fairfax.','IDBI Bank, DIPAM, Arunish Chawla, Fairfax, bank privatization, Indian banking, stocks','<p>DIPAM Secretary Arunish Chawla has stated that the service conditions for employees will remain unchanged following the ₹52,878 crore deal involving Fairfax. Addressing concerns regarding the transition, Chawla emphasized that staff members and pensioners have nothing to fear as the process moves forward. The Department of Investment and Public Asset Management, known as DIPAM, is the government body responsible for managing equity investments in public sector enterprises.</p>\n<p>The clarification comes as stakeholders monitor the developments surrounding the proposed transaction. By confirming that existing employment terms are protected, the government aims to provide stability for the workforce during the ownership transfer process. This assurance is intended to address anxieties among the bank&#039;s personnel who have been seeking clarity on their future status and benefits under the new arrangement.</p>\n<p>The proposed deal represents a significant shift in the ownership structure of the financial institution. The government has maintained that the interests of the current employees are being prioritized as part of the broader administrative framework governing the sale. Clear communication from administrative officials is often used to mitigate uncertainty among the staff of organizations undergoing such structural transitions.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The public commitment from the DIPAM Secretary regarding employee stability aims to ensure the continuity of operations during the divestment process. Investors often track official statements from government departments to gauge the progress of major corporate transactions. Market participants observe such updates to understand how potential regulatory or labor concerns are being addressed by the authorities involved in the sale.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261025-020237-TBASZA.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Mint','https://www.livemint.com/companies/news/idbi-bank-sale-employees-service-conditions-to-remain-unchanged-says-dipam-secretary-11792845187639.html','2026-10-25 02:02:37','2026-10-25 02:02:37',0,21,'active','2026-10-25 02:02:37','2026-10-28 05:33:47'),
(174,'Indian Hotels Revenue Growth Guidance Upgraded Following Strong Q2FY27 Performance','Indian Hotels raised its FY27 revenue growth guidance after reporting strong room rates and occupancy levels during the Q2FY27 period.','Indian Hotels, IHCL share price, Q2FY27 results, revenue growth, hospitality sector, NSE, stock market, Indian Hotels news','<p>Indian Hotels has officially increased its revenue growth guidance for FY27 following a strong performance in the Q2FY27 period. The company reported that the primary drivers for this upward revision were high room rates and robust occupancy levels recorded throughout the quarter. These financial updates reflect the current operational status of the hospitality firm as it navigates the fiscal year.</p>\n<p>The demand-supply mismatch in the hospitality sector is currently serving as a catalyst for revenue gains. This occurs when the number of available hotel rooms is insufficient to meet the total travel demand from guests, allowing operators to maintain higher pricing power. As demand outpaces the existing inventory of rooms, the company has adjusted its financial outlook to account for these market conditions.</p>\n<p>Brokerages have expressed their views on the prospects of the stock following the release of the Q2FY27 results. These institutions monitor various metrics to assess how the business is positioned within the industry. While the company has provided updated guidance for the remainder of the fiscal year, market participants continue to observe how these specific operational factors influence the overall valuation of the entity on the exchange.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The revision of revenue growth guidance provides a specific financial outlook for FY27 based on current occupancy and room rate trends. Investors should note the company identified a demand-supply mismatch as a key factor affecting performance. Future shifts in these market dynamics could impact the financial trajectory of the business.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261025-023024-Bf52QC.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Business Standard','https://www.business-standard.com/markets/news/demand-supply-mismatch-to-drive-revenue-growth-gains-for-indian-hotels-126102500052_1.html','2026-10-25 02:30:24','2026-10-25 02:30:24',0,25,'active','2026-10-25 02:30:24','2026-10-27 19:35:39'),
(175,'Infosys Shares Face Potential Selling Pressure Following 7% ADR Drop After Q2 Results','Infosys shares are anticipated to face pressure after Q2 results caused its ADR to fall 7% on Friday, following a downward revision in company guidance.','Infosys share price, Infosys Q2 results, ADR, NSE, IT sector, stock market, Indian investors, guidance cut','<p>Shares of Infosys are set to face volatility following the company’s recent Q2 results, which triggered a 7% decline in its ADR on Friday. The movement in the US-listed American Depositary Receipt often influences the domestic trading sentiment for the stock on Indian exchanges. An ADR is a negotiable certificate issued by a US bank representing shares in a foreign stock.</p>\n<p>The management at Infosys highlighted that the decision to lower its financial guidance was driven by a soft performance during the second quarter. The company pointed to reduced business volumes and ongoing pricing pressure as primary factors impacting its outlook. These challenges were attributed to the high level of competitive intensity currently present within the global market.</p>\n<p>Market participants will be watching the stock closely for any signs of stabilization or further decline during the upcoming sessions. Technical analysts often monitor price charts to identify a support level, which acts as a price point where a stock may stop falling, or a resistance level, which is a price point that the stock may struggle to rise above.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The downward revision in guidance and the reaction in overseas markets suggest that shareholders should remain cautious. Investors should monitor how the price reacts to the opening bell to gauge the sentiment surrounding the IT sector. Keeping an eye on the support level is essential for those assessing the risk profile of their holdings following these developments.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261026-003114-k46vAA.jpg',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/infosys-share-price-q2-result-reaction-adr-fall-guidance-cut-margins-buy-sell-target-outlook-20018869.htm','2026-10-26 00:31:14','2026-10-26 00:31:14',0,23,'active','2026-10-26 00:31:14','2026-10-27 22:31:10'),
(176,'IT Stocks Dividend Record Dates Set Between October 26 and October 30','Five IT companies including Cyient and L&T Technology Services have scheduled their dividend record dates for the current week.','IT stocks, dividend, record date, Cyient, LT Tech, Hexaware, Hypersoft, Sagility','<p>Investors monitoring the information technology sector should note that Cyient, LT Tech, Hexaware, Hypersoft, and Sagility have scheduled their dividend record dates between October 26 and October 30. During this period, L&amp;T Technology Services has announced a payout of ₹20 per share, while Cyient will provide ₹12 per share. Additionally, Hexaware has declared a dividend of ₹9.50 per share. A record date is the specific day on which a company finalizes the list of shareholders eligible to receive a dividend.</p>\n<p>The list of companies distributing payouts also includes Hypersoft and Sagility, though specific amounts for these entities were not disclosed in the recent filings. These distributions are part of the corporate actions scheduled by these five IT firms for the final week of October. Shareholders who hold the equity on the designated record date will be entitled to receive the declared cash payouts. Corporate actions refer to events initiated by a public company that bring material change to its securities.</p>\n<p>Market participants track these dates to ensure they remain eligible for upcoming distributions. The dividend amounts vary across these five companies, reflecting the specific payout policies adopted by each firm. Investors typically check their demat accounts to confirm the receipt of these funds after the payment date. A demat account is a digital facility that allows investors to hold shares in an electronic format.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: Tracking these record dates is essential for those aiming to capture the announced dividends. Shareholders must ensure their holdings are settled in their accounts by the record date to qualify for the payments.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261026-003229-tYUIOh.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Mint','https://www.livemint.com/market/stock-market-news/it-stocks-dividend-record-date-this-week-cyient-lt-tech-hexaware-hypersoft-sagility-who-pays-most-amount-return-11792938159348.html','2026-10-26 00:32:29','2026-10-26 00:32:29',0,16,'active','2026-10-26 00:32:29','2026-10-26 23:34:06'),
(177,'Raja Venkatraman Shares Two Stock Recommendations for 26 October Trading Session','Market expert Raja Venkatraman has provided his technical analysis and trade strategy for two specific stocks to watch on 26 October.','Raja Venkatraman, stock market, 26 October, technical analysis, trade strategy, NSE, BSE, Indian stocks','<p>Market expert Raja Venkatraman has released his technical outlook and trade strategy for two stocks for the trading session on 26 October. Investors often look toward technical analysis to identify potential entry points based on historical price patterns. These insights are intended to assist market participants in navigating the current volatility of the Indian stock market.</p>\n<p>For the first selected stock, the expert has identified a resistance level that traders should monitor closely during the session. If the price fails to break past this point, it may indicate a lack of buying momentum. Conversely, he has outlined a support level where the stock might find a floor if selling pressure increases. Support is the price level where a stock has historically had difficulty falling below.</p>\n<p>Regarding the second stock, the trade strategy focuses on specific price triggers that could signal a shift in trend. The expert suggests keeping a close watch on intraday fluctuations to determine if the stock will maintain its current trajectory. By observing these levels, investors can better understand the technical health of the security throughout the day. Resistance is a price level that a stock struggles to rise above.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: These recommendations provide a technical framework for those tracking these two specific stocks today. It is important to remember that technical levels do not guarantee future performance. Investors should remain cautious and consider their own risk appetite before making any decisions based on these identified support and resistance levels.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261026-010056-O6uZrm.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Mint','https://www.livemint.com/market/stock-market-news/raja-venkatraman-recommends-two-stocks-for-26-october-11792826087895.html','2026-10-26 01:00:56','2026-10-26 01:00:56',0,49,'active','2026-10-26 01:00:56','2026-10-28 05:11:32'),
(178,'Wow! Momo Eyes ₹300 Crore Funding and International Expansion Before Proposed IPO','Wow! Momo seeks ₹300 crore to fund overseas growth and scale its packaged-food business, targeting revenue of ₹1,050 crore by FY27.','Wow! Momo, IPO, funding, QSR chain, expansion, FMCG, investment, retail','<p>The Kolkata-based quick service restaurant chain Wow! Momo has announced plans to raise ₹300 crore in fresh funding. This capital injection is intended to support the company’s expansion into new international markets and the growth of its packaged-food division. The firm is currently preparing for a proposed IPO, which is a process where a private company offers its shares to the public for the first time.</p>\n<p>As part of its growth strategy, the organization intends to enter Sri Lanka within this calendar year. Furthermore, the company is actively exploring opportunities to establish a presence in the UAE. These moves are designed to broaden the brand’s reach beyond its existing domestic operations while simultaneously scaling its consumer-packaged goods portfolio.</p>\n<p>The company has set a specific financial goal of achieving ₹1,050 crore in revenue by the end of FY27. This target reflects the firm&#039;s focus on scaling its operations across both its restaurant outlets and its retail product lines. A QSR chain refers to a restaurant business model that provides fast service and limited table seating for customers.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The proposed IPO remains a key event to monitor as the company pursues its target of ₹1,050 crore by FY27. While the firm focuses on its entry into Sri Lanka and the UAE, the capital raise of ₹300 crore will be essential to fund these expansion efforts. Investors should watch for updates regarding the public offering timeline and progress in overseas markets.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261026-010114-lHsBs6.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Mint','https://www.livemint.com/companies/news/wow-momo-ipo-plans-fundraise-overseas-expansion-11792751168706.html','2026-10-26 01:01:14','2026-10-26 01:01:14',0,52,'active','2026-10-26 01:01:14','2026-10-28 04:39:37'),
(179,'Asian Stock Markets Open With Mixed Results Amid AI Sell-off Concerns','Asian markets opened with mixed results on October 26 as investors evaluated AI-related selling, upcoming earnings reports, and central bank meetings.','Asian markets, stock market, AI stocks, central bank meetings, earnings, global equities, NSE, Sensex','<p>Asian equity markets displayed a mixed performance on October 26 as investors processed various global factors. Market participants are currently balancing the recent selling pressure observed in artificial intelligence-related stocks against the anticipation surrounding upcoming corporate earnings reports and scheduled central bank meetings.</p>\n<p>The sentiment across regional exchanges remains cautious as traders monitor how these divergent forces impact broader indices. Central bank meetings are events where monetary authorities gather to discuss and decide on interest rate policies and economic measures that influence financial markets. The ongoing fluctuations in the technology sector, particularly regarding artificial intelligence firms, continue to be a primary point of focus for those tracking market movements across the continent.</p>\n<p>Investors are also preparing for the release of quarterly earnings data, which provides details on the financial health and profitability of listed companies. Earnings reports are formal documents that companies release to disclose their revenue, expenses, and net profit over a specific period of time. These filings are critical for market analysis as they offer a transparent look at how different industries are performing in the current economic environment.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The current market volatility highlights the importance of staying informed about broader macroeconomic events and sector-specific trends. Monitoring central bank updates and corporate results can provide clarity on how these factors shift investor sentiment and influence overall market direction. Maintaining a balanced perspective is essential when navigating periods of uncertainty driven by both technological sector adjustments and scheduled policy discussions.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261026-013045-r8F2nP.jpg',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/asia-stocks-share-price-kospi-nikkei-topix-hang-seng-ai-selloff-earnings-fed-rate-boj-brent-wti-crude-market-20018876.htm','2026-10-26 01:30:45','2026-10-26 01:30:45',0,38,'active','2026-10-26 01:30:45','2026-10-28 05:28:15'),
(180,'GIFT Nifty and Global Indices Signals for Stock Market on 26 October','Global market cues and GIFT Nifty data suggest a cautious start for Indian markets on Monday, 26 October 2026, as indices reflect international trends.','GIFT Nifty, Sensex, Nifty, stock market outlook, global indices, Indian share market','<p>The stock market outlook for Monday, 26 October 2026, is shaped by international signals and the performance of major global indices including the DJIA, S&amp;P, and NASDAQ. Domestic investors are monitoring the GIFT Nifty, which was trading around the 22,535 level. This figure represents a decline of nearly 72.50 points, or 0.32%, compared to the previous close of Nifty futures. A futures contract is a legal agreement to buy or sell an asset at a predetermined price at a specified time.</p>\n<p>Further cues for the trading session are derived from Asian markets, specifically the Kospi and Nikkei indices. These regional benchmarks provide a context for how sentiment is shifting across the continent before the opening bell in India. Traders observe these international movements to gauge the potential direction of local indices like the Sensex and Nifty throughout the day.</p>\n<p>Market participants are currently assessing the impact of these global fluctuations on local trading volumes and price movements. The combination of the DJIA, S&amp;P, and NASDAQ performance alongside the GIFT Nifty data serves as an indicator for the opening trends. Monitoring such data helps participants understand the prevailing mood in the financial ecosystem before the official market hours commence.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The current data regarding the GIFT Nifty and global indices suggests that participants should remain watchful of broader trends. These indicators provide a snapshot of international sentiment that often influences domestic opening gaps. Investors typically evaluate these external cues to adjust their strategy regarding support and resistance levels.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261026-013054-SsxUxF.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Mint','https://www.livemint.com/market/stock-market-news/stock-market-outlook-today-26-oct-sensex-nifty-prediction-djia-s-p-nasdaq-gift-nifty-kospi-nikkei-cues-11792975256498.html','2026-10-26 01:30:54','2026-10-26 01:30:54',0,34,'active','2026-10-26 01:30:54','2026-10-28 02:49:34'),
(181,'AU SFB Shares Drop Over 9 Percent Following Second Quarter Financial Results','Shares of AU SFB fell by more than 9 percent after the release of Q2 results. Brokerages remain divided regarding the future outlook for the bank.','AU SFB share price, AU Small Finance Bank, Q2 results, stock market, NSE, banking sector, Indian stock news','<p>Shares of AU SFB fell by more than 9 percent following the release of the company’s Q2 results. The market reaction to the financial performance led to a sharp decline in the stock price during the session. Investors are closely monitoring how the bank manages its operations after these latest figures were made public.</p>\n<p>Emkay Global stated that the current valuations of the bank provide a limited margin of safety for those holding the stock. The firm highlighted ongoing macro-uncertainties as a primary factor influencing their perspective on the bank. A brokerage firm is an entity that acts as an intermediary between investors and the stock exchange.</p>\n<p>Market analysts are currently displaying mixed views regarding the outlook for AU SFB. While some participants are assessing the impact of the Q2 results on the bank’s future, others are focusing on the broader economic environment. The volatility observed in the share price reflects the diverse reactions from market participants following the declaration of the quarterly earnings report.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The recent movement in the stock price highlights the sensitivity of the market to quarterly performance updates and external economic factors. Investors often use technical analysis to identify a support level, which is a price point where a stock may stop falling, or a resistance level, which is a price point that a stock may struggle to cross. It is essential for market participants to review the full financial disclosures provided by the bank to understand the data.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261026-052455-Iqocm1.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Business Standard','https://www.business-standard.com/markets/news/au-sfb-share-price-tank-over-9-post-q2-results-brokerages-mixed-on-outlook-126102600228_1.html','2026-10-26 05:24:55','2026-10-26 05:24:55',0,26,'active','2026-10-26 05:24:55','2026-10-28 02:36:40'),
(182,'Bharat Coking Coal Shares Jump 5% After Q2 Profit Turnaround Report','Bharat Coking Coal shares rose 5% on Monday as the Coal India subsidiary reported a Q2 FY27 profit of Rs 123.7 crore and 39% revenue growth.','Bharat Coking Coal share price, Coal India subsidiary, Q2 results, stock market, NSE, coal sector, Indian stocks, financial performance','<p>Bharat Coking Coal shares climbed 5% on Monday after the Coal India subsidiary announced its financial results for the second quarter of the 2027 fiscal year. The company reported a turnaround to profit, achieving a net profit of Rs 123.7 crore. Furthermore, the firm saw its revenue increase by 39% on a year-on-year basis. A subsidiary is a company that is owned or controlled by a parent organization.</p>\n<p>The market responded to these figures as investors analyzed the latest earnings update. This shift to a profit of Rs 123.7 crore, paired with the 39% revenue growth, served as the primary driver for the price movement observed on Monday. These results provide a clear view of the company’s recent performance within the coal sector, which is a vital component of the broader domestic industrial landscape.</p>\n<p>Market participants often examine these quarterly disclosures to evaluate the operational status of the business. The 39% revenue jump highlights the level of activity recorded during the three-month period. Traders typically monitor such updates to identify the current resistance level or support level for the stock based on the price action and trading volume observed throughout the active market session.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The reported turnaround to a profit of Rs 123.7 crore and the 39% revenue growth offer a snapshot of the current financial position of Bharat Coking Coal. Investors should review the full disclosure to understand the factors behind these specific results. All financial data remains subject to market conditions and the broader economic environment in which the company operates.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261026-052508-ivlPjo.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Economic Times','https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/bharat-coking-coal-shares-rally-5-after-q2-profit-turnaround-revenue-jumps-39-yoy/articleshow/135203231.cms','2026-10-26 05:25:08','2026-10-26 05:25:08',0,20,'active','2026-10-26 05:25:08','2026-10-27 06:32:56'),
(183,'BSE Share Price Rallies 4% Following Motilal Oswal Upgrade Recommendation','Shares of BSE jumped 4% today after Motilal Oswal upgraded the stock. The company has gained 28% in 2026, beating the 13% drop in the Nifty 50 index.','BSE share price, Motilal Oswal, Nifty 50, stock market, Indian stock exchange, BSE, equity market','<p>The BSE share price climbed 4% during the latest trading session following an upgrade by Motilal Oswal. This upward movement occurs within the context of the calendar year 2026, where the stock has demonstrated a gain of 28% while the Nifty 50 index experienced a decline of 13%.</p>\n<p>Market participants are observing these price fluctuations closely as the exchange continues to navigate the current financial year. The performance of the stock relative to the broader benchmark index highlights the specific price action observed in the equity market throughout this period. An upgrade typically reflects a change in the assessment of a company&#039;s financial outlook by a brokerage firm.</p>\n<p>The stock has maintained a strong momentum compared to the general market trend since the beginning of 2026. Investors often monitor how individual stocks perform against major indices like the Nifty 50 to gauge relative strength. Such movements are frequently tracked by those who follow exchange-related equities in the Indian financial space.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The recent price appreciation and the upgrade by Motilal Oswal provide updated information for those tracking the stock. While the company has seen a 28% increase in 2026, participants should remain aware of the 13% decline in the Nifty 50. Monitoring the resistance level and support is standard practice for those analyzing such market volatility. All market participants should conduct their own due diligence before making decisions based on these reported figures and shifts in brokerage assessments.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261026-053028-y0AhLC.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Business Standard','https://www.business-standard.com/markets/news/bse-share-price-rallies-4-motilal-oswal-upgrades-stock-to-buy-126102600254_1.html','2026-10-26 05:30:28','2026-10-26 05:30:28',0,16,'active','2026-10-26 05:30:28','2026-10-27 06:01:03'),
(184,'Infosys Share Price Drops 4% Following Revised FY27 Revenue Growth Guidance','Infosys shares fell by 4% today after the company lowered its revenue growth guidance for the fiscal year 2027, impacting investor sentiment.','Infosys, Infosys share price, NSE, BSE, IT sector, stock market news, revenue guidance','<p>Shares of Infosys declined by 4% during today’s trading session. This downward movement in the stock price follows the official announcement from the company regarding a reduction in its revenue growth guidance for the fiscal year 2027. Market participants reacted to this update by adjusting their positions, leading to the observed price correction on the stock exchanges.</p>\n<p>The revision in growth projections represents a change in the financial outlook provided by the management for the upcoming period. Revenue guidance is an estimate provided by a company to shareholders regarding its expected future income over a specific timeframe. Investors often monitor these updates closely as they reflect the internal projections and operational expectations of the firm for the fiscal year.</p>\n<p>The stock is currently trading below its previous closing level as market sentiment shifts following the guidance adjustment. Technical analysts may now look for a support level for the stock to stabilize after this decline. A support level is a price point where a stock has historically struggled to fall below, often acting as a floor for further downward movement.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The revision in the fiscal year 2027 revenue growth guidance directly influences how the market values the company. Investors are now observing the price action to determine if the stock will reach a resistance level. A resistance level is a price point where a stock typically faces selling pressure, hindering its ability to move higher. All market participants should monitor future filings for clarity.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261026-053216-Q298yX.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Hindu BusinessLine','https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/markets/infosys-shares-fall-4-after-fy27-revenue-growth-guidance-cut/article71625657.ece','2026-10-26 05:32:16','2026-10-26 05:32:16',0,27,'active','2026-10-26 05:32:16','2026-10-27 20:04:18'),
(185,'MakeMyTrip Reports $1.8 Million Profit for Q2 FY27 With Higher Gross Bookings','MakeMyTrip posted a profit of $1.8 million in Q2 FY27 as gross bookings increased by 20.9% to reach a total value of $2.7 billion during the quarter.','MakeMyTrip, Q2 FY27 results, travel sector, stock market news, gross bookings, Indian investors, quarterly earnings','<p>MakeMyTrip has officially reported a profit of $1.8 million for the second quarter of the fiscal year 2027. During this same period, the company recorded a 20.9% increase in gross bookings, reaching a total of $2.7 billion in constant currency terms. These figures reflect the financial performance of the business over the three-month duration ending in the second quarter.</p>\n<p>The company encountered specific operational challenges throughout the quarter. High airfares remained a persistent issue, and capacity constraints continued to impact the overall performance of its air ticketing business segment. These factors acted as headwinds against the company during this financial period. A quarterly report provides a standardized snapshot of a company’s financial health, including its revenue, expenses, and net profit or loss.</p>\n<p>The reported growth in gross bookings indicates the total value of travel services sold through the platform before accounting for cancellations and refunds. While the air ticketing division faced external pressures, the overall shift to a profit of $1.8 million marks a change in the financial outcome for the company. Investors typically monitor these reports to assess how specific market conditions influence the bottom line of a listed entity.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The financial data shows how the company managed its operations despite the mentioned market constraints. Monitoring these quarterly results helps in understanding the impact of pricing and capacity on the company&#039;s ability to maintain profitability in the competitive travel industry.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261027-000109-cXxIEw.webp',NULL,NULL,'Business Standard','https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/makemytrip-swings-to-1-8-million-profit-in-q2-fy27-despite-headwinds-126102700032_1.html','2026-10-27 00:01:09','2026-10-27 00:01:09',0,15,'active','2026-10-27 00:01:09','2026-10-28 05:39:22'),
(186,'Dalmia Bharat Reports Rs 205 Crore Loss During September Quarter','Dalmia Bharat reported a consolidated loss of Rs 205 crore for the September quarter of this year following an exceptional hit of Rs 339 crore.','Dalmia Bharat, Dalmia Bharat share price, Q2 results, September quarter, Dalmia Bharat loss, stock market, NSE, cement sector','<p>Dalmia Bharat recorded a consolidated loss of Rs 205 crore for the September quarter of this year. The financial performance of the company was impacted by an exceptional hit amounting to Rs 339 crore. This expense was attributed to asset impairment charges recorded during the period.</p>\n<p>The consolidated financial statement covers the operations of the business across the entire quarter ending in September. An impairment charge is an accounting recognition that an asset has lost value and is no longer worth its previously recorded amount on the balance sheet. This adjustment directly reduced the overall profitability of the firm for the three-month duration.</p>\n<p>Market participants often monitor quarterly results to understand how specific events or charges influence the bottom line of a listed entity. The reported figures reflect the accounting impact of the asset impairment on the earnings of the company for the current year. Investors typically review these disclosures to assess the financial health and operational outcomes reported in regulatory filings.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The reported loss highlights how specific accounting adjustments can alter the net financial results for a given period. Shareholders often track these updates to identify how non-recurring items affect the reported earnings per share. While the company has disclosed the impact of the asset impairment, market observers will continue to focus on future operational performance and the underlying stability of the business. Such updates are essential for maintaining transparency regarding the financial position of the firm.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261027-000154-FeY4sG.webp',NULL,NULL,'Economic Times','https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/earnings/dalmia-bharat-posts-rs-205-crore-q2-loss-on-exceptional-hit/articleshow/135217688.cms','2026-10-27 00:01:54','2026-10-27 00:01:54',0,16,'active','2026-10-27 00:01:54','2026-10-27 19:29:14'),
(187,'Indian Stock Markets Recover Following Four Days of Losses as Indices Rise','The Sensex and Nifty indices ended a four-day losing streak today, driven by gains in the metal, telecom, and healthcare sectors across the market.','Sensex, Nifty, Indian stock market, metal stocks, telecom stocks, healthcare stocks, NSE, BSE','<p>The Indian stock markets witnessed a recovery today as the Sensex jumped 483 points to close at 73,606.75. Simultaneously, the Nifty index rose 153 points to finish the session at 22,753.20. This positive movement successfully ended a four-day losing streak for the domestic benchmarks. An index is a statistical measure that tracks the performance of a specific group of stocks.</p>\n<p>Market participants observed a broad-based rally that helped the indices regain momentum after several days of decline. The upward trend was primarily supported by strong buying activity in metal, telecom, and healthcare stocks. These specific sectors saw increased interest from market participants throughout the trading day, contributing to the overall rise in the major indices.</p>\n<p>The session reflected a change in sentiment compared to the previous four trading sessions, which had been marked by consistent drops. By closing at 73,606.75 for the Sensex and 22,753.20 for the Nifty, the market demonstrated a rebound. Trading volume and sectoral participation remain key factors for analysts tracking the movement of these indices on the exchanges.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: While the recovery of 483 points on the Sensex and 153 points on the Nifty provides a positive signal, market participants often monitor resistance levels to gauge future price trends. Technical analysis involves studying historical chart patterns to identify potential price ceilings where selling pressure might increase. Investors should remain aware that market volatility is a natural part of trading, and individual stock performance can vary based on sector-specific developments and broader macroeconomic factors.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261027-003047-OnALCM.webp',NULL,NULL,'Business Standard','https://www.business-standard.com/markets/news/stock-markets-rebound-after-4-day-slump-sensex-jumps-483-points-126102601657_1.html','2026-10-27 00:30:47','2026-10-27 00:30:47',0,35,'active','2026-10-27 00:30:47','2026-10-28 04:26:50'),
(188,'Ather Energy Posts ₹1.26 Crore Profit and Announces Capacity Expansion Plans','Ather Energy reported a profit of ₹1.26 crore for the September quarter and revealed plans to increase production capacity by 225,000 units.','Ather Energy, Ather profit, EV sector, electric vehicles, manufacturing expansion, Indian auto industry, Hosur plant, Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar','<p>Ather Energy has announced a profit of ₹1.26 crore for the September quarter. Alongside these financial results, the company disclosed plans to increase its annual production capacity by 225,000 units. This expansion project involves a total investment of ₹122 crore, which will be distributed across the company&#039;s existing manufacturing facilities located in Hosur and Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar. The firm aims to complete this capacity enhancement by the second quarter of the financial year 2028.</p>\n<p>The investment of ₹122 crore is specifically earmarked for scaling operations at these two sites. By adding 225,000 units to its annual output, the company intends to increase the volume of vehicles it can produce. A manufacturing facility is a factory where goods are produced on a large scale for distribution and sale. The timeline for this development is set for Q2FY28, marking a strategic phase for the company’s production infrastructure.</p>\n<p>The reported profit of ₹1.26 crore reflects the company&#039;s financial performance during the recent September quarter. The company operates manufacturing plants in Hosur and Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar, which serve as the primary hubs for its production activities. The planned expansion is designed to utilize the existing footprint of these plants to accommodate the additional production capacity of 225,000 units.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The financial disclosure and capital expenditure plans provide clarity on the company&#039;s operational goals. Investors often monitor capacity expansion announcements to understand how a business intends to manage its future output requirements and long-term production capabilities within the competitive electric vehicle market.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261027-080705-QcJaiT.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Business Standard','https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/ather-reports-1-26-cr-profit-in-sep-qtr-plans-to-further-boost-capacity-126102601655_1.html','2026-10-27 00:30:55','2026-10-27 00:30:55',0,17,'active','2026-10-27 00:30:55','2026-10-27 15:04:17'),
(189,'Indian Rupee Declines to 95.18 Against US Dollar Amid Rising Oil Prices','The Indian rupee fell to 95.18 against the dollar this Monday as oil prices increased and importer demand for the American currency remained strong.','Indian rupee, USDINR, currency market, oil prices, forex, Indian economy, dollar demand','<p>On Monday, the Indian rupee weakened against the US dollar, reaching a level of 95.18. This movement in the currency market occurred as global oil prices saw an upward trend, which typically increases the demand for dollars from domestic importers. The currency reached this point of 95.18 during the trading session, reflecting the current supply and demand dynamics for foreign exchange.</p>\n<p>Market participants noted that there was consistent demand for dollars from importers throughout the day. This pressure on the rupee persisted even as market observers recorded higher hedging costs. Hedging is a financial strategy used by companies to reduce the risk of adverse price movements in an asset by taking an offsetting position in a related security.</p>\n<p>The fluctuation of the rupee against the dollar is influenced by various global and domestic economic factors. Crude oil is a major import for India, and higher prices often lead to a greater requirement for foreign currency to settle payments. This creates a direct impact on the valuation of the rupee in the international currency markets.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: A weaker rupee can influence the cost of imported goods and impact the profitability of companies that rely heavily on imports. Investors often monitor these currency shifts as they can affect inflation levels and the overall cost structure within the broader economy. Changes in the exchange rate may also influence the decisions of foreign institutional investors participating in the domestic equity markets.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261027-080035-MuXcOn.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Economic Times','https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/forex/rupee-slips-below-to-95-18-against-dollar-on-elevated-oil-prices/articleshow/135222166.cms','2026-10-27 01:00:35','2026-10-27 01:00:35',0,16,'active','2026-10-27 01:00:35','2026-10-27 21:39:38'),
(190,'Retail Investors Invest Rs 10,572 Crore in Indian Equities During September','Retail investors made a comeback to the secondary market in September, investing a total of ₹10,572 crore into equities after two months of inactivity.','retail investors, Indian stock market, equity investment, secondary market, September data, stock market trends, NSE, BSE','<p>Retail investors have returned to the secondary market in September, recording a total investment of ₹10,572 crore in equities. This activity follows a period of two months during which these participants remained silent regarding their market participation. The secondary market is a platform where investors trade existing securities that have already been issued by companies.</p>\n<p>This influx of capital highlights a notable shift in the behavior of individual participants within the broader financial landscape. The investment figure of ₹10,572 crore represents the net buying activity conducted by retail participants throughout the month of September. Such data points are often tracked to understand the prevailing sentiment among individual market participants who trade directly on stock exchanges.</p>\n<p>The return of this liquidity is a development observed after the previous two months of limited engagement from the retail segment. Market participants often monitor these monthly inflows to gauge the participation levels of non-institutional investors in the secondary market. A secondary market trade occurs when one investor sells shares to another investor rather than buying them directly from the issuing company.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The data regarding the ₹10,572 crore investment in September serves as a record of recent participation trends. Understanding these flows provides a clearer picture of how individual investors are navigating the current market environment. While this movement shows renewed interest, it remains a snapshot of past activity rather than an indication of future price movements or specific resistance levels for individual stocks.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261027-080032-2Gd83s.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Economic Times','https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/retail-investors-return-to-equities-with-rs-10572-crore-buying-in-september/articleshow/135221795.cms','2026-10-27 01:02:01','2026-10-27 01:02:01',0,24,'active','2026-10-27 01:02:01','2026-10-28 03:39:39'),
(191,'Power Sector Earnings Outlook: Elara Capital Highlights NTPC and Tata Power Performance','Rupesh Sankhe of Elara Capital anticipates better Q2 earnings for power firms due to higher electricity demand and coal offtake.','NTPC share price, Tata Power, power sector stocks, Q2 earnings, Elara Capital, Indian stock market, NSE, electricity demand','<p>Rupesh Sankhe, Senior Vice President at Elara Capital, projects that power sector companies will report stronger Q2 earnings. This positive outlook is primarily driven by an increase in electricity demand and higher coal offtake across the industry. Among the various players in the sector, the analyst has identified NTPC and Tata Power as top picks. Earnings reports are the official documents where companies disclose their financial performance for a specific period.</p>\n<p>The assessment from Elara Capital suggests that the operational environment for power generators is improving. By tracking variables like coal supply and total power consumption, analysts attempt to forecast the revenue streams of utility companies. This analysis focuses on the upcoming quarterly results, which provide a snapshot of how these firms are managing their production costs during the current cycle.</p>\n<p>Market analysts frequently review sectoral trends to determine which companies are positioned to handle changes in demand. By monitoring coal offtake, which is the amount of coal lifted from mines for power generation, experts gauge the intensity of plant operations. These metrics are essential for understanding the operational efficiency of large-scale utility providers in the country.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: Tracking sector-specific reports from brokerage firms helps in understanding the trends influencing the power industry. While analysts provide insights, individual portfolio decisions should align with personal risk appetite. Always verify company data through official regulatory filings before making any final decisions regarding your holdings in the stock market.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261027-080029-ei8UpX.jpg',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/earnings/ntpc-tata-power-q2-earnings-electricity-demand-elara-capital-iex-renewable-energy-nhpc-power-grid-results-alpha-article-20020051.htm','2026-10-27 06:17:29','2026-10-27 06:17:29',0,18,'active','2026-10-27 06:17:29','2026-10-28 02:47:13'),
(192,'Dr Reddy\'s Stock Could Rise 10-15% Following December Biosimilar Approval Says Systematix','Systematix analyst Vishal Manchanda evaluates the outlook for Dr Reddy’s, Mankind Pharma, Cipla, and Shilpa Medicare regarding key drug approvals.','Dr Reddy\'s share price, Systematix Group, pharma stocks, NSE, biosimilar approval, Indian stock market','<p>Systematix Group pharma analyst Vishal Manchanda has assessed the market outlook for Dr Reddy’s, Mankind Pharma, Cipla, and Shilpa Medicare. The report highlights that the stock price of Dr Reddy’s could potentially increase by 10-15% if a major biosimilar receives regulatory approval in December. A biosimilar is a biological product that is highly similar to an already approved reference medicine.</p>\n<p>The analysis focuses on the impact of upcoming drug approvals on the performance of these pharmaceutical entities. While the report mentions various companies, the specific growth projection is linked to the potential regulatory outcome for Dr Reddy’s in the final month of the year. Investors often monitor these regulatory milestones as they can influence the future revenue streams of drug manufacturers.</p>\n<p>The assessment by Vishal Manchanda also touches upon growth challenges faced by the sector. The pharmaceutical industry frequently deals with complex regulatory environments where the timing of product clearances plays a significant role in market valuation. Each company mentioned, including Mankind Pharma, Cipla, and Shilpa Medicare, operates within this competitive landscape where product pipelines are critical for long-term stability.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The potential 10-15% move in Dr Reddy’s is contingent upon a specific December approval. Market participants should note that resistance levels for such stocks can shift based on regulatory news, while support levels may be tested if approvals face delays. This report provides an independent analysis of current industry trends without offering any specific financial advice regarding individual portfolios.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261027-075155-ConI18.webp',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/stocks/dr-reddys-mankind-pharma-cipla-shilpa-medicare-stock-outlook-drug-approvals-systematix-group-alpha-article-20020035.htm','2026-10-27 06:17:42','2026-10-27 06:17:42',0,16,'active','2026-10-27 06:17:42','2026-10-28 04:14:33'),
(193,'L&T Secures Orders Worth Up To ₹10,000 Crore For Dhaka Metro Project','L&T and partner Sumitomo Corporation won orders worth up to ₹10,000 crore for the Dhaka Metro project as the company prepares for its Q2 financial results.','L&T, Dhaka Metro, infrastructure projects, stock market, construction sector, NSE, BSE, Q2 results','<p>L&amp;T has secured new orders valued at up to ₹10,000 crore for the Dhaka Metro project ahead of the company&#039;s upcoming Q2 results. The project, designated as CP09, will be executed by L&amp;T in partnership with the Japanese firm Sumitomo Corporation. This infrastructure development involves a comprehensive scope of work for the metro system in Bangladesh.</p>\n<p>The contract covers the design, procurement, installation, testing, and commissioning of the complete track works and power supply systems. These technical components are essential for the operational functionality of the metro rail network. A block deal refers to a single transaction of a large number of shares, which is often executed off the open market.</p>\n<p>L&amp;T is currently managing its operational commitments while moving toward the announcement of its financial performance for the second quarter. The company has maintained its focus on large-scale international infrastructure projects as part of its business activities. The engineering and construction sector remains a key area for such capital-intensive projects across the South Asian region.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The securing of this contract provides clarity on the order book status of the company before the release of the Q2 results. Market participants often track such project wins to assess the future revenue visibility of the firm. While the stock may see movement based on these developments, the current resistance level remains a point of interest. Investors should wait for official financial disclosures to understand the impact on margins.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261027-075150-0vCdql.webp',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/larsen-and-toubro-lt-share-price-major-order-win-up-to-10000-crore-dhaka-metro-project-q2-results-date-20020060.htm','2026-10-27 06:27:52','2026-10-27 06:27:52',0,18,'active','2026-10-27 06:27:52','2026-10-28 03:01:12'),
(194,'360 ONE Asset Executive Anup Maheshwari Expresses Optimism Regarding Indian Equity Markets','Anup Maheshwari of 360 ONE Asset notes that Indian markets are approaching the lower end of their range, supported by better earnings and valuations.','360 ONE Asset, Anup Maheshwari, Indian equity markets, stock market outlook, earnings, valuations, investment strategy','<p>Anup Maheshwari, who is associated with 360 ONE Asset, has shared his perspective on the current state of Indian equities. He stated that the domestic markets are currently moving toward the bottom of their established range. This assessment is based on a combination of improving corporate earnings and current market valuations.</p>\n<p>Equities represent ownership stakes in a company, which allow investors to participate in the growth and profitability of the business. By monitoring these financial indicators, market participants attempt to gauge the future direction of share prices. The observations provided by 360 ONE Asset highlight the importance of tracking internal corporate performance alongside broader economic metrics to understand market movements.</p>\n<p>Mr. Maheshwari suggested that those participating in the market should maintain a sense of patience during this period. His comments reflect an observation of the technical and fundamental factors currently influencing the trading environment in India. While volatility is a common feature of financial markets, the focus remains on the relationship between price levels and the underlying health of the companies involved.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: This update provides a professional perspective on the current positioning of Indian equities within their trading range. Understanding these insights regarding earnings and valuations can help individuals evaluate their own portfolios against the broader market trends. It is important to remember that market conditions are subject to change based on various economic factors. Investors often use such expert commentary to refine their approach to long-term financial planning and asset allocation decisions.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261027-075146-0gqK4M.webp',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/market-correction-volatility-analysts-upside-risk-360-one-asset-anup-maheshwari-fund-managers-geopolitical-tensions-crude-oil-prices-earnings-alpha-article-20020034.htm','2026-10-27 06:30:50','2026-10-27 06:30:50',0,25,'active','2026-10-27 06:30:50','2026-10-28 05:11:54'),
(195,'PG Electroplast Share Price Reacts to Q2 Results and Increased Trade Payables','PG Electroplast reported September quarter results beating expectations, though trade payables and gross debt rose due to ongoing capacity expansion plans.','PG Electroplast, PG Electroplast share price, Q2 results, NSE, stock market, Indian stocks, corporate earnings','<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">PG Electroplast share price will react to Q2 results that beat expectations, but trade payables rise following the company&#039;s performance in the September quarter. The financial figures disclosed for the period ended September surpassed the initial projections held by the market. These results reflect the current operational status of the firm as it navigates its fiscal year objectives.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The company reported that its gross debt has experienced an increase during this timeframe. This rise in debt levels is directly attributed to the ongoing capacity expansion plans currently being executed by the organization. Capacity expansion refers to the process of increasing a company&#039;s production output capabilities through new infrastructure or machinery investments.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Alongside the rise in debt, the report highlights that trade payables have also increased. Trade payables represent the total amount of money a company owes to its suppliers for goods or services received on credit. Monitoring these obligations is essential for understanding the short-term liquidity management and operational commitments of a business as it scales its activities.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">What it means for investors: The market will now evaluate the balance between the positive earnings performance and the growing liabilities. Investors often analyze how debt-funded expansion affects future profitability and cash flow sustainability. While the earnings exceeded projections, the rise in trade payables and total debt provides a specific context for the company’s current financial health. Market participants will be observing how these factors influence the stock price movement and the broader volatility of the scrip in upcoming trading sessions.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261028-000050-tjRJeH.jpg',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/pg-electroplast-share-price-reaction-q2-results-revenue-margin-beat-payables-debt-increase-cash-falls-outlook-capacity-expansion-20020813.htm','2026-10-28 00:00:50','2026-10-28 00:00:50',0,11,'active','2026-10-28 00:00:50','2026-10-28 05:09:27'),
(196,'Sebi Extends Compliance Deadline for Debenture Trustees Until April 27, 2027','The market regulator Sebi has granted a six-month extension for debenture trustees to meet specific operational requirements by April 27, 2027.','Sebi, debenture trustees, compliance deadline, financial regulations, Indian market news, capital markets, regulatory updates','<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Securities and Exchange Board of India, known as Sebi, announced on Tuesday that it has pushed back the deadline for debenture trustees. These entities now have until April 27, 2027, to fulfill specific requirements regarding activities conducted outside their core functions. This decision provides an additional six months for the relevant parties to align their internal processes with the regulatory framework set by the authority.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Debenture trustees are financial institutions that act as intermediaries to protect the interests of investors who hold debentures. Debentures are essentially debt instruments issued by companies to raise capital, where the trustee ensures that the issuer follows the terms of the trust deed. By extending this timeline, the regulator has effectively adjusted the compliance window for these specific operational mandates.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This regulatory change applies specifically to the activities governing the scope of work performed by these trustees. The extension was officially communicated on Tuesday, marking a shift from the previously established timeline. Market participants involved in debt instruments are now expected to complete the necessary adjustments by the new date of April 27, 2027.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">What it means for investors: This extension provides operational flexibility for debenture trustees to manage their regulatory obligations. Investors should note that this adjustment does not change the underlying structure of their holdings or the legal protections afforded to them. It simply shifts the timeframe for trustees to meet the specific requirements set by the regulator for their non-core activities.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261028-000119-duLFH7.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Business Standard','https://www.business-standard.com/markets/news/sebi-extends-compliance-deadline-for-debenture-trustees-till-april-2027-126102701364_1.html','2026-10-28 00:01:19','2026-10-28 00:01:19',0,14,'active','2026-10-28 00:01:19','2026-10-28 04:46:35'),
(197,'Icra Projects Credit Growth to Moderate in FY27 Amid Policy Rate Changes','Icra expects credit growth to slow to 15-16% in FY27 as policy rates harden. Public sector bank slippages are estimated to hit ₹1 lakh crore in FY27.','Icra, credit growth, FY27, public sector banks, Indian economy, banking sector, RBI','<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Credit growth in the Indian banking sector is projected to moderate to a range of 15-16% for FY27. According to the report by Icra, this slowdown in the expansion of loan books is driven by the impact of hardening policy rates. Policy rates are the interest rates set by the central bank to manage inflation and liquidity in the economy.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The report also highlights potential challenges regarding asset quality for state-run lenders. Fresh slippages for public sector banks are estimated to increase to ₹1 lakh crore in FY27. Slippages are defined as the amount of standard assets that turn into non-performing assets during a specific period. This rise in stressed assets indicates a shift in the repayment environment for these lending institutions.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The data suggests that the financial landscape is adjusting to the current interest rate cycle. As banks face higher costs of funds and changing borrower behavior, the pace of lending is expected to adjust. This trend reflects the ongoing transition in the credit cycle as institutions navigate the tightening monetary environment and its effect on their balance sheets throughout the upcoming fiscal year.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">What it means for investors: The projected moderation in credit growth and the rise in slippages for public sector banks highlight potential headwinds for the banking sector. Market participants monitor these credit metrics to gauge the health of financial stocks and the stability of the banking system in response to shifting macroeconomic conditions.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261028-010049-NorXod.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Economic Times','https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/credit-growth-to-moderate-in-h2-fy27-icra/articleshow/135248523.cms','2026-10-28 01:00:49','2026-10-28 01:00:49',0,13,'active','2026-10-28 01:00:49','2026-10-28 04:25:42'),
(198,'Samvat 2083: Eight Potential Triggers to Reverse Current Negative Market Sentiment','Axis Securities identifies eight key catalysts that could potentially improve the outlook for Indian equities following recent negative market trends.','Samvat 2083, Axis Securities, Indian stock market, market sentiment, equity outlook, NSE, Sensex','<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Axis Securities has identified eight specific triggers that could potentially reverse the current negative market sentiment for Samvat 2083. The report highlights factors such as a correction in crude oil prices and the stabilisation of foreign investments as primary catalysts for improving the overall outlook for Indian equities. These identified triggers are intended to provide a framework for understanding potential shifts in market direction during the upcoming period.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A correction in crude oil prices is often monitored by analysts because it directly impacts the import bill and inflation levels in India. Market sentiment refers to the prevailing attitude of investors regarding the anticipated price movement of a security or the broader market. When sentiment is negative, it often indicates that investors are more cautious or pessimistic about future performance.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The stabilisation of foreign institutional investor flows is another factor mentioned by Axis Securities. Foreign institutional investors are entities that invest in financial markets outside their home country, which significantly influences liquidity in the Indian stock exchanges. Monitoring these flows helps market participants gauge the level of confidence international capital providers have in the domestic economy and its listed companies.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">What it means for investors: The eight triggers outlined by the brokerage firm serve as indicators to track for potential changes in the market environment. While these factors are highlighted as catalysts, they do not guarantee a shift in trends. Investors typically monitor these macroeconomic variables to assess how global and domestic conditions might influence their portfolios in the near future.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261028-013029-aBuOSh.jpg',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/samvat-2083-eight-triggers-interest-rate-foreign-portfolio-investor-crude-oil-prices-that-can-reverse-current-negative-market-sentiment-20020690.htm','2026-10-28 01:30:29','2026-10-28 01:30:29',0,11,'active','2026-10-28 01:30:29','2026-10-28 04:49:03'),
(199,'Ather Energy Stock Price Performance and Market Outlook for Today','Ather Energy shares are trading at ₹1,671 following a 20 per cent surge this week, signaling a shift in the current short-term market trend.','Ather Energy, Ather Energy share price, Sensex, Nifty, stock market, Indian stock market, NSE, share prices','<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Ather Energy is currently trading at a price of ₹1,671 as investors monitor recent market movements. The stock has experienced a 20 per cent surge during this week, which follows a period of a corrective fall that had been impacting the price since a previous date.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The recent price action indicates that the corrective phase has reached its conclusion. Market participants are now observing the price levels to determine the strength of this upward movement. A corrective fall is a temporary decline in a stock&#039;s price that occurs within a larger trend.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Technical analysts often monitor price charts to identify potential support and resistance levels. In this context, a resistance level represents a price point where selling pressure might increase, while support is a level where buying interest could prevent further declines. These levels are derived from historical price data and volume patterns observed on the exchange.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">What it means for investors: The current data shows a shift in momentum for Ather Energy after the recent 20 per cent increase. Investors should remain aware that market volatility can influence price stability in the short term. It is important to note that the recent trend marks the end of the previous downward correction phase. All participants should conduct their own research before making any decisions based on these live market figures. The stock market involves risks that are inherent to the nature of equity trading and price fluctuations across different sectors.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261028-013040-zhoaqc.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Hindu BusinessLine','https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/markets/sensex-nifty50-today-stock-market-live-updates-28-october-2026/article71631075.ece','2026-10-28 01:30:40','2026-10-28 01:30:40',0,10,'active','2026-10-28 01:30:40','2026-10-28 05:02:11'),
(200,'Infy, Midhani, Choice Intl, Kothari Industrial, Subros, Gulf Oil, Exide and Steamhouse in Focus','Infy, Midhani, Choice Intl, Kothari Industrial, Subros, Gulf Oil, Exide, and Steamhouse are seeing market activity due to global deals and new partnerships.','Infy share price, Midhani, Choice Intl, Kothari Industrial, Subros, Gulf Oil, Exide, Steamhouse','<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Market participants are closely tracking Infy, Midhani, Choice Intl, Kothari Industrial, Subros, Gulf Oil, Exide, and Steamhouse today. These companies are generating interest following recent developments involving global deal activity and strategic partnerships. Such corporate movements influence how traders view specific scrips during active trading sessions on the stock exchange.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The momentum across the technology, manufacturing, and energy sectors is attributed to a series of major investments, the signing of new Memorandums of Understanding, and various contract wins. These activities are currently shaping the operational path for these eight entities. A Memorandum of Understanding is a formal agreement between parties that outlines the terms of an intended common line of action.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">These developments highlight the shift in business landscapes as firms look to expand through international collaborations. Each company is navigating these external changes, impacting their performance on the bourses. Analysts monitor these specific operational updates to understand the broader trends currently influencing the market sentiment for these particular stocks.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">What it means for investors: Tracking these companies is essential as news of partnerships and deals can lead to volatility in price movements. Investors often watch for a support level or a resistance level to manage their positions when trading stocks that are currently in the news due to high corporate activity. It is important to stay updated on these specific developments to understand how they might influence the short-term direction of these entities in the Indian market.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261028-020048-mPCGSX.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Hindu BusinessLine','https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/markets/buzzing-stocks-infy-midhani-choice-intl-kothari-industrial-subros-gulf-oil-exide-steamhouse/article71634126.ece','2026-10-28 02:00:48','2026-10-28 02:00:48',0,12,'active','2026-10-28 02:00:48','2026-10-28 05:24:00'),
(201,'Jio Platforms, RIL, HUL, Adani Enterprises and Other Stocks in Focus Today','Jio Platforms, RIL, HUL, Adani Enterprises, TVS Motor, Larsen & Toubro and Maruti Suzuki are in focus for investors on Wednesday, 28 October.','Jio Platforms share, RIL share, HUL share, Adani Enterprises, TVS Motor, L&T, Maruti Suzuki, NSE','<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Jio Platforms, Reliance Industries, Hindustan Unilever, Adani Enterprises, TVS Motor, Larsen &amp; Toubro and Maruti Suzuki are the stocks in focus for investors on Wednesday, 28 October. These companies are being tracked closely by market participants as the trading session begins. Tracking such stocks helps investors understand the current sentiment across different sectors in the Indian equity markets.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Equity indices often reflect the overall performance of these major corporations during the trading day. When specific companies are in focus, traders typically monitor their price movements and trading volumes to gauge market activity. A block deal is a single transaction of a large number of shares or a high total value, which can influence the daily price trends of these major entities.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Market participants analyze these specific stocks to observe how they react to broader economic news and sector-specific updates. By keeping an eye on these companies, investors stay updated on the price action of large-cap entities that carry significant weight in the benchmark indices. This monitoring process is a standard practice for those looking to follow the movement of influential firms listed on the exchange.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">What it means for investors: Tracking these stocks provides a view of how major companies perform on 28 October. By observing the price movements and volume trends of Jio Platforms, RIL, HUL, Adani Enterprises, TVS Motor, Larsen &amp; Toubro, and Maruti Suzuki, investors can identify the support and resistance levels for these stocks during the trading day.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261028-023019-7YTSR0.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Mint','https://www.livemint.com/market/stock-market-news/top-stocks-to-watch-today-jio-platforms-ril-hul-adani-enterprises-shares-in-focus-on-wed-28-oct-full-list-11793152271100.html','2026-10-28 02:30:19','2026-10-28 02:30:19',0,8,'active','2026-10-28 02:30:19','2026-10-28 05:09:27'),
(202,'Hindustan Unilever Reports 6 Percent Profit Rise to 2,844 Crore Rupees','Hindustan Unilever posted a 6 percent profit increase to 2,844 crore rupees as strong consumer demand successfully countered rising raw material expenses.','Hindustan Unilever, HUL share price, FMCG sector, NSE, BSE, Indian stock market, quarterly results, corporate earnings','<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Hindustan Unilever has announced its financial performance for the recent quarter, reporting a profit of 2,844 crore rupees. This figure represents a 6 percent increase compared to the previous period. The company stated that the growth in its bottom line was achieved despite the impact of higher raw material costs during the same timeframe.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The management noted that robust demand for its products across various categories played a critical role in maintaining financial stability. By effectively managing operational challenges, the company was able to offset the pressure exerted by increasing input prices. This balance between consumer interest and cost management remains a central theme in the latest financial filing from the organization.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A quarterly result refers to the periodic disclosure of a company&#039;s financial health, including revenue, expenses, and net profit, which allows stakeholders to assess performance over a three-month duration. These filings are mandatory for all publicly traded entities on the stock exchange to ensure transparency and provide investors with current data regarding the business operations and fiscal trajectory of the firm.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">What it means for investors: The reported 6 percent profit growth to 2,844 crore rupees highlights the company&#039;s ability to navigate inflationary pressures through sustained market demand. Investors often monitor these updates to gauge how specific corporations handle rising commodity prices while maintaining their margins. While this data provides insight into the recent quarter, market participants should continue to track how future raw material fluctuations might influence upcoming financial statements and overall profitability trends for the business.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261028-043631-qKNqBi.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Hindu BusinessLine','https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/companies/hindustan-unilever-profit-up-6-at-2844-crore-on-healthy-demand/article71634298.ece','2026-10-28 04:36:31','2026-10-28 04:36:31',0,4,'active','2026-10-28 04:36:31','2026-10-28 05:09:27'),
(203,'Subros Shares Surge 10 Percent Following Major Maruti Suzuki Order Win','Subros shares rose 10% after securing a ₹1,225 crore order from Maruti Suzuki to supply HVAC assemblies for the YM3 and YU0 models over seven years.','Subros share price, Maruti Suzuki order, HVAC assemblies, NSE, stock market news, auto components, Indian investors','<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Subros shares climbed 10% following the announcement that the company secured a ₹1,225 crore order from Maruti Suzuki. This contract involves the supply of HVAC assemblies for the automaker’s YM3 and YU0 models, with the production timeline spanning the vehicle models&#039; roughly seven-year life cycles.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The transaction highlights a major supply agreement within the automotive component sector. An HVAC assembly is a system responsible for the heating, ventilation, and air conditioning functions within a vehicle, which is essential for passenger comfort and climate control.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Market participants are currently monitoring the stock closely as it reacts to this development. Technical analysts often look for a resistance level to gauge potential price movements during periods of high volatility following significant corporate announcements. Investors generally watch these price levels to understand how the market processes new supply contracts.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">What it means for investors: While the order covers a long-term period of roughly seven years, it is important to note that this news reflects a specific contract win rather than a change in broader market conditions. Investors should monitor how this project impacts future financial filings and production schedules. The company has not provided further details regarding the specific delivery phases or the exact annual revenue split from this ₹1,225 crore deal. As always, market participants should remain cautious and base their decisions on the official disclosures provided by the firm to the stock exchanges regarding its long-term operational commitments.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261028-043637-mNbyiB.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Mint','https://www.livemint.com/market/stock-market-news/subros-shares-jump-10-after-rs-1-225-crore-maruti-suzuki-order-key-details-to-know-what-lies-ahead-for-investors-11793159896612.html','2026-10-28 04:36:37','2026-10-28 04:36:37',0,6,'active','2026-10-28 04:36:37','2026-10-28 05:09:27'),
(204,'Kirloskar Pneumatic Reports 9 Percent Decline in Q2 Net Profit to ₹40 Crore','Kirloskar Pneumatic posted a net profit of ₹40 crore for Q2 FY27. Total income for the quarter also saw a decline compared to the previous fiscal year.','Kirloskar Pneumatic, Kirloskar Pneumatic share price, Q2 results, quarterly earnings, Indian stock market, NSE, BSE, financial report','<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Kirloskar Pneumatic has reported a net profit of ₹40 crore for the second quarter of FY27, marking a 9% decline. During this period, the company recorded a total income of ₹334.4 crore, which is lower than the ₹393.6 crore reported in the same period of the previous fiscal year. Net profit represents the actual earnings of a company after all operating expenses, taxes, and interest costs have been deducted from the total revenue.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The financial data released for the second quarter highlights a shift in performance metrics for the firm. While the company generated ₹334.4 crore in total income, this figure reflects a reduction from the ₹393.6 crore achieved during the same period in the earlier fiscal year. These figures provide a specific snapshot of the company&#039;s financial health over the three-month period ending in the second quarter.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The reported net profit of ₹40 crore indicates the bottom-line result for the quarter. This figure is compared against the performance of the same quarter in the previous fiscal year to provide context on the current financial trajectory. Investors often look at these quarterly updates to assess how a company is managing its income and expenses in the current economic environment.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">What it means for investors: The reported figures for Kirloskar Pneumatic offer a look at the latest quarterly financial performance. When reviewing these updates, market participants often evaluate the resistance level of the stock based on how the company manages its income. These financial statements are based on the specific data provided for the second quarter of FY27.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261028-044225-Yb23RY.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Hindu BusinessLine','https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/companies/kirloskar-pneumatic-q2-net-profit-drops-9-to-40-crore/article71634212.ece','2026-10-28 04:42:25','2026-10-28 04:42:25',0,4,'active','2026-10-28 04:42:25','2026-10-28 05:09:28');
