(46,'OYO parent PRISM to reduce IPO size to ₹3,350 crore amid progress','OYO\'s parent PRISM reduces IPO fresh issue. Stronger operating performance reduces need for capital.','OYO, PRISM, IPO, fundraising, EBITDA, stock market','<p>OYO&#039;s parent company PRISM is planning to reduce the size of its initial public offering (IPO) fresh issue to ₹3,350 crore. This decision comes as the company&#039;s operating performance has improved, leading to a reduction in its need for fresh capital. An IPO is a way for companies to raise funds from the public by issuing shares, which can be used to finance business activities.</p>\n<p>The improvement in the company&#039;s EBITDA, which has more than doubled, is a key factor in this decision. EBITDA, or earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation, and amortization, is a measure of a company&#039;s profitability. This increase in earnings indicates a stronger financial position for the company. EBITDA is often used by investors to assess a company&#039;s financial health.</p>\n<p>The reduction in the IPO size is a result of the company&#039;s improved cash generation. As a result, PRISM requires less external funding to meet its business needs. This change in plans may reflect the company&#039;s ability to manage its finances more effectively. Fundraising through an IPO can provide companies with the necessary capital to expand their operations.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The reduced IPO size may indicate a more stable financial outlook for PRISM. Investors will be watching the company&#039;s progress closely as it prepares for its public market debut. Investors typically consider various factors, including a company&#039;s financial performance and funding needs, when making investment decisions. This information can help investors make informed choices about their investments.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261021-000149-DxFIIt.jpg',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/oyo-parent-prism-ipo-fresh-issue-3350-crore-20015549.htm','2026-10-21 00:01:49','2026-10-21 00:01:49',0,11,'active','2026-10-21 00:01:49','2026-10-25 13:32:21'),
(47,'Edelweiss Group to sell ₹1,200-crore stake in EAAA India Alternatives IPO','EAAA India Alternatives to float IPO, Edelweiss Group to sell shares.','EAAA India Alternatives, Edelweiss Group, IPO, OFS, NSE, Sensex','<p>EAAA India Alternatives is set to launch its ₹1,200-crore initial public offering on October 26. The issue is an Offer for Sale by Edelweiss Group, where the group will sell its existing shares. This means there will be no fresh issue of shares, and the proceeds will go to the selling shareholder. An initial public offering, or IPO, is a process by which a company raises capital by issuing shares to the public.</p>\n<p>The IPO launch is scheduled for October 26, and investors can expect to see the issue open for subscription on that day. An Offer for Sale, or OFS, is a process where existing shareholders sell their shares to the public, allowing them to exit their investment. This type of issue does not result in any fresh capital infusion into the company.</p>\n<p>Edelweiss Group is the sole seller in this IPO, and the entire issue size of ₹1,200 crore will be sold by the group. The IPO will provide an opportunity for investors to buy shares of EAAA India Alternatives. The issue size is a significant amount, indicating a substantial stake being sold by Edelweiss Group.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The IPO launch of EAAA India Alternatives will allow investors to participate in the issue and buy shares of the company. As an OFS, the issue will not result in any fresh capital infusion into the company, but will rather provide an exit opportunity for Edelweiss Group. Investors should review the issue details and consider their investment options carefully.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261021-010106-BTSSIg.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Hindu BusinessLine','https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/markets/eaaa-india-alternatives-to-float-1200-crore-ipo-on-oct-26/article71603713.ece','2026-10-21 01:01:06','2026-10-21 01:01:06',0,28,'active','2026-10-21 01:01:06','2026-10-28 05:40:12'),
(48,'Eric Schmidt to gain from Anthropic PBC\'s upcoming initial public offering','Eric Schmidt owns 1% of Anthropic PBC, set for a massive windfall.','Anthropic PBC, Eric Schmidt, Google, IPO, startup, windfall','<p>Eric Schmidt, the former CEO of Google, has a stake in Anthropic PBC, a startup. He owns about 1% of the company. This stake positions him for a significant financial gain. An initial public offering, or IPO, is when a company issues stocks to the public for the first time.</p>\n<p>The upcoming IPO of Anthropic PBC is expected to bring a financial windfall to its stakeholders, including Eric Schmidt. A windfall is a sudden, large amount of money, often received unexpectedly. In this case, the windfall would result from the IPO.</p>\n<p>A startup like Anthropic PBC is a newly formed company, typically in the early stages of development. Startups often rely on investments to grow and expand their operations. An IPO can provide a significant source of funding for a startup.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: the upcoming IPO of Anthropic PBC may be of interest to those looking to invest in startups with notable stakeholders like Eric Schmidt, who has a background in the tech industry, having led Google. Investors may want to consider the potential risks and rewards of investing in an IPO, as it can be a way to potentially earn high returns, but also involves uncertainty and risk.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261021-013112-EMwqMQ.jpg',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/former-google-ceo-eric-schmidts-1pc-anthropic-stake-set-to-pay-massive-windfall-20015433.htm','2026-10-21 01:31:13','2026-10-21 01:31:13',0,14,'active','2026-10-21 01:31:13','2026-10-26 08:49:19'),
(49,'PC Jeweller Q2 Net Profit Climbs 58 Percent to ₹331 Crore','PC Jeweller reported a 58% rise in Q2 net profit to ₹331 crore as revenue grew 28%. First-half revenue for FY27 reached ₹1,932 crore, up 25% year-on-year.','PC Jeweller, PC Jeweller share price, Q2 results, stock market India, jewellery sector, NSE, BSE, financial performance','<p>PC Jeweller announced its financial performance for the second quarter, reporting a net profit of ₹331 crore, which marks a 58% increase. During the same period, the company recorded a revenue growth of 28%. Additionally, for the first half of FY27, the consolidated revenue of the firm rose by 25% year-on-year to reach a total of ₹1,932 crore.</p>\n<p>The management stated that the company maintained its growth momentum throughout the quarter. This performance was supported by steady consumer demand for its products. A consolidated financial statement combines the assets and liabilities of a parent company with its various subsidiaries to provide a single view of the entity&#039;s health.</p>\n<p>The reported figures highlight the financial trajectory of the business over the recent three-month window and the initial six months of the current fiscal year. These numbers reflect the operational output and market activity of the firm during these specific timeframes. Investors often monitor these periodic disclosures to understand how a company manages its income and expenses relative to its total sales.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The disclosed data provides a factual update on the earnings and revenue trends of the company. Market participants analyze these specific financial metrics to track the performance of the business against its previous quarterly results. This information serves as a record of the financial activity reported by the company for the specified periods in the current fiscal year.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261022-000142-yzJVpL.jpg',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/earnings/pc-jeweller-q2-results-net-profit-rises-58-pc-to-rs-331-crore-revenue-up-28-pc-20016299.htm','2026-10-22 00:01:42','2026-10-22 00:01:42',0,26,'active','2026-10-22 00:01:42','2026-10-27 22:03:58'),
(50,'Carlsberg Nears Public Filing for $700 Million India IPO Launch','Carlsberg is preparing to file documents for an IPO of its India operations to raise $700 million, with a potential launch scheduled for December.','Carlsberg, IPO, India business, stock market, public filing, new listings, beverage industry, investment','<p>Carlsberg is reportedly nearing the public filing of documents for an initial public offering of its India business, aiming to raise as much as $700 million. The company is currently targeting a launch for this public offering as early as December. An IPO is the process by which a private company offers its shares to the public for the first time on a stock exchange.</p>\n<p>The move to initiate this public filing marks a significant step for the company as it prepares to enter the capital markets. The specified amount of $700 million represents the target capital the entity intends to secure through this market debut.</p>\n<p>The timeline for the launch is currently set for December, according to the available information regarding the company&#039;s plans. This schedule indicates the period during which the firm intends to complete its offering process for potential market participants.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The entry of a major entity into the public market provides new opportunities for portfolio diversification within the beverage sector. Investors typically monitor these filings to evaluate the financial disclosures and business details provided in the prospectus before making decisions. By tracking the progress of this $700 million offering, market participants can stay informed about the upcoming supply of new shares. This development remains subject to the company&#039;s official filing procedures and the regulatory environment governing such public issues in the Indian market.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261022-010047-RCZYyt.jpg',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/carlsberg-near-public-filing-usd-700-million-india-ipo-20016099.htm','2026-10-22 01:00:47','2026-10-22 01:00:47',0,21,'active','2026-10-22 01:00:47','2026-10-26 10:36:04'),
(51,'Gold Prices Near Rs 1.47 Lakh Per 10 Grams As Silver Declines','Gold prices moved lower and silver dropped by Rs 1,144 per kg on the MCX as investors monitored the US Federal Reserve for future interest rate signals.','gold price, silver price, MCX, US Federal Reserve, interest rates, bullion market, commodity trading, India gold','<p>Gold prices are trading near Rs 1.47 lakh per 10 grams following a slight decline in value. Simultaneously, silver has recorded a decrease of Rs 1,144 per kg on the Multi Commodity Exchange. Market participants are currently monitoring these movements as they prepare for the upcoming policy decision from the US Federal Reserve.</p>\n<p>The fluctuations in the bullion market are driven by anticipation regarding the US Federal Reserve’s stance on interest rates. Investors are looking for clues from the central bank that could influence the cost of borrowing. The MCX serves as a platform in India where traders buy and sell commodity derivatives, which are contracts deriving their value from an underlying asset like gold or silver.</p>\n<p>Traders are maintaining a cautious approach while waiting for official signals regarding potential adjustments to interest rates. These policy decisions are significant because they often dictate the flow of capital between different asset classes. As the market awaits clarity, the price trends for both gold and silver remain sensitive to any new information released by the US monetary authorities.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The ongoing price adjustments reflect the sensitivity of precious metals to global central bank policies. Monitoring official announcements from the US Federal Reserve is essential for those tracking commodity trends. Investors should observe how these international cues influence domestic market sentiment and impact the valuation of their holdings in the coming trading sessions.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261022-013105-PhpLxz.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Economic Times','https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/commodities/news/gold-prices-near-rs-1-47-lakh/10-grams-silver-falls-by-rs-1144/kg-as-traders-await-fed-rate-signals-what-lies-ahead/articleshow/135083841.cms','2026-10-22 01:31:05','2026-10-22 01:31:05',0,14,'active','2026-10-22 01:31:05','2026-10-26 08:49:19'),
(52,'TTML Reports Q2 Loss of ₹59 Crore as Revenue Increases by 8 Percent','TTML reported a reduced loss of ₹59 crore for the second quarter. Meanwhile, the stock price rose by 9.26 percent during the trading session on the NSE.','TTML, Tata Teleservices, Q2 results, NSE, stock market, share price, India','<p>TTML has announced its financial performance for the second quarter, reporting a loss of ₹59 crore alongside an 8 percent increase in revenue. The firm stated that revenue from operations reached ₹309.65 crore, marking an 8.2 percent growth compared to the same period last year. Following these disclosures, company shares saw a 9.26 percent increase on the NSE, reaching a price of ₹35.03 by early afternoon. Trading activity remained high, with total volumes recorded at over 9.16 crore shares.</p>\n<p>A financial loss occurs when a company&#039;s total expenses exceed its total revenue over a specific period. These figures reflect the latest operational data provided by the firm for the current fiscal quarter. Investors monitor such updates to understand the financial trajectory of listed entities.</p>\n<p>The surge in the stock price coincided with the release of these quarterly results. Market participants observed the price movement as the stock reached ₹35.03 during the active trading hours on the NSE. The reported growth in revenue of 8.2 percent represents the year-on-year change for the business. This data provides a snapshot of the company&#039;s financial standing as presented in the recent regulatory filing.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The reported figures provide a look at the company&#039;s quarterly performance and the reaction in the stock price. Market participants review these updates to track how revenue changes and loss adjustments impact trading activity. All data points, including the ₹59 crore loss and the 8.2 percent revenue growth, are based on the latest company report.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261023-003115-2siZdC.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Hindu BusinessLine','https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/markets/stock-markets/ttml-narrows-q2-loss-to-59-crore-revenue-up-8-stock-surges-9-on-results-day/article71610687.ece','2026-10-23 00:31:15','2026-10-23 00:31:15',0,9,'active','2026-10-23 00:31:15','2026-10-26 00:04:49'),
(53,'UBS Acquires 4.8% Stake In 360 One WAM For Over $200 Million','Swiss bank UBS has acquired a 4.8% stake in 360 One WAM by converting 20.5 million warrants into shares, valued at over $200 million.','UBS, 360 One WAM, stake acquisition, warrants, Indian wealth management, stock market news, financial deals, equity investment','<p>UBS has officially acquired a 4.8% stake in 360 One WAM in a transaction valued at over $200 million. The Swiss bank finalized this acquisition by converting 20.5 million warrants into equity shares of the Indian wealth management company. Warrants are financial instruments that grant the holder the right to purchase company shares at a specific price within a set timeframe.</p>\n<p>This move marks a deepening of the existing partnership between the two financial entities. Previously, the Swiss bank had transferred its onshore wealth management business to the Indian firm. This strategic transition of business operations formed the foundation for the current equity involvement between the two parties.</p>\n<p>The conversion process effectively integrates the bank further into the capital structure of 360 One WAM. By exercising these warrants, the institution has increased its ownership interest, reflecting the formalization of their collaborative relationship. Such transactions are common methods for institutional investors to solidify their holdings in specific target firms without navigating the open market.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The increased stake held by a major global institution like UBS provides clarity regarding the ownership structure of 360 One WAM. While this transaction demonstrates a commitment from the Swiss bank to the Indian wealth manager, it remains a corporate development regarding the distribution of equity. Investors should monitor how this relationship influences the future operational direction of the company as both entities continue their long-term professional association in the financial sector.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261023-010054-eJZKFP.jpg',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/ubs-acquires-4-8-pc-stake-360-one-wam-converting-warrants-20017136.htm','2026-10-23 01:00:54','2026-10-23 01:00:54',0,24,'active','2026-10-23 01:00:54','2026-10-27 18:02:33'),
(54,'Sebi Permits Margin Relief for Subsequent Trades Using Early Pay-in of Securities','Sebi now allows margin relief on cash-market trades when early pay-in is accepted, reducing requirements for clients holding net sell obligations.','Sebi, margin relief, stock market, early pay-in, cash market, trading rules, Indian investors','<p>The Securities and Exchange Board of India has introduced new guidelines permitting margin relief for subsequent cash-market trades when investors utilize early pay-in of securities. This regulatory update applies specifically to instances where an early pay-in has been successfully accepted by the clearing corporation. By facilitating this change, the regulator aims to streamline the existing margin framework for market participants.</p>\n<p>Under the current system, margin requirements act as collateral that traders must maintain to cover potential losses during settlement cycles. This adjustment provides a mechanism for clients who possess net sell obligations to manage their capital more efficiently during the trading day. The move focuses on the technical processing of securities that have already been transferred to the clearing house before the final settlement deadline occurs.</p>\n<p>This policy shift is designed to optimize the usage of funds and securities within the financial ecosystem. By recognizing early pay-in as a valid form of margin relief, the regulator intends to reduce the financial burden on participants who have already fulfilled their delivery requirements for specific transactions. The updated process ensures that the clearing mechanism remains aligned with current market practices while maintaining necessary risk control standards for all active participants.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: This change allows traders to utilize their early pay-in of securities to offset margin requirements for later trades. It effectively lowers the amount of liquid capital that must be kept as collateral when a net sell position is already secured through the early delivery process.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261023-020051-PZKmt4.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Business Standard','https://www.business-standard.com/markets/news/sebi-allows-margin-relief-on-subsequent-trades-against-early-pay-in-126102201148_1.html','2026-10-23 02:00:51','2026-10-23 02:00:51',0,17,'active','2026-10-23 02:00:51','2026-10-26 11:08:21'),
(55,'Tata Motors CV Reports Profit Of ₹2,138 Crore Following 41.9% Revenue Growth','Tata Motors CV posted a profit of ₹2,138 crore in Q2 as revenue rose 41.9%. The firm is nearing the finalization of its €3.91-billion Iveco acquisition.','Tata Motors CV, Tata Motors share price, Q2 results, NSE, stock market, Indian automotive sector, financial news','<p>Tata Motors CV announced a financial rebound in its latest performance report, recording a profit of ₹2,138 crore for the second quarter. During this same period, the company witnessed a notable increase in its top-line performance, with revenue jumping by 41.9%. These figures reflect the current fiscal position of the business as it manages its ongoing operational activities in the commercial vehicle segment.</p>\n<p>Alongside these financial results, the company provided an update regarding its international expansion strategy. The organization is moving closer to completing its €3.91-billion Iveco acquisition. An acquisition is a corporate action where one company purchases most or all of another company&#039;s ownership stakes to assume control of its assets and operations.</p>\n<p>The management confirmed that the process for this significant deal is currently underway. This transaction involves a substantial capital commitment of €3.91-billion, marking a major step in the company&#039;s international footprint. The firm continues to navigate the regulatory and procedural requirements necessary to finalize the transfer of ownership of the entity involved in this transaction.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The reported profit of ₹2,138 crore and the 41.9% revenue growth provide a snapshot of the company&#039;s fiscal health during the quarter. Market participants are monitoring the €3.91-billion Iveco acquisition as it progresses toward completion. Investors often track such large-scale corporate developments to understand how they might impact the company&#039;s future balance sheet and overall market position in the automotive industry.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261024-000119-pDZ0vu.webp',NULL,NULL,'Hindu BusinessLine','https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/companies/tata-motors-cvs-profit-rebounds-to-2138-crore-in-q2-as-revenue-jumps-419/article71615837.ece','2026-10-24 00:01:19','2026-10-24 00:01:19',0,9,'active','2026-10-24 00:01:19','2026-10-26 19:40:55'),
(56,'Himadri Speciality Chemicals Announces ₹1,613 Crore Investment for Capacity Expansion Projects','Himadri Speciality Chemicals will invest ₹1,613 crore to expand capacity in speciality chemicals, lithium iron phosphate, and new energy materials.','Himadri Speciality Chemicals, chemical sector stocks, capacity expansion, Indian stock market, NSE, investment news, speciality chemicals, lithium iron phosphate','<p>Himadri Speciality Chemicals has officially announced a capital expenditure plan amounting to ₹1,613 crore. This investment is designated for capacity expansion across the company’s key business segments, specifically targeting speciality chemicals, lithium iron phosphate, and new energy materials.</p>\n<p>The planned expenditure aims to enhance the company&#039;s production capabilities in these specific areas. Capital expenditure, commonly referred to as capex, represents the funds a company uses to acquire, upgrade, and maintain physical assets such as buildings, technology, or equipment.</p>\n<p>The strategic focus of this financial commitment is to drive sustainable growth and profitability for the firm. By expanding its operational footprint in the lithium iron phosphate and new energy materials sectors, the company intends to strengthen its presence within these evolving industrial segments.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: This announcement details the company&#039;s specific financial commitment toward its future production capacity. Market participants should monitor how these investments influence the firm&#039;s operational scale and financial performance in the coming periods. Investors often track such large-scale capital deployments to understand how a business intends to utilize its resources to build long-term value. While the company has outlined its expansion roadmap, this information is provided for tracking purposes only and does not constitute any form of financial guidance. The market will observe the execution of these projects as the company progresses with its stated expansion goals in the speciality chemicals and energy materials space.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261024-013020-zk9qcf.jpg',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/business/himadri-speciality-chemicals-rs-1613-crore-capacity-expansion-key-businesses-20017610.htm','2026-10-24 01:30:20','2026-10-24 01:30:20',0,24,'active','2026-10-24 01:30:20','2026-10-28 05:37:32'),
(57,'IndusInd Bank Reports Q2 Net Profit Of Rs 1,176 Crore','IndusInd Bank declared a standalone net profit of Rs 1,176 crore for the second quarter, recovering from a loss of Rs 445 crore in the same period last year.','IndusInd Bank, Q2 results, net profit, banking sector, NSE, BSE, Indian stock market','<p>IndusInd Bank has officially released its financial performance for the second quarter of this fiscal year. The lender reported a standalone net profit of Rs 1,176 crore. This figure marks a shift in the bank&#039;s financial position when compared to the corresponding period of the previous year, during which the institution recorded a loss of Rs 445 crore. A standalone net profit represents the earnings of a company calculated without including the financial results of its various subsidiaries.</p>\n<p>The transition from a loss of Rs 445 crore to a profit of Rs 1,176 crore highlights the change in the bank’s quarterly outcome. Investors often monitor these quarterly disclosures to assess the financial health of listed entities. These reports are mandatory filings submitted to stock exchanges to ensure transparency for all market participants.</p>\n<p>Market analysts frequently review these figures to determine if the stock price is approaching a specific resistance level or a support level. Such technical indicators are used by traders to track price movements based on the latest financial updates provided by the bank. The bank&#039;s performance is now part of the public record for this fiscal period.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The reported profit of Rs 1,176 crore provides the latest data regarding the bank&#039;s current financial standing. Shareholders now have access to the specific figures for the second quarter, allowing them to evaluate the company&#039;s performance against the previous year&#039;s loss of Rs 445 crore. This information serves as the basis for understanding the recent economic activity reported by the lender.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261024-020042-VwTnNA.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Economic Times','https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/earnings/indusind-bank-q2-results-lender-posts-profit-of-rs-1176-crore-vs-rs-445-crore-loss-a-year-ago/articleshow/135142692.cms','2026-10-24 02:00:42','2026-10-24 02:00:42',0,13,'active','2026-10-24 02:00:42','2026-10-27 08:44:47'),
(58,'Goldman Sachs Downgrades Ola Electric Stock to Sell With ₹23 Resistance Level','Goldman Sachs has downgraded Ola Electric to Sell, reducing the resistance level to ₹23 from ₹39.28 due to various operational and financial concerns.','Ola Electric share price, Goldman Sachs report, NSE, stock market India, electric vehicle stocks, Ola Electric downgrade, Indian stock news','<p>Goldman Sachs has downgraded the stock of Ola Electric to Sell and lowered its resistance level to ₹23 from the previous level of ₹39.28. This adjustment follows a review of the company&#039;s financial position and operational performance. A resistance level is the price point at which market participants expect a stock to face selling pressure, making it difficult for the price to rise further.</p>\n<p>The financial institution cited several specific factors for this change in its outlook. These include the company&#039;s weak cash flow and its ongoing requirements for additional funding. Furthermore, the report pointed to high interest costs that the business is currently facing, alongside various operational challenges that have impacted its performance. These elements combined form the basis for the revised valuation provided by the analysts.</p>\n<p>Investors often track such research updates to understand how global financial institutions perceive the financial health of listed entities. When a brokerage firm adjusts its outlook, it reflects a reassessment of the company&#039;s ability to manage its debt or generate sufficient liquidity to sustain its daily business activities. Such reports are part of the broader market analysis conducted by financial experts.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The change in the resistance level for Ola Electric highlights the importance of monitoring cash flow and interest expenses. Market participants should observe how the stock price reacts to these updated figures in upcoming trading sessions. Tracking these financial metrics is essential for observing how external analysts view the company&#039;s ability to overcome its current operational hurdles.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261025-003049-4s3QFK.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Mint','https://www.livemint.com/market/stock-market-news/goldman-sachs-ola-electric-downgrade-why-stock-rating-changed-to-sell-23-downside-seen-new-target-price-rationale-11792817294346.html','2026-10-25 00:30:50','2026-10-25 00:30:50',0,15,'active','2026-10-25 00:30:50','2026-10-28 05:16:17'),
(59,'Castrol India Q3 Profit Declines 49.3 Percent Amid Rising Raw Material Costs','Castrol India reported a sharp decline in Q3 financial results as net profit fell by 49.3 percent to ₹176.4 crore due to higher input and currency costs.','Castrol India, Castrol India share price, Q3 results, Indian stock market, NSE, BSE, corporate earnings','<p>Castrol India announced its financial performance for the third quarter, reporting a net profit of ₹176.4 crore, which represents a decline of 49.3 percent sequentially. This drop in profitability follows a period where the company faced increased raw material costs and adverse currency movements. The firm also noted a decline in total revenue for the same period. Financial results are the periodic disclosures companies make to update shareholders on their profitability and operational performance.</p>\n<p>The company attributed these financial outcomes to the rising expenses associated with raw materials required for their operations. Furthermore, the volatility in currency exchange rates exerted additional pressure on the margins during the quarter. These combined factors contributed to the overall reduction in the bottom line reported by the organization in their latest regulatory filing. Margins refer to the difference between the selling price of a product and the cost of the inputs used to produce it.</p>\n<p>Investors often monitor these quarterly updates to assess how external economic factors impact specific businesses. The data released by Castrol India provides a clear snapshot of the current challenges regarding input costs and currency fluctuations. Market participants typically observe such reports to understand the financial health of the company in the current economic environment.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The reported figures highlight the direct impact of inflationary pressures on corporate earnings. Shareholders should note that these results reflect the specific cost environment faced by the company during the third quarter period.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261025-010046-epHCin.jpg',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/castrol-india-share-price-q3-results-profit-drops-raw-material-costs-weigh-margins-20018596.htm','2026-10-25 01:00:46','2026-10-25 01:00:46',0,13,'active','2026-10-25 01:00:46','2026-10-27 23:47:37'),
(60,'UTI AMC Reports 17 Percent Rise In Net Profit To ₹132 Crore','UTI AMC recorded a net profit of ₹132 crore for the period. Income for the company decreased slightly to ₹415 crore from the previous ₹419 crore.','UTI AMC, UTI AMC share price, quarterly results, Indian stock market, financial news, NSE, BSE, asset management','<p>UTI AMC has announced its financial results, reporting that its net profit increased by 17 percent to reach a total of ₹132 crore. This financial update also highlights that the company’s income for the period was recorded at ₹415 crore, which is a marginal decline when compared to the previous figure of ₹419 crore.</p>\n<p>A net profit is the actual amount of money a business keeps after paying all its operational and tax-related expenses. These figures reflect the performance of the firm over the specific timeframe provided in the latest regulatory filing. Investors often monitor these periodic disclosures to understand the current financial health of the listed entity as reported by the management.</p>\n<p>The slight dip in income from ₹419 crore to ₹415 crore represents a minor change in the top-line performance of the company. Such fluctuations in income are common in the financial services sector and are often influenced by market conditions affecting fee-based revenues. The company continues to operate within the regulatory framework established for asset management firms in India.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: These figures provide a clear picture of the recent profitability and income trends for UTI AMC. Market participants typically observe these official reports to assess how the business is managing its costs and revenue streams in the current environment. While the profit shows a positive shift of 17 percent, the marginal change in total income is a detail that market observers will evaluate alongside the broader performance metrics of the company.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261025-013045-FllkKh.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Hindu BusinessLine','https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/money-and-banking/uti-amc-net-up-17-to-132-cr/article71617031.ece','2026-10-25 01:30:45','2026-10-25 01:30:45',0,16,'active','2026-10-25 01:30:45','2026-10-27 20:03:04'),
(61,'Top 10 Indian Firms Lose ₹1.55 Trillion in Market Valuation Last Week','Eight of the top 10 most valuable Indian companies saw their market capitalization drop by Rs 1.55 lakh crore, led by HDFC Bank and Bajaj Finance.','HDFC Bank, Bajaj Finance, market cap, stock market, valuation, Sensex, NSE, Indian stocks','<p>The combined market valuation of eight of the top 10 most valuable firms in India decreased by Rs 1.55 lakh crore during the previous week. HDFC Bank and Bajaj Finance were the primary contributors to this total decline in market capitalization. Market capitalization is the total value of a company’s outstanding shares based on the current market price.</p>\n<p>Among the 10 most valuable companies, eight experienced a reduction in their total worth. These fluctuations reflect the broader movements within the domestic equity indices as investors adjusted their positions. While some firms saw their valuations contract, the losses were most pronounced in the financial sector, specifically impacting the two major entities mentioned.</p>\n<p>The stock market serves as a platform where the total valuation of listed companies fluctuates daily based on trading activity and investor sentiment. When the market capitalization of these major firms drops, it often influences the overall performance of benchmark indices. These shifts highlight how the valuations of large-cap companies are sensitive to the prevailing trading environment and the collective actions of market participants.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: Tracking the changes in market capitalization for the top 10 companies provides insights into the general direction of the broader market. These large firms often carry significant weight in major indices, meaning their price movements can impact the performance of index-based portfolios. Investors typically monitor these valuation shifts to understand how leading companies are faring relative to the market and to gauge overall sentiment in the financial landscape.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261026-003029-FZqUmV.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Business Standard','https://www.business-standard.com/markets/news/top-10-firms-lose-1-55-trillion-in-mcap-as-hdfc-bank-bajaj-finance-fall-126102500268_1.html','2026-10-26 00:30:29','2026-10-26 00:30:29',0,10,'active','2026-10-26 00:30:29','2026-10-27 06:02:19'),
(62,'Nifty Outlook for October 26: 22,200 Support Level as Crude Oil Hits $117','Nifty faces a critical test at 22,200 amid rising crude oil prices of $117. Investors are closely watching Fed policy and upcoming corporate earnings.','Nifty, Nifty index, crude oil, stock market, NSE, Sensex, market outlook, trading','<p>The Nifty index faces a critical session on October 26 as the benchmark establishes 22,200 as a key support level. This comes as global crude oil prices have climbed to $117 per barrel. Market participants are now focusing on the upcoming Federal Reserve policy decisions and the latest corporate earnings reports. A support level is a price point where a stock or index has historically had difficulty falling below.</p>\n<p>The index has struggled recently, recording a decline over four consecutive sessions. This downward trend has impacted broader market sentiment, with small-cap stocks experiencing their steepest weekly decline. These movements reflect the current volatility within the financial landscape as traders evaluate macroeconomic pressures and individual company performance.</p>\n<p>Investors are monitoring these developments to determine if the Nifty can successfully arrest its current losing streak or if the market will face further downside pressure. The combination of rising energy costs and central bank interest rate policies remains a primary influence on trading activity. Understanding these macroeconomic indicators helps market participants assess the broader economic environment.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The current market environment requires close attention to the 22,200 support level on the Nifty index. With crude oil prices at $117 and major policy announcements ahead, volatility may continue to influence trading decisions. Investors should remain aware of how these external factors impact their portfolios while focusing on the upcoming earnings results that will provide clarity on individual company performance in this challenging economic climate.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261026-010037-IFAhys.jpg',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/nifty-outlook-monday-october-26-22200-key-support-crude-oil-fed-policy-earnings-in-focus-20018821.htm','2026-10-26 01:00:38','2026-10-26 01:00:38',0,10,'active','2026-10-26 01:00:38','2026-10-27 13:37:10'),
(63,'Foreign Portfolio Investors Pull Out Rs 48,056 Cr From Indian Equities This October','Foreign portfolio investors have withdrawn Rs 48,056 crore from Indian stock markets in October as rising crude oil prices impact investor sentiment.','FPI, Indian stock market, equity outflow, crude oil prices, NSE, BSE, foreign investment, Indian economy','<p>Foreign Portfolio Investors have withdrawn a total of Rs 48,056 crore from Indian equities during the month of October so far. This substantial outflow of capital from the domestic market occurs as global investors react to the ongoing volatility in crude oil prices. Foreign Portfolio Investors are entities that invest in financial assets of a country other than their own, often influencing market liquidity.</p>\n<p>The recent trend of selling by overseas participants is linked to broader concerns regarding inflation and the fluctuating costs of energy resources. While the market witnessed heavy selling pressure throughout the month, there have been some recent signs indicating a moderation in the pace of these equity withdrawals. Market participants continue to monitor these capital flows closely as they impact the overall stability of the domestic indices.</p>\n<p>The relationship between crude oil prices and equity markets is significant for India, as the nation is a major importer of oil. When energy costs rise, it can influence the fiscal deficit and the valuation of domestic companies. A block deal is a single transaction of a large number of shares, often used by institutional investors to adjust their holdings without causing excessive volatility in the open market.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The current outflow reflects a cautious approach by international participants. Monitoring these net investment figures is essential for understanding the sentiment of foreign institutions. Investors should observe how these capital movements interact with local economic indicators and the prevailing resistance level of major indices during this period.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261026-013036-hslAby.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Economic Times','https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/fpis-withdraw-rs-48056-cr-from-equities-in-oct-so-far-amid-elevated-crude-oil-prices/articleshow/135185267.cms','2026-10-26 01:30:36','2026-10-26 01:30:36',0,12,'active','2026-10-26 01:30:36','2026-10-27 06:30:18'),
(64,'Tata Consumer Products Q2 Profit Increases 18 Percent With Higher Revenue','Tata Consumer Products reports an 18% profit rise and 14% revenue growth to ₹5,661 crore for the quarter ending September 30, 2026.','Tata Consumer Products, TCPL share price, Q2 results, Tata Group, NSE, stock market, Indian stocks, quarterly earnings','<p>Tata Consumer Products has reported its unaudited financial performance for the period ending September 30, 2026. The firm achieved an 18% increase in profit and a 14% rise in total revenue, which reached ₹5,661 crore. Additionally, the company declared a dividend for its shareholders as part of these latest financial disclosures.</p>\n<p>Financial results are periodic statements that allow publicly traded companies to inform the public about their earnings, expenses, and fiscal health. These reports are mandatory filings for entities listed on stock exchanges, providing transparency for those monitoring the company’s economic trajectory. Investors analyze these documents to understand the profitability of the firm over a three-month interval.</p>\n<p>Regarding technical price levels for the stock, market participants track specific indicators to manage their positions. A support level represents a price point where a stock historically struggles to fall further, while a resistance level indicates a price ceiling where upward movement might encounter selling pressure. These technical markers are used by traders to establish entry and exit points.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The growth in revenue and profit provides a snapshot of the company&#039;s financial standing as of September 30, 2026. While the dividend declaration adds a return for shareholders, the earnings figures reflect the specific fiscal outcomes for the quarter. Market participants will now observe how these results influence the stock&#039;s price action relative to its support and resistance levels in upcoming trading sessions.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261027-000059-RPbJzR.webp',NULL,NULL,'CNBC-TV18','https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/earnings/tata-consumer-q2-results-profit-beats-estimates-growth-businesses-surge-40-percent-tata-salt-starbucks-sampann-20019570.htm','2026-10-27 00:00:59','2026-10-27 00:00:59',0,10,'active','2026-10-27 00:00:59','2026-10-28 05:11:51'),
(65,'Tamilnad Mercantile Bank Reports 42 Percent Net Profit Growth For Q2 Period','Tamilnad Mercantile Bank posted a net profit of Rs 451 crore for the July to September quarter, driven by an increase in net interest income.','Tamilnad Mercantile Bank, Q2 results, net profit, banking sector, TMB share, Indian stock market, quarterly earnings, NSE','<p>Tamilnad Mercantile Bank announced its financial performance for the quarter spanning July to September, reporting a net profit of Rs 451 crore. This figure represents a 42% increase compared to the previous corresponding period. The growth in the bottom line was primarily supported by high net interest income recorded during these three months. Net interest income is the difference between the interest earned by a bank from its lending activities and the interest paid to its depositors.</p>\n<p>The bank’s financial disclosure highlights the specific earnings achieved during the second quarter of the current fiscal year. By focusing on core banking operations, the institution managed to improve its profitability metrics significantly. The reported profit of Rs 451 crore reflects the bank’s operational outcome for the specified timeframe, providing a clear snapshot of its earnings trajectory for the July to September window.</p>\n<p>Investors often track these quarterly disclosures to understand the operational efficiency of financial institutions. These reports are mandatory filings that allow stakeholders to review the income generated and expenses incurred by a company over a three-month period. The 42% growth indicates how the bank navigated its interest-related revenue streams during the quarter.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The reported net profit of Rs 451 crore provides a factual basis for evaluating the bank&#039;s recent performance. Market participants may observe how this financial outcome impacts the stock&#039;s movement relative to its current support or resistance level of the bank&#039;s share price in the coming trading sessions.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261027-003029-jIeOe5.webp',NULL,NULL,'Economic Times','https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/earnings/tamilnad-mercantile-bank-q2-results-net-profit-rises-42-to-record-rs-451-crore-on-high-net-interest-income/articleshow/135214844.cms','2026-10-27 00:30:30','2026-10-27 00:30:30',0,11,'active','2026-10-27 00:30:30','2026-10-28 05:09:28'),
(66,'Gold Prices Drop Rs 500 While Silver Declines By Rs 2,400 Per Kilogram','Precious metal prices retreated on the MCX today as market participants prepare for the upcoming Federal Reserve policy meeting and inflation data.','Gold price, Silver price, MCX, Federal Reserve, bullion market, commodity trading, precious metals','<p>Gold prices decreased by Rs 500 per 10 grams while silver prices fell by Rs 2,400 per kilogram on the Multi Commodity Exchange, or MCX, as traders monitor the United States Federal Reserve meeting scheduled for this Wednesday. The MCX is an electronic platform where various commodities are traded. The decline in these precious metals follows a period where a stronger US dollar has exerted downward pressure on bullion valuations.</p>\n<p>Market participants are currently focused on the upcoming policy decision from the Federal Reserve along with the release of US PCE inflation data. This inflation data measures the change in prices paid by consumers for goods and services. The anticipation surrounding these economic indicators has influenced trading sentiment, leading to the observed price adjustments in the domestic bullion market.</p>\n<p>The movement in gold and silver prices reflects broader shifts in the financial landscape as investors adjust their positions ahead of major central bank announcements. When the US dollar strengthens, it often makes dollar-denominated assets like gold more expensive for holders of other currencies, which can lead to reduced demand. Traders are carefully observing these developments to gauge the impact on market trends.</p>\n<p>What it means for investors: The current price volatility highlights the influence of international monetary policy on local commodity markets. Investors monitor central bank interest rate decisions because they affect the cost of borrowing and the attractiveness of assets. Watching these indicators helps in understanding the factors that drive price fluctuations in the bullion sector during periods of uncertainty.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261027-080722-GjmiHK.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Economic Times','https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/commodities/news/gold-prices-dip-rs-500/10-grams-silver-falls-rs-2400/kg-as-traders-eye-us-fed-meet-this-week-what-should-you-do/articleshow/135224447.cms','2026-10-27 06:05:36','2026-10-27 06:05:36',0,9,'active','2026-10-27 06:05:36','2026-10-27 23:17:20'),
(67,'Anup Bagchi Appointed as the New Managing Director and CEO of HDFC Bank','Anup Bagchi has officially assumed the role of managing director and CEO at HDFC Bank, taking over the position from predecessor Sashidhar Jagdishan.','HDFC Bank, Anup Bagchi, Sashidhar Jagdishan, banking sector, CEO appointment, Indian stock market, HDFC Bank news, Nifty Bank','<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">On Tuesday, HDFC Bank officially announced that Anup Bagchi has taken charge as the organization’s managing director and chief executive. He succeeds Sashidhar Jagdishan, who previously held these leadership responsibilities at the private sector lender. The transition marks a change in the top management structure for the institution, as the new appointee steps into the primary executive role to oversee the bank’s operations.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A managing director and CEO is responsible for the overall strategic direction, governance, and daily management of a company’s business activities. This appointment follows the formal completion of the leadership change process within the bank. The bank communicated this update regarding its executive transition through an official statement released on Tuesday to inform stakeholders and the public about the change in leadership.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The handover from Sashidhar Jagdishan to Anup Bagchi is now complete, with the new executive assuming all duties associated with the dual titles. The bank, which operates as a major private sector lender in the country, has finalized this internal transition to ensure continuity in its corporate leadership. No further details regarding the specific terms of the appointment or additional management shifts were mentioned in the official announcement provided by the institution on the day the change took effect.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">What it means for investors: Leadership changes in large-cap entities are closely watched as they can influence corporate strategy and long-term operational focus. Market participants often monitor executive transitions to observe how new management navigates the bank&#039;s existing resistance level or support trends.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261028-013020-msUx7F.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Business Standard','https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/anup-bagchi-takes-charge-as-hdfc-bank-ceo-and-md-succeeds-jagdishan-126102700313_1.html','2026-10-28 01:30:20','2026-10-28 01:30:20',0,7,'active','2026-10-28 01:30:20','2026-10-28 04:57:27'),
(68,'Tata Motors Bid to Takeover Iveco Clears 80% Acceptance Threshold','Tata Motors has secured 89.42% of Iveco’s common share capital following a bid that successfully surpassed the 80% acceptance threshold set by the firm.','Tata Motors, Iveco, takeover, acquisition, common share capital, global automotive, stock market, investment news','<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Tata Motors has announced that its bid to acquire Iveco has successfully cleared the 80% acceptance threshold. According to provisional results released by both companies, Tata Motors now holds 89.42% of the common share capital of Iveco. This development follows a formal process where the company invited existing shareholders to tender their holdings.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A takeover bid is a corporate action where one entity makes an offer to purchase the shares of another company to gain control of its operations. The process involves meeting specific regulatory requirements and securing a minimum level of support from the target company&#039;s investors to finalize the acquisition of the business entity.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The confirmation of the 89.42% stake marks a significant update regarding the ownership structure of Iveco. Both Tata Motors and Iveco issued statements confirming these figures after verifying the provisional results of the offer. The transition of share ownership is expected to proceed based on these verified totals as the companies move toward completing the remaining administrative requirements of the deal.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">What it means for investors: The finalization of this acquisition represents a change in the equity structure for Iveco shareholders. Investors should monitor official regulatory filings for any updates regarding the delisting process or future changes to the capital structure. Any shift in ownership can influence market sentiment and the resistance level of the stock price for the involved entities during the transition period.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261028-020034-GhMgwa.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Business Standard','https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/tata-motors-bid-to-takeover-iveco-clears-80-acceptance-threshold-126102601676_1.html','2026-10-28 02:00:34','2026-10-28 02:00:34',0,7,'active','2026-10-28 02:00:34','2026-10-28 05:09:27'),
(69,'Crude Oil Prices Rise Following Houthi Attack On Saudi Refinery','Brent and WTI crude oil futures increased following a Houthi attack on a Saudi refinery, while MCX crude oil futures also saw gains in early trade.','crude oil, Brent futures, WTI crude, MCX, oil prices, Saudi refinery, energy sector','<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">International oil prices witnessed an upward movement following a Houthi attack on a Saudi refinery. Brent futures climbed to $115.53 a barrel, while WTI crude rose to $101.31 a barrel. Simultaneously, MCX crude oil futures recorded gains of up to 1.70% during the early trading session. Futures are financial contracts that obligate the buyer to purchase an asset at a predetermined future date and price.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The global energy market reacted promptly to the geopolitical tension involving the refinery infrastructure. Market participants monitored the supply chain implications after the incident was reported. These price fluctuations reflect the immediate impact of regional conflicts on global commodity benchmarks. Commodity benchmarks are standard reference points used to price various goods and raw materials in the global market.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Investors in the Indian market often observe these developments closely as they impact domestic fuel costs and inflation expectations. The movement in MCX futures provides a local perspective on how international supply shocks influence domestic trading platforms. These platforms allow traders to hedge against volatility in energy prices by locking in current rates for future delivery.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">What it means for investors: Fluctuations in global crude oil prices can influence the profitability of oil marketing companies and the broader manufacturing sector. Changes in input costs often impact the margins of companies that are heavily dependent on fuel for their operations. Market participants should monitor how these price shifts affect the overall cost of production across different industries.</p>','headline-news/photo-20261028-043559-Uh4ESL.jpg',NULL,NULL,'Hindu BusinessLine','https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/markets/commodities/crude-oil-futures-gain-after-houthi-attack-on-saudi-refinery/article71634280.ece','2026-10-28 04:35:59','2026-10-28 04:35:59',0,1,'active','2026-10-28 04:35:59','2026-10-28 05:09:27');
INSERT INTO `news` VALUES
(7,'Market Outlook : Nifty Support at 22202–22088; Resistance at 22474–22606',NULL,'Investment Point Daily | Monday, October 12, 2026 Friends, The Indian stock market witnessed renewed selling pressure on Monday, October 12, 2026, as benchmark indices failed to sustain their early gains. Despite Friday\'...','<div>\r\n<p><strong>Investment Point Daily | Monday, October 12, 2026</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>Friends,</strong></p>\r\n<p>The Indian stock market witnessed renewed selling pressure on Monday, October 12, 2026, as benchmark indices failed to sustain their early gains. Despite Friday\'s strong recovery, investors remained cautious amid rising crude oil prices, persistent foreign institutional selling, inflation concerns and global economic uncertainty.</p>\r\n<p>The Nifty 50 declined 157.10 points (0.70%) to close at 22,363.35, while the BSE Sensex dropped 547.65 points (0.76%) to settle at 71,924.68.</p>\r\n<p>However, broader market performance remained mixed, with selective buying in small-cap stocks indicating that investor interest has not disappeared entirely.</p>\r\n<h2><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Major Reasons Behind Market Decline :&nbsp;</span></h2>\r\n<p><strong>1. Continued Foreign Institutional Selling</strong></p>\r\n<p>Persistent selling by Foreign Institutional Investors (FIIs) remained a major concern. Foreign capital outflows continued to weigh on market sentiment, particularly in heavyweight stocks, limiting the potential for a sustained recovery.</p>\r\n<p><strong>2. Rising Crude Oil Prices</strong></p>\r\n<p>Brent crude oil traded around $106 per barrel, raising concerns about India\'s import bill, inflation and corporate profitability. Higher energy prices can increase transportation and manufacturing costs, affecting profit margins across several industries.</p>\r\n<p><strong>3. RBI Policy and Inflation Concerns</strong></p>\r\n<p>Investors closely monitored the Reserve Bank of India\'s measures to support the Indian rupee while awaiting domestic inflation data. Uncertainty surrounding inflation and monetary policy contributed to cautious trading.</p>\r\n<p><strong>4. Profit Booking in Heavyweight Stocks</strong></p>\r\n<p>Following Friday\'s recovery, profit booking emerged in banking, IT and other index-heavyweight stocks. Selling pressure prevented benchmark indices from maintaining their initial upward momentum.</p>\r\n<p><strong>5. Quarterly Corporate Earnings</strong></p>\r\n<p>With the quarterly earnings season underway, investors are assessing whether corporate profitability can withstand rising input costs, currency fluctuations and global economic challenges.</p>\r\n<h2><span style=\"color: rgb(22, 145, 121);\">FII&ndash;DII Activity :</span></h2>\r\n<p>Institutional investment flows remain an important factor influencing market direction.</p>\r\n<p>According to the latest available confirmed figures, FIIs recorded net cash-market sales of ₹3,568.90 crore on Friday, <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">October 9</span><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">,</span> while Domestic Institutional Investors (DIIs) registered net purchases of ₹4,743.26 crore.</p>\r\n<p>Domestic institutional buying helped absorb part of the foreign selling pressure. However, continued overseas outflows remain a challenge for large-cap stocks.</p>\r\n<p><em>Note: These figures relate to October 9, not October 12. The final October 12 FII&ndash;DII figures have not been independently verified for this report.</em></p>\r\n<h2><span style=\"color: rgb(22, 145, 121);\">Sector-Wise Performance :</span></h2>\r\n<p>Sectoral performance remained mixed throughout Monday\'s trading session.</p>\r\n<p>The media index gained approximately 4.6%, followed by realty at around 1% and auto at 0.9%. Pharmaceutical stocks also witnessed selective buying.</p>\r\n<p>The Nifty Smallcap 100 index advanced approximately 1.4%, while the midcap segment remained largely unchanged.&nbsp;Conversely, IT, FMCG, metals and banking stocks faced selling pressure. Tech Mahindra, ITC, Larsen &amp; Toubro, Hindalco and Hindustan Unilever were among the weaker performers.&nbsp;Meanwhile, Dr. Reddy\'s Laboratories, Bajaj Auto and Bharat Electronics attracted buying interest.</p>\r\n<p>This divergence indicates a stock-specific market rather than uniform weakness across all sectors.</p>\r\n<h2><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Crude Oil, Rupee and RBI :</span>&nbsp;</h2>\r\n<p>Brent crude prices around $106 per barrel remain a concern for India\'s import-dependent economy.&nbsp;Higher crude prices could increase import expenditure, fuel inflation and pressure corporate margins.&nbsp;Meanwhile, the Indian rupee reportedly appreciated by approximately 1% following RBI measures aimed at managing dollar demand.</p>\r\n<p>Although currency stability may support market sentiment, sustained improvement will depend on crude oil movements, foreign investment flows and broader global conditions.</p>\r\n<h2>Nifty Technical Outlook : Important Support and Resistance Levels</h2>\r\n<p>Technically, Nifty\'s short-term trend remains cautious, with resistance at higher levels.</p>\r\n<p><strong>NIFTY OCT Future : 22,399.90</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong>Support Zone :</strong> </span>22272 / 22202 Points</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong>Further Downside Levels :</strong></span> 22173 / 22088 Points</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 80, 233);\"><strong>Resistance Zone :</strong></span> 22474 / 22533 / 22606 Points</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>A sustained move above 22474 could encourage short covering towards 22533 &ndash; 22606. A further breakout above 22606 may open the possibility of recovery towards 22707.</p>\r\n<p>Conversely, a decisive breakdown below 22272 &ndash; 22202 could increase selling pressure, potentially extending the decline towards 22180 and 22088.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Nifty <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">22202 is a crucial support level</span>, while <span style=\"color: rgb(38, 80, 233);\">22474 remains the immediate recovery hurdle.</span></strong></p>\r\n<p>The next trading session will be influenced by global market cues, crude oil prices, rupee movements, institutional flows, inflation data and quarterly earnings announcements.</p>\r\n<p>Traders should avoid aggressive positions without price and volume confirmation.</p>\r\n<h2><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 80, 233);\">Investment Point\'s View</span> :</h2>\r\n<p>The Indian equity market is experiencing heightened volatility, making disciplined risk management particularly important. Short-term traders should follow predefined stop-loss levels, avoid excessive leverage and monitor important technical zones.</p>\r\n<p>Long-term investors should focus on fundamentally strong companies, reasonable valuations, earnings growth and financial stability rather than reacting to short-term fluctuations.</p>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong>Conclusion :</strong></span> The near-term market outlook remains cautious. A sustained recovery above 22474&ndash;22606 could improve sentiment, while a breakdown below 22202 may increase downside risks. Institutional flows, crude oil prices and corporate earnings will remain key market drivers.</p>\r\n<span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong>Disclaimer :</strong> </span></div>\r\n<div>This article is published solely for educational, informational and investor-awareness purposes. It does not constitute investment advice or a recommendation to buy or sell securities. Stock market investments are subject to market risks. Technical levels are indicative and may change with market conditions.</div>\r\n<p>Editorial note : This article is based on the market figures and institutional data supplied in avaible data, Those figures, including the crude oil price and technical levels, have not been independently verified in this. Please confirm them against NSE/BSE and other reliable market sources before investing.</p>','news/cEgLWjksa7SWNQNjmKjCnVUQ4BznwmU9zXIYyv7T.jpg','active',0,79,'2026-10-12 14:03:17','2026-10-28 03:20:35'),
(8,'Nifty Derivative Market Trend Analysis: Expert Insights for Traders',NULL,'1. Technical Analysis : The Nifty 50 October Derivative index displays a volatile yet resilient structure near key moving average boundaries, trading around the 22686 Levels. Downside Support : A breakdown below the imme...','<div dir=\"auto\"><strong>1. Technical Analysis :&nbsp;</strong></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The Nifty 50 October Derivative index displays a volatile yet resilient structure near key moving average boundaries, trading around the 22686 Levels.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;<strong>Downside Support :</strong></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">A breakdown below the immediate support zone of 22676 &ndash; 22606 could invite sharp selling pressure, opening lower tracks toward the psychological 22474 psychological floor.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><strong>&nbsp;Upside Resistance :</strong></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">A sustained breakout and consolidation above the 22676 &ndash; 22808 resistance band will validate improving upward momentum, setting up a path toward the 22880 &ndash; 22909.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><strong>2. Fundamental &amp; Market Behavior :-</strong></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><strong>Volatility &amp; Sentiment :</strong></span></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Market participants remain cautious amid global macroeconomic cues and domestic corporate earnings expectations. Intraday price swings reflect a tug-of-war between value buyers defending support zones and overhead supply capping aggressive rallies.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><strong>Derivatives Overview :</strong></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Open Interest (OI) data on weekly and monthly contracts indicates heavy call writing at the 22600 and 22700 strikes, while considerable put base positioning is active around the 22000 to 22200 strikes, defining the active boundaries for the current settlement cycle.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img class=\"an1\" draggable=\"false\" src=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/e/notoemoji/17.0/1f449_1f3fd/32.png\" alt=\"👉🏽\" loading=\"lazy\" data-emoji=\"👉🏽\" aria-label=\"👉🏽\"> <strong>Foreign Institutional Investors (FIIs) :</strong></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">FIIs continue to exhibit a cautious stance, registering net selling in cash equities and selective short indexing in derivatives to hedge portfolio risks against global headwinds.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img class=\"an1\" draggable=\"false\" src=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/e/notoemoji/17.0/1f449_1f3fd/32.png\" alt=\"👉🏽\" loading=\"lazy\" data-emoji=\"👉🏽\" aria-label=\"👉🏽\"> <strong>Domestic Institutional Investors (DIIs):</strong></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">DIIs remain prominent market stabilizers, consistently absorbing selling pressure through steady systemic inflows and counter-cyclical buying support.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img class=\"an1\" draggable=\"false\" src=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/e/notoemoji/17.0/1f3db_fe0f/32.png\" alt=\"🏛️\" loading=\"lazy\" data-emoji=\"🏛️\" aria-label=\"🏛️\"> <strong>SEBI Compliance &amp; Disclaimer :-</strong></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">This content is published strictly for educational and informational purposes only and does not constitute financial, legal, tax, or investment advice, nor does it represent a specific Buy / Sell recommendation for any derivative contract or equity security.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The publisher and authors disclaim any liability for financial losses arising from the utilization of these technical levels.</div>','news/TduKCLwdyAiyBbNG98m8QxCqBkbyJwvYs74Rgepu.jpg','active',0,144,'2026-10-14 07:31:29','2026-10-26 09:43:40'),
(9,'Nifty Derivative Market Trend Analysis: Expert Insights for Traders',NULL,'1. Technical Analysis : The Nifty 50 October Derivative index displays a volatile yet resilient structure near key moving average boundaries, trading around the 22993 Levels. Downside Support : A breakdown below the imme...','<p><span style=\"color: rgb(35, 111, 161);\"><strong>1. Technical Analysis : </strong></span></p>\r\n<p>The Nifty 50 October Derivative index displays a volatile yet resilient structure near key moving average boundaries, trading around the 22993 Levels.</p>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><strong>&nbsp;Downside Support :</strong></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">A breakdown below the immediate support zone of 22880 &ndash; 22808 could invite sharp selling pressure, opening lower tracks toward the psychological 22737 psychological floor.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><strong>&nbsp;Upside Resistance :</strong></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">A sustained breakout and consolidation above the 23008 &ndash; 23088 resistance band will validate improving upward momentum, setting up a path toward the 23108 &ndash; 23188.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"color: rgb(35, 111, 161);\"><strong>2. Fundamental &amp; Market Behavior :-</strong></span></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><strong>&nbsp;Volatility &amp; Sentiment :</strong></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Market participants remain cautious amid global macroeconomic cues and domestic corporate earnings expectations. Intraday price swings reflect a tug-of-war between value buyers defending support zones and overhead supply capping aggressive rallies.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><strong>Derivatives Overview :</strong></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Open Interest (OI) data on weekly and monthly contracts indicates heavy call writing at the 22600 and 22500 strikes, while considerable put base positioning is active around the 22400 to 22300 strikes, defining the active boundaries for the current settlement cycle.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><strong>Foreign Institutional Investors (FIIs) :</strong></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">FIIs continue to exhibit a cautious stance, registering net selling in cash equities and selective short indexing in derivatives to hedge portfolio risks against global headwinds.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><strong>Domestic Institutional Investors (DIIs) :</strong></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">DIIs remain prominent market stabilizers, consistently absorbing selling pressure through steady systemic inflows and counter-cyclical buying support.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><strong>Note :- The publisher and authors disclaim any liability for financial Profits &amp; losses arising from the utilization of these technical levels.</strong></div>','news/RkWoxol9cv7clBYUJuqT1hHSvLa0juN8qhEFkj9d.jpg','active',0,48,'2026-10-15 14:25:39','2026-10-26 09:43:40'),
(10,'Nifty Derivative Market Trend Analysis : Nifty Opens With Mild Gains Amidst Mixed Global Market Cues','nifty','Indian equity markets displayed a cautious start as the Nifty 50 opened at 22742.2, marking a gap up of 54.55 points. The index traded at 22719.45, reflecting a gain of 31.8 points or 0.14 percent from the previous close...','<p>Indian equity markets displayed a cautious start as the Nifty 50 opened at 22742.2, marking a gap up of 54.55 points. The index traded at 22719.45, reflecting a gain of 31.8 points or 0.14 percent from the previous close of 22687.65. The Sensex followed this trend, rising 354.22 points or 0.48 percent to 73603.61. Conversely, the Bank Nifty faced selling pressure, trading lower by 0.31 percent at 54756.3 during the early session.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Market Behaviour &amp; Activity :</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>A. Global Market Influence :</strong> Global markets presented a fragmented picture as the latest session concluded. In the United States, the S&amp;P 500 declined 0.64 percent and the Nasdaq fell 1.57 percent, while the Dow Jones rose 0.71 percent. European markets saw mixed results with the FTSE 100 down 0.07 percent and DAX up 0.27 percent. Meanwhile, Asian markets showed divergence with the Nikkei down 1.11 percent.</p>\r\n<p><strong>B. FIIs Activity :</strong>Foreign Institutional Investors remained net sellers in the cash market, offloading shares worth 3459 crore Such persistent selling by overseas participants may impact market liquidity and exert downward pressure on index heavyweights as investors monitor global flows and institutional participation throughout the trading session today.</p>\r\n<p><strong>C. DIIs Activity :</strong>Domestic Institutional Investors acted as a counterweight to foreign outflows by net buying shares worth 2891 crore This consistent deployment of capital by domestic funds may provide a necessary cushioning effect to the broader market, helping to stabilize sentiment amidst the prevailing selling activity from foreign investors.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Macroeconomic, Energy &amp; Currency Drivers :</strong> Macroeconomic factors remain a focal point as Brent crude prices climbed to 113.17 US dollars per barrel, a rise of 4.00 percent. Simultaneously, the US Dollar Index stood at 101.61, down 0.12 percent. The Rupee weakened against the US dollar to 94.79, reflecting a 0.51 percent decline. These developments in energy and currency markets may influence domestic inflation expectations and general sentiment regarding global monetary policy directions.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Sector Wise Performance :</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>Top Gainers</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>IT :</strong>The sector led the market with a gain of 1.69 percent, showing resilience compared to other segments during the morning trade session.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>Top Losers</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>Metal :</strong> The sector emerged as one of the weakest performers, recording a decline of 1.43 percent</li>\r\n<li><strong>Energy :</strong> This sector faced significant selling pressure, dropping 1.38 percent as market participants reacted to rising crude oil prices during the morning session.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>Market Sentiment &amp; Technical Analysis :</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>Market Breadth &amp; Volatility :</strong> The market breadth on the NSE remains tilted toward the bears, with 19 advances against 31 declines. Meanwhile, the India VIX has climbed 4.11 percent to 16.41. This rise in volatility suggests that participants are bracing for potential price swings as the market navigates the current trading environment.</p>\r\n<p><strong>A. Downside Levels :</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Support levels at 22680 and 22570</li>\r\n<li>All key moving averages are overhead</li>\r\n<li>The low of 22699.7 serves as an immediate reference point.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>B. Upside Levels :</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Resistance levels at 22800 and 22910</li>\r\n<li>20-day 22751.09, 50-day 23439.28, and 200-day 24141.59 moving averages</li>\r\n<li>The high of 22787.25 acts as a near-term hurdle.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>Session Outlook &amp; Key Triggers :</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Investors are monitoring the Jio Platforms IPO which saw strong demand on day two</li>\r\n<li>Market participants are evaluating the latest quarterly results from Colgate-Palmolive, Adani Total Gas, and Swiggy for sectoral impact.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The market continues to exhibit a cautious stance as the Nifty 50 struggles to surpass its short-term moving average. While domestic buying provides some support, the combination of rising crude prices and negative sector breadth suggests a period of consolidation. Investors may continue to watch for further institutional flows and corporate result updates throughout the day.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Recommendation :</strong> Neutral Editorial Assessment &ndash; No Buy / Sell Recommendation.</p>','news/r5awuQEZvRlA8vUtewijvJO99QQiKsLKNKx4NYGz.jpg','active',0,219,'2026-10-23 04:00:50','2026-10-26 13:59:45'),
(11,'Nifty Derivative Market Trend Analysis : Indian Equity Markets Face Selling Pressure Amid Broad Market Decline','nifty','The domestic equity market witnessed a downward trend today as the Nifty 50 closed at 22600, recording a decline of 87.65 points or 0.39 percent. The index opened at 22742.2 and touched a high of 22787.25 before falling...','<p>The domestic equity market witnessed a downward trend today as the Nifty 50 closed at 22600, recording a decline of 87.65 points or 0.39 percent. The index opened at 22742.2 and touched a high of 22787.25 before falling to a low of 22372. Similarly, the Sensex settled at 73123.83, down by 125.56 points or 0.17 percent. The Bank Nifty also faced significant selling pressure, ending the session at 54287.35 with a loss of 1.16 percent as investors reacted to prevailing market conditions.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Market Behaviour &amp; Activity :</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>A. Global Market Influence :</strong> Global sentiment remained cautious as international indices showed mixed results. The S&amp;P 500 fell 1.21 percent and the Nasdaq declined 2.60 percent, while the Dow Jones rose 0.02 percent. European markets were largely negative with the FTSE 100 down 0.48 percent, the DAX down 0.74 percent, and the CAC 40 down 0.62 percent. Asian markets showed mixed trends, with Nikkei falling 0.34 percent and Hang Seng rising 0.69 percent.</p>\r\n<p><strong>B. FIIs Activity :</strong> Foreign Institutional Investors were net sellers in the cash market today, offloading shares worth 3459 crore. Such sustained selling activity by foreign participants often impacts market liquidity and creates downward pressure on major indices, reflecting a cautious stance from global investors regarding current valuations in the domestic market.</p>\r\n<p><strong>C. DIIs Activity :</strong> Domestic Institutional Investors provided some support to the market by net buying shares worth 2891 crore. This consistent deployment of capital by local institutions acts as a potential cushion against the selling pressure exerted by foreign entities, helping to mitigate the overall volatility experienced during the trading session today.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Macroeconomic, Energy &amp; Currency Drivers :</strong> Macroeconomic indicators showed a mixed impact on market sentiment. Brent crude prices declined by 2.76 percent to 110.05 per barrel, which may influence energy-related costs. The US Dollar Index rose to 101.8, reflecting a 0.18 percent increase. Meanwhile, the Rupee weakened against the US dollar to 94.94, marking a 0.67 percent change. Investors generally monitor these fluctuations in currency and energy markets as they influence domestic inflation dynamics and the broader economic outlook for the country.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Sector Wise Performance :</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>Top Gainers</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>IT :</strong> The sector performed relatively better compared to others, ending the session with a minor decline of 0.27 percent despite recent corporate earnings announcements.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Auto :</strong> This segment recorded a decline of 0.60 percent, showing resilience compared to the broader market sell-off observed across most other major sectoral indices during the day.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>Top Losers</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>Metal :</strong> This sector emerged as the weakest performer, shedding 2.71 percent as selling pressure intensified across the index components during the session.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Realty :</strong> The index followed closely behind, recording a decline of 2.38 percent as investors reduced exposure to real estate stocks amidst the prevailing negative market sentiment.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>Market Sentiment &amp; Technical Analysis :</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>Market Breadth &amp; Volatility :</strong> Market breadth remained significantly negative with 14 advances and 36 declines among Nifty 50 stocks. The India VIX rose by 6.98 percent to 16.86, indicating an increase in market volatility and a heightened sense of caution among participants as they navigate the current phase of price adjustments.</p>\r\n<p><strong>A. Downside Levels :</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Support levels at 22590 and 22390</li>\r\n<li>All key moving averages including the 20-day at 22713.45, 50-day at 23403.72, and 200-day at 24125.36 are overhead resistance levels.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>B. Upside Levels :</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Resistance levels at 22800 and 23000</li>\r\n<li>Overhead resistance from 20-day moving average at 22713.45, 50-day at 23403.72, and 200-day at 24125.36.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>Next Session Outlook &amp; Key Triggers :</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Ongoing corporate results including Infosys, HPCL, Colgate-Palmolive, and Adani Total Gas</li>\r\n<li>Subscription updates for Jio Platforms and Paras Healthcare IPOs</li>\r\n<li>Swiggy financial performance reports.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The market remains in a consolidation phase with overhead resistance from multiple moving averages. While domestic institutional support persists, the negative breadth and rising volatility suggest that investors may continue to monitor global cues and upcoming corporate results. The market could witness further range-bound activity as participants assess the impact of recent earnings and macroeconomic developments.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Recommendation :</strong> Neutral Editorial Assessment &ndash; No Buy / Sell Fully Recommendation.</p>','news/M070qeBf8YWPwZnE4UghetIqDEhtk4JZv5EfMo5P.jpg','active',0,137,'2026-10-23 11:30:30','2026-10-27 08:18:46'),
(12,'Nifty Derivative Market Trend Analysis : Nifty Remains Subdued As Markets Navigate Mixed Corporate Results Performance','nifty','The Indian equity markets are trading with a cautious tone during the morning session. The Nifty 50 is currently at 22592.6, reflecting a mainor decline of 7.4 points or 0.03 percent from the previous close of 22600. The...','<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Indian equity markets are trading with a cautious tone during the morning session. The Nifty 50 is currently at 22592.6, reflecting a mainor decline of 7.4 points or 0.03 percent from the previous close of 22600. The index opened at 22524.4, marking a gap down of 75.6 points. Meanwhile, the Sensex is trading at 73217.22, up by 93.39 points or 0.13 percent. Conversely, the Bank Nifty is under pressure, currently trading at 54020.45, down by 0.49 percent.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Market Behaviour &amp; Activity :</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>A. Global Market Influence :</strong> Global sentiment remains largely negative as major indices struggle. The S&amp;P 500, Nasdaq, and Dow Jones saw declines of 0.52 percent, 0.21 percent, and 1.23 percent respectively. European markets including the FTSE 100, DAX, and CAC 40 also traded lower. In Asia, the Nikkei declined by 0.18 percent, while the Hang Seng bucked the trend by rising 0.65 percent.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>B. FIIs Activity :</strong> Foreign Institutional Investors were net buyers in the cash market, deploying 888 crore. Such consistent participation from overseas participants generally provides a layer of liquidity to the Indian markets, though investors often monitor these flows closely to gauge the broader appetite for emerging market equities.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>C. DIIs Activity :</strong> Domestic Institutional Investors provided significant support to the market by net buying 3235 crore. This substantial deployment of capital by domestic entities often acts as a crucial cushion against selling pressure, helping to stabilize indices during periods of volatility or when global cues appear unfavorable.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Macroeconomic, Energy &amp; Currency Drivers :</strong> Macroeconomic variables show mixed signals today. Brent crude is trading at 109.92 per barrel, down 5.83 percent, which may influence input costs. The US Dollar Index stands at 101.67, a decline of 0.14 percent. Meanwhile, the Rupee has weakened against the US dollar at 95.13, a change of 0.44 percent. Investors may continue to monitor these developments alongside potential global policy shifts and inflationary trends that could impact domestic market stability.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Sector Wise Performance :</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Top Gainers</strong></p>\r\n<ul style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong>Metal :</strong> This sector is the leader today with a gain of 0.82 percent, reflecting positive momentum in the commodities space during the morning trade.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Energy :</strong> The sector has moved up by 0.67 percent, showing resilience amid broader market fluctuations as investors assess the latest energy market developments.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Top Losers</strong></p>\r\n<ul style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong>PSU Bank :</strong> This sector is currently the weakest, down by 0.78 percent, as market participants react to sector-specific pressure and ongoing corporate result updates.</li>\r\n<li><strong>FMCG :</strong> The sector has declined by 0.69 percent, indicating a cautious approach from investors toward defensive stocks during the current session of trade.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Market Sentiment &amp; Technical Analysis :</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Market Breadth &amp; Volatility :</strong> The market breadth is currently negative with 23 advances against 27 declines. The India VIX has climbed to 17.78, representing an increase of 5.44 percent. This rise in volatility suggests that participants are bracing for potential swings as the market processes various corporate results and global cues.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>A. Downside Levels :</strong></p>\r\n<ul style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li>Support levels at 22590 and 22390</li>\r\n<li>All key moving averages are overhead</li>\r\n<li>Breakdown zone near 22387.35</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>B. Upside Levels :</strong></p>\r\n<ul style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li>Resistance levels at 22800 and 23000</li>\r\n<li>20-day 22689.86, 50-day 23366.83, and 200-day 24107.67</li>\r\n<li>Breakout zone near 22706.15</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Session Outlook &amp; Key Triggers :</strong></p>\r\n<ul style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li>Ongoing corporate results for Paytm, Tata Consumer, Mankind Pharma, REC, IOB, Ather Energy, Aegis Logistics, Supreme Ind, ITC Hotels, and Sumitomo Chemical</li>\r\n<li>Market focus on the Jio Platforms IPO allotment and the EAAA India Alternatives IPO launch</li>\r\n<li>Monitoring of global policy decisions and crude oil price movements.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The market is currently exhibiting a consolidation phase as it balances the impact of various corporate earnings against global volatility. While domestic institutional support remains a positive factor, the rise in volatility suggests a cautious environment for the remainder of the session. Investors may continue to observe sector-specific movements and global cues.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Recommendation :</strong> Neutral Editorial Assessment &ndash; No Buy / Sell Fully Recommendation.</p>','news/a6Um1Ru4RwD6Jlz0bdXFO9L8L4XcniDL9o1VMIgm.jpg','active',0,45,'2026-10-26 05:41:20','2026-10-27 02:44:12'),
(13,'Nifty Derivative Market Trend Analysis : Indian Markets Trade Higher Amidst Volatile Corporate Earnings Season','nifty','The Indian equity markets are showing resilience during the afternoon session as the Nifty 50 trades at 22649.25, marking a gain of 49.25 points or 0.22 percent from the previous close of 22600. After opening at 22524.4,...','<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Indian equity markets are showing resilience during the afternoon session as the Nifty 50 trades at 22649.25, marking a gain of 49.25 points or 0.22 percent from the previous close of 22600. After opening at 22524.4, the index fluctuated between a low of 22387.35 and a high of 22706.15. Meanwhile, the Sensex is up by 222.81 points or 0.30 percent to reach 73346.64. Conversely, the Bank Nifty remains under pressure, trading lower by 0.31 percent at 54119.5 today.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Market Behaviour &amp; Activity :</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>A. Global Market Influence :</strong> Global markets present a mixed picture today. In the United States, the S&amp;P 500 declined 0.52 percent, the Nasdaq fell 0.21 percent, and the Dow Jones dropped 1.23 percent. European indices show positive momentum, with the FTSE 100 up 0.44 percent, the DAX up 0.57 percent, and the CAC 40 rising 0.68 percent. Asian markets saw Japan Nikkei fall 0.80 percent while Hong Kong Hang Seng gained 0.51 percent.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>B. FIIs Activity :</strong> Foreign Institutional Investors were net buyers in the cash market, purchasing shares worth 888 crore. Such inflows generally provide necessary liquidity to the equity markets and help sustain broader sentiment, though investors continue to monitor these flows closely alongside global developments and ongoing corporate results for further directional clarity.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>C. DIIs Activity :</strong> Domestic Institutional Investors net bought 3235 crore in the cash market. This significant deployment of capital by domestic entities continues to act as a vital cushion for the markets, helping to absorb selling pressure and providing stability even when global cues remain uncertain or when specific sectors face volatility.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Macroeconomic, Energy &amp; Currency Drivers :</strong> Macroeconomic indicators show Brent crude trading at 110.12, reflecting a decline of 5.65 percent. The US Dollar Index stands at 101.78, down 0.03 percent. Meanwhile, the Rupee weakened against the US dollar, trading at 95.25, which is a change of 0.56 percent. These factors, alongside general global developments regarding inflation and central bank policies, may influence investor sentiment and the broader market trajectory as participants assess the impact of currency fluctuations on domestic corporate earnings.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Sector Wise Performance :</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Top Gainers</strong></p>\r\n<ul style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong>Pharma :</strong> The sector leads with a gain of 1.58 percent, reflecting positive sentiment in healthcare stocks</li>\r\n<li><strong>Metal :</strong> This sector follows with a rise of 1.35 percent, showing renewed interest from market participants during the afternoon session.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Top Losers</strong></p>\r\n<ul style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong>Banking :</strong> The sector is the weakest, declining 0.31 percent amid volatility in financial stocks</li>\r\n<li><strong>FMCG :</strong> This sector is down 0.30 percent, reflecting cautious sentiment among investors regarding consumer goods companies.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Market Sentiment &amp; Technical Analysis :</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Market Breadth &amp; Volatility :</strong> The market breadth remains positive with 28 advances against 22 declines. Simultaneously, the India VIX has risen by 3.31 percent to 17.42. This combination suggests that while the broader market is holding gains, the increase in volatility indicates that participants are closely monitoring risks as the session progresses toward the close.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>A. Downside Levels :</strong></p>\r\n<ul style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li>Support levels at 22590 and 22390</li>\r\n<li>All key moving averages are overhead</li>\r\n<li>Breakdown zone at 22390</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>B. Upside Levels :</strong></p>\r\n<ul style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li>Resistance levels at 22800 and 23000</li>\r\n<li>20-day moving average at 22692.79, 50-day moving average at 23368, and 200-day moving average at 24107.96</li>\r\n<li>Breakout zone at 22800</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Session Outlook &amp; Key Triggers :</strong></p>\r\n<ul style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li>Ongoing Q2 results for companies including Paytm, Tata Consumer, Mankind Pharma, REC, IOB, Ather Energy, Aegis Logistics, Supreme Ind, ITC Hotels, and Sumitomo Chemical</li>\r\n<li>Market participants are also tracking the US Fed decision and crude oil price movements for the remainder of the session.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The market remains in a state of consolidation as investors weigh the impact of mixed corporate earnings against global cues. With the index trading near its moving averages, the session may continue to see volatility. Market participants may remain cautious, focusing on sector-specific updates and institutional flows to gauge the momentum for the next session.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Recommendation :</strong> Neutral Editorial Assessment &ndash; No Buy / Sell Fully Recommendation.</p>','news/w8Q3SqhUs2h0r2Lvy9SYEONdugvKljQrI4UMJOjU.jpg','active',0,48,'2026-10-26 08:33:16','2026-10-28 04:05:18'),
(14,'Nifty Derivative Market Trend Analysis : Indian Markets Close Higher As Investors Monitor Corporate Earnings Results','nifty','The Indian equity markets experienced a positive session today as the Nifty 50 concluded at 22775 marking a gain of 153.2 points or 0.68 percent. The index opened at 22524.4 and touched a high of 22753.2 during the day....','<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Indian equity markets experienced a positive session today as the Nifty 50 concluded at 22775 marking a gain of 153.2 points or 0.68 percent. The index opened at 22524.4 and touched a high of 22753.2 during the day. Similarly, the Sensex ascended by 482.92 points or 0.66 percent to settle at 73606.75. Meanwhile, the Bank Nifty reflected a more subdued performance, ending the day at 54366.7, which represents a marginal rise of 0.15 percent.</p>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(35, 111, 161);\"><strong>Market Behaviour &amp; Activity :</strong></span></h2>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>A. Global Market Influence :</strong> Global markets presented a mixed picture today. In the United States, the S&amp;P 500 declined 0.52 percent, the Nasdaq fell 0.21 percent, and the Dow Jones dropped 1.23 percent. European indices showed strength, with the FTSE 100 up 0.42 percent, the DAX rising 0.76 percent, and the CAC 40 gaining 0.59 percent. Asian markets saw the Nikkei fall 0.80 percent while the Hang Seng rose 0.51 percent.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>B. FIIs Activity :</strong> Foreign Institutional Investors were net buyers in the cash market, deploying 888 crore during the latest session. Such inflows generally provide a degree of liquidity and support to the broader market sentiment, signaling that international participants are maintaining an active interest in the domestic equity space despite prevailing global volatility.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>C. DIIs Activity :</strong> Domestic Institutional Investors continued to act as a significant support pillar for the market, net buying 3235 crore in the latest session. This consistent deployment of capital by local institutions often serves to cushion the indices against sudden selling pressure, reflecting a stable outlook from domestic market participants regarding the current economic landscape.</p>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(35, 111, 161);\"><strong>Macroeconomic, Energy &amp; Currency Drivers :</strong></span></h2>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The macroeconomic environment remains a focal point for investors. Brent crude prices stood at 109.83 per barrel, reflecting a decline of 5.90 percent. The US Dollar Index was at 101.88, up 0.06 percent, while the Rupee weakened against the US dollar to 95.21, a change of 0.53 percent. These factors, alongside general global developments regarding inflation and central bank policies, may influence market sentiment in the coming sessions.</p>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(35, 111, 161);\"><strong>Sector Wise Performance :</strong></span></h2>\r\n<h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(22, 145, 121);\"><strong>Top Gainers</strong></span></h4>\r\n<ul style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong>Metal :</strong> This sector led the gains with a rise of 2.21 percent, reflecting positive momentum among industrial commodities.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Pharma :</strong> The sector advanced 1.76 percent, showing resilience amid ongoing corporate results and sector-specific developments.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\"><strong>Top Losers</strong></span></h4>\r\n<ul style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong>Banking :</strong> This sector was among the weakest performers, recording a marginal rise of 0.15 percent as investors assessed recent quarterly earnings reports.</li>\r\n<li><strong>FMCG :</strong> The sector ended with a modest gain of 0.28 percent, indicating a period of consolidation for consumer-focused companies during the current trading session.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(35, 111, 161);\"><strong>Market Sentiment &amp; Technical Analysis :</strong></span></h2>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The overall market stance remains cautiously positive, contingent on the index sustaining above immediate key hurdles. In the short term, a decisive and sustained trade above the crucial 22,808 level could open the doorway for a quick upward move toward the 22,880 mark. However, traders are advised to align their positions strictly with the prevailing trend and maintain rigorous risk control, as systematic profit-booking on intraday rallies remains an integral part of sustainable investing.​</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Key Resistance &amp; Support Framework<br>From a technical standpoint, Derivative Nifty Futures are likely to encounter initial overhead resistance within the <span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">22,808</span> to <span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">22,880</span> zone. If buying momentum pushes the index above this barrier, the secondary resistance range is projected between <span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">22,909</span> and <span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">22,979</span>, an area where heightened caution is recommended due to potential supply pressures.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">On the downside, anticipated profit-booking on upward moves may establish an initial support zone between 22,676 and 22,606. Should the derivative market experience a deeper pullback, the next crucial demand range is expected to emerge between 22,570 and 22,505.</p>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(35, 111, 161);\"><strong>Next Session Outlook &amp; Key Triggers :</strong></span></h2>\r\n<ul style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li>Monitoring upcoming corporate results for companies like Paytm, Tata Consumer, Mankind Pharma, REC, IOB, Ather Energy, Aegis Logistics, Supreme Ind, ITC Hotels, and Sumitomo Chemical</li>\r\n<li>Evaluating the impact of the US Fed decision and fluctuations in crude oil prices on overall market stability.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The market maintains a cautious yet positive stance as it navigates through a busy period of corporate earnings. While the Nifty 50 shows resilience, investors may continue to watch global cues and institutional flows. A balanced approach remains prudent as the index approaches key resistance levels while supported by its moving averages in the next session.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Recommendation : Neutral Editorial Assessment &ndash; No Buy / Sell Fully Recommendation.</span></p>','news/bK0lYq9JJrs6GfPOpBggThrQFEqpXS5S7paQ2iuw.jpg','active',0,67,'2026-10-26 11:30:26','2026-10-27 20:28:35'),
(15,'Nifty Derivative Market Trend Analysis : Nifty Remains Flat Amidst Mixed Corporate Results And Global Cues','nifty','The Indian equity market exhibits a cautious tone during the morning session as the Nifty 50 trades at 22746, reflecting a marginal decline of 7.2 points or 0.03 percent from the previous close of 22753.2. The index open...','<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Indian equity market exhibits a cautious tone during the morning session as the Nifty 50 trades at 22746, reflecting a marginal decline of 7.2 points or 0.03 percent from the previous close of 22753.2. The index opened at 22708.8, marking a gap down of 44.4 points. Meanwhile, the Sensex is positioned at 73601.25, down 5.5 points or 0.01 percent. The Bank Nifty also remains largely unchanged, trading at 54363.2, showing a minor dip of 0.01 percent in early trade.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Market Behaviour &amp; Activity :</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>A. Global Market Influence :</strong> Global sentiment remains mixed as major indices show varied movements. While the S&amp;P 500, Nasdaq, and Dow Jones gained in the latest session, European markets like FTSE 100, DAX, and CAC 40 also trended higher. In Asia, the Nikkei posted gains of 1.76 percent, whereas the Hang Seng index declined by 0.58 percent, providing a diverse set of cues for domestic market participants.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>B. FIIs Activity :</strong> Foreign Institutional Investors were net sellers in the cash market, offloading shares worth 1462 crore. Such institutional outflows often influence market liquidity and could contribute to the prevailing cautious sentiment observed among participants as they assess the broader impact of these consistent selling patterns on domestic price discovery.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>C. DIIs Activity :</strong> Domestic Institutional Investors provided a cushion to the market by net buying shares worth 2610 crore. This sustained participation from local institutions often acts as a stabilizing force, potentially helping to absorb selling pressure and providing support to the overall market structure during periods of volatility in the morning session.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Macroeconomic, Energy &amp; Currency Drivers :</strong> Brent crude prices have eased to 109.74 per barrel, reflecting a decline of 5.24 percent, which may offer some relief to the domestic economy. The US Dollar Index stands at 102.1, up 0.13 percent, while the Rupee weakened against the US dollar to 95.14, a change of 0.21 percent. These macroeconomic variables, alongside global inflationary trends and interest rate expectations, remain key factors that investors monitor for their impact on corporate margins and capital flows.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Sector Wise Performance :</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Top Gainers</strong></p>\r\n<ul style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong>Pharma :</strong> This sector leads with a gain of 1.99 percent, reflecting positive momentum in the morning session as investors rotate into defensive and growth-oriented healthcare stocks.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Realty :</strong> The sector has advanced by 1.53 percent, indicating continued interest in property-related equities as market participants evaluate sectoral performance amidst the ongoing quarterly earnings season.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Top Losers</strong></p>\r\n<ul style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li><strong>IT :</strong> The sector is the weakest, declining by 1.69 percent, as investors react to ongoing earnings reports and global demand concerns affecting the technology services landscape.</li>\r\n<li><strong>FMCG :</strong> The index has slipped by 0.40 percent, showing a cautious trend as market participants weigh the impact of input costs and demand fluctuations on consumer goods companies.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Market Sentiment &amp; Technical Analysis :</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Market Breadth &amp; Volatility :</strong> The market breadth remains positive with 28 advances against 22 declines. Simultaneously, the India VIX has cooled by 1.21 percent to 16.95. This combination of a positive advance-decline ratio and a lower volatility index suggests that investors are maintaining a relatively stable outlook despite the marginal index fluctuations.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>A. Downside Levels :</strong></p>\r\n<ul style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li>22630 and 22510 support levels</li>\r\n<li>20-day moving average at 22678.25</li>\r\n<li>Breakdown zone below 22510</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>B. Upside Levels :</strong></p>\r\n<ul style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li>22880 and 23000 resistance levels</li>\r\n<li>50-day moving average at 23337.08 and 200-day moving average at 24091.48</li>\r\n<li>Breakout zone above 23000</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Session Outlook &amp; Key Triggers :</strong></p>\r\n<ul style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<li>Ongoing Q2 results including Paytm, Tata Consumer, Mankind Pharma, REC, IOB, Ather Energy, Aegis Logistics, Supreme Ind, ITC Hotels, and Sumitomo Chemical</li>\r\n<li>Recent DAC proposals worth 2.12 lakh crore impacting defence stocks like HAL, BEL, and Paras Defence.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The market continues to trade within a narrow range as participants digest a flurry of quarterly results and global cues. With the index hovering near its 20-day moving average, the trend for the remainder of the session may depend on institutional flows and the reaction to specific corporate earnings announcements scheduled for today.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Recommendation :</strong> Neutral Editorial Assessment &ndash; No Buy / Sell Fully Recommendation.</p>','news/nifty-20261027-111126.jpg','active',0,36,'2026-10-27 05:41:26','2026-10-28 03:20:38'),
(16,'Nifty Derivative Market Trend Analysis : Nifty Trades Lower Amid Volatility As Investors Evaluate Corporate Earnings','nifty','The Indian equity market is experiencing a cautious afternoon session, with the Nifty 50 trading at 22690.25, reflecting a decline of 62.95 points or 0.28 percent from its previous close. The index opened at 22708.8, mar...','<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Indian equity market is experiencing a cautious afternoon session, with the Nifty 50 trading at 22690.25, reflecting a decline of 62.95 points or 0.28 percent from its previous close. The index opened at 22708.8, marking a gap down of 44.4 points. Similarly, the Sensex is down by 249.82 points or 0.34 percent at 73356.93. The banking sector faces pressure as well, with the Bank Nifty currently positioned at 54051, showing a decline of 0.58 percent during the ongoing trade.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Market Behaviour &amp; Activity :</strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>A. Global Market Influence :</strong> Global markets present a mixed picture today. In the latest session, US indices like the S&amp;P 500 rose 0.70 percent, the Nasdaq added 0.82 percent, and the Dow Jones climbed 0.28 percent. Conversely, European markets saw declines, with the FTSE 100 down 1.01 percent, the DAX off 0.19 percent, and the CAC 40 down 0.44 percent. Meanwhile, the Nikkei gained 1.73 percent, while the Hang Seng slipped 0.73 percent.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>B. FIIs Activity :</strong> Foreign Institutional Investors were net sellers in the cash market, offloading shares worth 1462 crore. Such consistent outflows from foreign participants often influence market liquidity and may contribute to the prevailing cautious sentiment observed among domestic investors as they navigate the current volatility in the broader indices.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>C. DIIs Activity :</strong> Domestic Institutional Investors provided a cushion to the market by net buying shares worth 2610 crore. Their sustained participation serves as a stabilizing force, helping to absorb the selling pressure generated by foreign institutional outflows and supporting the overall market structure during periods of intraday price fluctuations.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Macroeconomic, Energy &amp; Currency Drivers :</strong> Macroeconomic indicators show Brent crude at 111.31 per barrel, marking a decline of 3.89 percent. The US Dollar Index stands at 102.17, up 0.21 percent, while the Rupee weakened against the US dollar to 95.16, a change of 0.23 percent. These factors, alongside global monetary policy trends and inflation concerns, remain critical for market participants as they assess the impact on corporate costs and the broader economic environment in the coming sessions.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Sector Wise Performance :</strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Top Gainers</strong></p>\n<ul><li><strong>Realty :</strong> This sector leads the market today with a gain of 1.98 percent, reflecting positive sentiment in the real estate space during the afternoon trading session.</li><li><strong>Pharma :</strong> The sector follows with an increase of 1.64 percent, indicating renewed interest from investors as they shift focus toward defensive segments amid the ongoing market volatility.</li></ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Top Losers</strong></p>\n<ul><li><strong>IT :</strong> The sector is the weakest performer today, declining by 0.67 percent as investors react to broader market trends and potential shifts in global demand outlooks.</li><li><strong>Banking :</strong> The sector is trading lower by 0.58 percent, mirroring the overall negative sentiment in the financial space and contributing to the downward pressure on the main indices.</li></ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Market Sentiment &amp; Technical Analysis :</strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Market Breadth &amp; Volatility :</strong> The market breadth is currently negative, with 23 stocks advancing against 27 declines. The India VIX has eased by 2.39 percent to 16.75, suggesting a slight reduction in expected market volatility. This narrow advance-decline ratio highlights the ongoing struggle between buyers and sellers during the current trading day.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>A. Downside Levels :</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Immediate support at 22630 and 22510</li><li>20-day moving average at 22675.37</li><li>Crucial breakdown zone at 22510</li></ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>B. Upside Levels :</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Immediate resistance at 22880 and 23000</li><li>50-day moving average at 23335.93 and 200-day moving average at 24091.19</li><li>Breakout zone at 23000</li></ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Session Outlook &amp; Key Triggers :</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Defence stocks continue to rally following news that the DAC cleared proposals worth 2.12 lakh crore</li><li>Investors are tracking ongoing quarterly results for companies including Paytm, Tata Consumer, Mankind Pharma, REC, IOB, Ather Energy, Aegis Logistics, Supreme Ind, ITC Hotels, and Sumitomo Chemical.</li></ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The market remains in a consolidation phase, with the Nifty hovering near its 20-day moving average. While defence stocks show strength due to policy developments, the broader index reflects caution. Investors may continue to monitor global cues and incoming corporate results for further direction as the session progresses toward the close.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Recommendation :</strong> Neutral Editorial Assessment – No Buy / Sell Fully Recommendation.</p>','news/nifty-20261027-140219.jpg','active',0,72,'2026-10-27 08:32:19','2026-10-28 04:05:43'),
(17,'Nifty Derivative Market Trend Analysis : Nifty Ends Flat Amid Mixed Sectoral Performance And Volatility','nifty','The Indian equity market concluded the session on a muted note as the Nifty 50 settled at 22749.75 with a marginal decline of 3.45 points or 0.02 percent. The Sensex followed a similar trajectory, closing at 73598.67 aft...','<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Indian equity market concluded the session on a muted note as the Nifty 50 settled at 22749.75 with a marginal decline of 3.45 points or 0.02 percent. The Sensex followed a similar trajectory, closing at 73598.67 after shedding 8.08 points. Meanwhile, the Bank Nifty faced more pronounced pressure, retreating 0.72 percent to end at 53974.9. Market participants navigated a day of consolidation, with the index oscillating between a high of 22829.75 and a low of 22636.85 before finding stability at the close.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Market Behaviour &amp; Activity :</strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>A. Global Market Influence :</strong> Global sentiment remained varied during the latest session. In the United States, the S&amp;P 500 rose 0.70 percent, the Nasdaq gained 0.82 percent, and the Dow Jones added 0.28 percent. European indices showed a mixed performance with the DAX up 0.27 percent and the CAC 40 rising 0.42 percent, while the FTSE 100 declined 0.66 percent. Asian markets also diverged as the Nikkei climbed 1.73 percent.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>B. FIIs Activity :</strong> Foreign Institutional Investors were net sellers in the cash market, offloading shares worth 1462 crore. This sustained selling activity from foreign participants may continue to impact overall market liquidity and influence the short-term direction of domestic indices as investors monitor these capital flows closely in the coming sessions.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>C. DIIs Activity :</strong> Domestic Institutional Investors provided a cushion to the market by net purchasing shares worth 2610 crore. This consistent deployment of capital by domestic funds acts as a balancing force against foreign outflows, potentially offering some stability to the broader market structure during periods of heightened volatility or institutional selling.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Macroeconomic, Energy &amp; Currency Drivers :</strong> Energy and currency dynamics remained in focus as Brent crude traded at 109.75 per barrel, reflecting a decline of 5.23 percent. The US Dollar Index stood at 102.19, up 0.23 percent, while the Rupee weakened against the US dollar to 95.12. These macroeconomic variables may influence investor sentiment regarding inflationary pressures and the broader economic outlook, as market participants track how these global factors impact domestic corporate profitability and policy expectations.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Sector Wise Performance :</strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Top Gainers</strong></p>\n<ul><li><strong>Realty :</strong> This sector led the gains with an increase of 1.94 percent as investors showed renewed interest in the space during the latest trading session.</li><li><strong>Pharma :</strong> The sector followed with a rise of 1.91 percent, reflecting positive momentum as market participants rotated their capital into defensive segments amid the ongoing market consolidation.</li></ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Top Losers</strong></p>\n<ul><li><strong>Banking :</strong> The sector emerged as the weakest performer, declining 0.72 percent during the session as selling pressure weighed on major financial institutions.</li><li><strong>IT :</strong> The sector faced a marginal downturn, slipping 0.26 percent as market participants remained cautious regarding the near-term outlook for technology-focused companies in the current environment.</li></ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Market Sentiment &amp; Technical Analysis :</strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Market Breadth &amp; Volatility :</strong> The market breadth remained perfectly balanced with 25 advances and 25 declines, indicating a neutral sentiment among participants. Simultaneously, the India VIX eased by 4.41 percent to 16.4, suggesting a reduction in expected volatility and a relatively calmer environment for traders as the market maintains its current consolidation phase.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>A. Downside Levels :</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Immediate support levels at 22740 and 22650</li><li>20-day moving average at 22678.42</li><li>Crucial breakdown zone near 22650.</li></ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>B. Upside Levels :</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Immediate resistance levels at 22840 and 22930</li><li>50-day moving average at 23337.15 and 200-day moving average at 24091.5</li><li>Potential breakout zone near 22930.</li></ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Next Session Outlook &amp; Key Triggers :</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Defence stocks including Apollo Micro, Paras Defence, BEL, and HAL to remain in focus following DAC proposal clearances</li><li>Upcoming corporate results for Paytm, KFin Tech, and Nazara</li><li>Ongoing market reaction to Q2 results from Maruti Suzuki, Tata Consumer, and Aequs.</li></ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The market appears to be in a phase of consolidation, balancing between institutional selling and domestic buying support. Investors may continue to monitor sectoral rotation and the impact of ongoing corporate earnings on index movements. Maintaining a focus on defined support and resistance levels could be prudent as the market seeks a clear trend in the next session.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Recommendation :</strong> Neutral Editorial Assessment – No Buy / Sell Fully Recommendation.</p>','news/nifty-20261027-170027-redrawn2.jpg','active',1,36,'2026-10-27 11:30:27','2026-10-28 05:00:23');
INSERT INTO `technical_analyses` VALUES
(9,'Adani Ensol Technical View: Trend, Momentum & Price Levels',NULL,'1270','1256','1293 - 1303','Adani Ensol is the subject of this technical analysis, which delves into its share price movement in relation to key support and resistance levels, specifically ₹1256 as support and ₹1293 - 1303 as resistance. This type...','<p>Adani Ensol is the subject of this technical analysis, which delves into its share price movement in relation to key support and resistance levels, specifically ₹1256 as support and ₹1293 - 1303 as resistance. This type of analysis is crucial for understanding the potential direction and momentum of the stock.</p>\r\n<p>The support level of ₹1256 is a critical price point because it is where buyers have historically demonstrated a willingness to buy, thus preventing the stock\'s price from declining further. This level essentially acts as a floor, where the demand for the stock is sufficient to offset the selling pressure. Buyers often step in near this level, anticipating that the stock will rebound from here.</p>\r\n<p>The resistance level, ranging from ₹1293 to 1303, signifies a price zone where selling interest is typically strong. Sellers often emerge at this level to sell the stock, effectively capping its upward trajectory. This resistance level acts as a ceiling, limiting the stock\'s ability to ascend unless there is substantial buying interest to push through it.</p>\r\n<p>A move above the resistance level or below the support level may generally indicate a shift in the stock\'s trend. A breakout above the resistance level could suggest increased buying interest, while a breakdown below the support level might indicate increased selling pressure. Traders usually look for volume to confirm such moves, as high volume can signify a more significant shift in market sentiment, making the move more credible and potentially sustainable.</p>','technical-analysis/bLFsPixtlDcHtFItSR67oojIvaV270gmDGEu7PU6.jpg','active','2026-10-13','2026-10-12 08:39:36','2026-10-13 06:10:14'),
(10,'Reliance Industries Technical Analysis : Trend, Support & Resistance',NULL,'1160','1153','1174 - 1180','Reliance Industries Limited : Financial Performance, Growth Outlook and Risk Assessment Report Date : 12 October 2026 NSE Symbol : RELIANCE | BSE Code: 500325 Sector : Energy, Telecom, Retail and New Energy Recommendatio...','<h2>Reliance Industries Limited : Financial Performance, Growth Outlook and Risk Assessment</h2>\r\n<p><strong>Report Date :</strong> 12 October 2026<br><strong>NSE Symbol :</strong> RELIANCE | <strong>BSE Code:</strong> 500325<br><strong>Sector :</strong> Energy, Telecom, Retail and New Energy<br><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong>Recommendation :</strong> Neutral Editorial Assessment &ndash; No Buy/Sell Recommendation</span></p>\r\n<p>Reliance Industries Limited (RIL) is one of India\'s largest diversified conglomerates, operating across oil-to-chemicals, telecommunications, organised retail, oil and gas exploration, media and renewable energy. Its diversified business model provides exposure to India\'s expanding digital economy, consumer spending and energy requirements.</p>\r\n<h3>Financial Performance :</h3>\r\n<p>For the quarter ended June 2026 (Q1 FY2026&ndash;27), Reliance Industries reported consolidated revenue from operations of approximately ₹3.12 lakh crore, representing year-on-year growth of 25.4%.&nbsp;Consolidated EBITDA stood at approximately ₹51,403 crore, increasing 9.9%, while net profit attributable to shareholders was approximately ₹20,946 crore, declining 22.3% year-on-year.</p>\r\n<p>Although revenue and operating earnings improved, lower reported profitability highlights the importance of monitoring margins, financing expenses, other income and cash generation.</p>\r\n<h3>Business Segment Analysis :</h3>\r\n<p><strong>Oil-to-Chemicals:</strong> Refining and petrochemical operations remain significant revenue contributors. Profitability depends on crude oil prices, refining margins, petrochemical spreads and international demand.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Reliance Jio:</strong> Digital services offer growth opportunities through mobile connectivity, broadband, enterprise solutions and digital platforms. Subscriber additions, average revenue per user and network investments remain important performance indicators.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Reliance Retail:</strong> The retail business benefits from India\'s expanding consumer market. Store productivity, consumption trends, operating efficiency and competitive pricing influence profitability.</p>\r\n<p><strong>New Energy:</strong> Investments in solar manufacturing, battery storage and green hydrogen could support long-term diversification. However, these businesses require substantial capital expenditure and successful commercial execution.</p>\r\n<h3>Technical Trend and Share Price Outlook</h3>\r\n<p>Reliance Industries has experienced selling pressure amid broader market uncertainty. The ₹ 1153 &ndash;₹ 1140 range represents an indicative support zone, while ₹ 1174 &ndash;₹ 1180 remains an important resistance area. Sustained movement above resistance could improve technical sentiment, whereas weakness below support may increase selling pressure.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">These technical levels are indicative and should not be interpreted as trading recommendations.</span></p>\r\n<h3>Growth Opportunities</h3>\r\n<p>Reliance\'s long-term opportunities include increasing digital penetration, higher telecom monetisation, organised retail expansion, consumer brands and India\'s transition towards cleaner energy.</p>\r\n<p>The company\'s diversified operations may support future revenue growth. Nevertheless, sustainable profitability will depend on operating efficiency, disciplined capital allocation and returns from new investments.</p>\r\n<h3>Key Risk Factors</h3>\r\n<p>Major risks include volatile crude oil prices, weakening petrochemical margins, global economic uncertainty, currency fluctuations and competitive pressures.&nbsp;Substantial capital expenditure, project execution delays, regulatory changes and financing costs could also influence earnings and shareholder returns.</p>\r\n<p>Foreign institutional investment flows, interest rates and geopolitical developments may affect short-term share-price movements.</p>\r\n<h3>Investment Point Editorial Assessment</h3>\r\n<p>Reliance Industries maintains a diversified business portfolio with established market positions. Digital services, retail and new-energy initiatives provide potential growth opportunities.&nbsp;However, <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">investors should evaluate consolidated earnings, debt, free cash flow, valuations and capital expenditure before making investment / financial decisions.</span></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>Disclaimer:</strong> This report is intended exclusively for educational and informational purposes. It does not constitute investment advice or a Buy, Sell or Hold recommendation. Securities investments are subject to market risks. Readers should independently verify financial information and consult appropriately registered professionals when necessary.</p>','technical-analysis/SKCgvwxFfo27AgB8i8r30T2NGUAuUhEaBIYQqJKZ.jpg','active','2026-10-13','2026-10-12 14:28:02','2026-10-13 06:10:05'),
(11,'JSW STEEL Technical Analysis : Trend, Support & Resistance',NULL,'1173','1765','1183 - 1190','Report Date: 13 October 2026 NSE Symbol: JSWSTEEL | BSE Code: 500228 Sector: Iron & Steel – Metals & Mining Recommendation: Neutral Editorial Assessment – No Buy / Sell Recommendation JSW Steel Limited is one of India\'s...','<p>Report Date: 13 October 2026<br>NSE Symbol: JSWSTEEL | BSE Code: 500228<br>Sector: Iron &amp; Steel &ndash; Metals &amp; Mining<br><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Recommendation: Neutral Editorial Assessment &ndash; No Buy / Sell Recommendation</span></p>\r\n<p>JSW Steel Limited is one of India\'s leading integrated steel manufacturers, supplying products to infrastructure, construction, automobiles, engineering and manufacturing industries. Its operations include flat steel, long steel and value-added products. Business performance depends on domestic steel demand, raw material costs, capacity utilisation and international steel prices.</p>\r\n<h3>Latest Financial Performance</h3>\r\n<p>For Q1 FY2026&ndash;27, ended June 2026, JSW Steel reported consolidated revenue of ₹47,364 crore and EBITDA of ₹9,383 crore. Consolidated profit after tax reached ₹4,696 crore, compared with ₹2,209 crore in the corresponding previous-year quarter.&nbsp;Crude steel production stood at 6.59 million tonnes, while steel sales reached 6.25 million tonnes. Net debt was approximately ₹46,157 crore as of 30 June 2026.</p>\r\n<p>Improved profitability reflects stronger operating performance, although steel-price volatility and raw material expenses remain important considerations.</p>\r\n<h3>Technical Analysis :</h3>\r\n<p>On 12 October 2026, JSW Steel traded around ₹ 1173. The technical structure indicated a bearish short-term trend, with the share price below important moving averages. The 14-day Relative Strength Index (RSI) was approximately 31, suggesting weak momentum and proximity to oversold conditions. The negative MACD also indicated prevailing selling pressure.&nbsp;The 20-day moving average was approximately ₹1253, while the 50-day moving average stood near ₹1,281. Trading below these averages indicates that sustained recovery has not yet been established.</p>\r\n<p>Sustained movement above ₹ 1183&ndash;₹ 1190, supported by improving volumes, could indicate recovering momentum. Subsequent resistance lies near ₹ 1203 and ₹ 1212.</p>\r\n<p>Weakness below ₹1165 may increase downside pressure towards ₹ 1157 and ₹ 1140. A temporary oversold recovery would not independently confirm a trend reversal.</p>\r\n<h3>Growth Opportunities</h3>\r\n<p>India\'s infrastructure development, urbanisation, industrial expansion and manufacturing investment support long-term steel consumption.</p>\r\n<p>JSW Steel\'s capacity expansion, operational efficiency and value-added product portfolio may contribute to future growth. However, returns depend on demand conditions, pricing discipline and capital expenditure execution.</p>\r\n<h3>Key Risk Factors :</h3>\r\n<p>Major risks include fluctuating iron ore and coking coal prices, steel imports, international trade restrictions, global economic slowdown and rising financing costs.</p>\r\n<p>High capital requirements, environmental regulations and changing steel demand may influence profitability. Investors should monitor debt, operating cash flows and quarterly margins.</p>\r\n<h3>Investment Point Editorial Assessment :</h3>\r\n<p>JSW Steel demonstrates substantial manufacturing capabilities and exposure to India\'s industrial growth. Recent quarterly profitability improved, but its short-term technical trend remains weak.&nbsp;A sustained recovery above resistance, accompanied by stronger volumes, would provide additional evidence of improving market sentiment.</p>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Overall Assessment : Neutral &ndash; Observation-Based. No Buy, Sell or Hold recommendation or target price is assigned.</span></p>\r\n<p>This report is intended for educational and informational purposes only. It does not constitute personalised investment advice or a securities recommendation. Technical levels may change without notice. Investments in securities markets are subject to market risks.</p>','technical-analysis/i1UmkMLvCQZzRRxtqqfoy26MZDUOJAScKniDrq0c.jpg','active','2026-10-13','2026-10-12 14:51:46','2026-10-13 06:09:52'),
(12,'Bharti Artl Technical Analysis : Trend, Support & Resistance',NULL,'1779','1764','1794-1808','Bharti Airtel Limited : Technical Analysis – Trend, Support & Resistance Report Date : 12 October 2026 NSE Symbol: BHARTIARTL | BSE Code: 532454 Sector: Telecommunications – Telecom Services Recommendation : Neutral Edit...','<h2>Bharti Airtel Limited : Technical Analysis &ndash; Trend, Support &amp; Resistance</h2>\r\n<p>Report Date : 12 October 2026 NSE Symbol: BHARTIARTL | BSE Code: 532454 Sector: Telecommunications &ndash; Telecom Services</p>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Recommendation : Neutral Editorial Assessment &ndash; No Buy/Sell Recommendation</span></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p>Bharti Airtel Limited is one of India\'s leading telecommunications companies, providing mobile connectivity, broadband, digital television, enterprise communication and digital services. Its operations extend across India and several African markets.</p>\r\n<p>The company\'s business performance depends on subscriber growth, average revenue per user (ARPU), network investment, operating efficiency and increasing demand for digital connectivity.</p>\r\n<h3>Latest Financial Performance :</h3>\r\n<p>For the quarter ended June 2026 (Q1 FY2026&ndash;27), Bharti Airtel reported consolidated revenue of approximately ₹58,539 crore, representing year-on-year growth of 18.4%.&nbsp;Consolidated EBITDA stood at approximately ₹33,599 crore, with an EBITDA margin of 57.4%.&nbsp;India revenue reached ₹41,214 crore, reflecting 9.7% annual growth. India mobile ARPU improved to ₹264 compared with ₹250 in the corresponding previous-year quarter.The company reported a customer base of approximately 681 million across 15 countries.</p>\r\n<p>These results demonstrate revenue expansion and improved customer monetisation. However, profitability and cash generation remain sensitive to capital expenditure, financing costs and competitive conditions.</p>\r\n<h3>Technical Analysis :&ndash;</h3>\r\n<p>On 12 October 2026, Bharti Airtel traded around ₹1,779, reflecting continued short-term selling pressure.&nbsp;The stock remained below its 20-day and 50-day simple moving averages, indicating a weak near-term technical structure.&nbsp;The 14-day Relative Strength Index (RSI) stood around 46.64, suggesting neutral-to-weak momentum rather than deeply oversold conditions.</p>\r\n<p>A negative MACD reading also indicated that bearish momentum remained present.</p>\r\n<p>A sustained recovery above important moving averages would be required before interpreting the price action as a stronger technical reversal.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Support and Resistance Levels :</span>&nbsp;</h3>\r\n<p>A sustained recovery above ₹ 1794&ndash;₹ 1808, supported by stronger trading volumes, could indicate improving short-term sentiment. Subsequent resistance is located near ₹ 1820.</p>\r\n<p>Continued trading <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">below ₹ 1764 may indicate persistent weakness</span>. Further downside levels require confirmation from updated price charts and recent swing lows.</p>\r\n<p>Technical indicators should be considered alongside price action, volumes and broader market conditions.</p>\r\n<h3>Growth Opportunities</h3>\r\n<p>India\'s expanding digital economy, increasing data consumption, 5G adoption, broadband penetration and enterprise connectivity provide potential long-term growth opportunities.</p>\r\n<p>Improvement in ARPU, customer retention and operating efficiency may support future financial performance.</p>\r\n<h3>Key Risk Factors</h3>\r\n<p>Major risks include intense industry competition, regulatory changes, spectrum-related obligations, substantial network expenditure, currency fluctuations and debt-servicing requirements.</p>\r\n<p>African operations also face exchange-rate and geopolitical uncertainties.</p>\r\n<h3>Investment Point Editorial Assessment</h3>\r\n<p>Bharti Airtel maintains an established telecommunications business with improving revenue and customer monetisation. Nevertheless, its short-term technical indicators reflect cautious market sentiment.</p>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Overall Assessment : Neutral and Observation-Based. No target price or Buy, Sell or Hold recommendation is assigned.</span></p>\r\n<p>This report is intended exclusively for educational and informational purposes. It does not constitute personalised investment advice or a recommendation to transact in securities. Technical levels may change without notice. Investments in securities markets are subject to market risks.</p>\r\n</div>','technical-analysis/xXbyUszSQwusxTyYSomsB3GJGd4vVGnLKbRJBzMS.jpg','active','2026-10-13','2026-10-12 15:07:49','2026-10-13 06:09:40'),
(13,'Adani Ports Technical Analysis: Trend, Support & Resistance',NULL,'1755','1740','1778 - 1790','Report Date: 13 October 2026 NSE Symbol: ADANIPORTS | BSE Code: 532921 Sector: Infrastructure – Ports, Logistics & Marine Services Recommendation: Neutral Editorial Assessment – No Buy / Sell Recommendation Adani Ports a...','<p>Report Date: 13 October 2026<br>NSE Symbol: ADANIPORTS | BSE Code: 532921<br>Sector: Infrastructure &ndash; Ports, Logistics &amp; Marine Services<br><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Recommendation: Neutral Editorial Assessment &ndash; No Buy / Sell Recommendation</span></p>\r\n<p>Adani Ports and Special Economic Zone Limited (APSEZ) is India\'s largest integrated transport operator, with businesses spanning domestic and international ports, logistics, marine services and special economic zones.</p>\r\n<p>Its operations support international trade, industrial activity, container transportation and India\'s expanding logistics infrastructure. Business performance depends on cargo volumes, port utilisation, operating margins and global trade conditions.</p>\r\n<h3>Latest Financial Performance</h3>\r\n<p>For Q1 FY2026&ndash;27, ended June 2026, Adani Ports reported consolidated revenue of ₹10,821 crore, representing 19% year-on-year growth. Consolidated EBITDA increased 19% to ₹6,541 crore, while profit after tax rose 10% to ₹3,650 crore. Domestic cargo volumes reached 115.3 million metric tonnes. International ports revenue increased 80%, reflecting business expansion and contributions from overseas operations.</p>\r\n<p>The company\'s net debt-to-EBITDA ratio stood at approximately 1.9 times. These results indicate operational growth, although future performance remains dependent on cargo demand, capital expenditure and international economic conditions.</p>\r\n<h3>Technical Analysis &ndash; Market Trend</h3>\r\n<p>On 12 October 2026, Adani Ports traded around ₹1755.</p>\r\n<p>The technical structure indicated a broadly positive medium-term trend with short-term consolidation.&nbsp;The 14-day Relative Strength Index (RSI) stood near 50.94, indicating neutral momentum without significant overbought or oversold conditions.&nbsp;The stock traded below its 20-day simple moving average of approximately ₹ 1770 but remained above its 50-day moving average of ₹ 1721 and 200-day moving average of ₹ 1634.</p>\r\n<p>This combination suggests short-term hesitation within a relatively stronger longer-term price structure.</p>\r\n<h3>Support and Resistance Levels :</h3>\r\n<p>Sustained movement above ₹ 1760, accompanied by improving trading volumes, could indicate strengthening momentum. Subsequent resistance levels are located near ₹ 1778-1790.</p>\r\n<p>Weakness below the ₹ 1740 may indicate deteriorating short-term sentiment. Further support is positioned near ₹ 1727 followed by ₹ 1720.</p>\r\n<p>Neither scenario represents a prediction or trading recommendation.</p>\r\n<h3>Growth Opportunities</h3>\r\n<p>India\'s expanding international trade, industrial infrastructure and container transportation requirements provide potential long-term growth opportunities.</p>\r\n<p>Adani Ports\' capacity expansion, integrated logistics operations and international presence may support business diversification and operating efficiencies.</p>\r\n<p>However, successful project execution and financial discipline remain essential.</p>\r\n<h3>Key Risk Factors</h3>\r\n<p>Major risks include global trade disruptions, geopolitical uncertainty, shipping-route disturbances, currency fluctuations and changing cargo demand.</p>\r\n<p>Other considerations include infrastructure investment requirements, regulatory developments, debt servicing and competition from domestic and international port operators.</p>\r\n<h3>Investment Point Editorial Assessment</h3>\r\n<p>Adani Ports demonstrates improving financial performance and an expanding transport infrastructure business.&nbsp;Its medium-term technical structure remains relatively constructive, while near-term price movement suggests consolidation.&nbsp;Investors should independently examine valuations, financial disclosures, operating cash flows and market risks.</p>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Overall Assessment: Neutral and Observation-Based. No target price or Buy, Sell or Hold recommendation is assigned.</span></p>\r\n<p>This report is intended exclusively for educational and informational purposes. It does not constitute personalised investment advice or a securities recommendation. Technical levels are subject to change. Investments in securities markets are subject to market risks.</p>','technical-analysis/TQnm1pAVcVUFHZ5NTkzaE750X9g4PXcvEgvrCo12.jpg','active','2026-10-13','2026-10-12 15:18:25','2026-10-13 06:09:30'),
(14,'Tech Mahindra Technical Analysis : Trend , Support & Resistance',NULL,'1774',NULL,NULL,'Report Date : 16 October 2026 NSE Symbol : TECHM | BSE Code : 532755 Sector : Information Technology – IT Services Recommendation : Neutral Editorial Assessment – No Buy / Sell Recommendation Tech Mahindra Limited is a g...','<p><strong>Report Date :</strong> 16 October 2026</p>\r\n<p><strong>NSE Symbol :</strong> TECHM | <strong>BSE Code :</strong> 532755</p>\r\n<p><strong>Sector :</strong> Information Technology &ndash; IT Services</p>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Recommendation : Neutral Editorial Assessment &ndash; No Buy / Sell Recommendation</span></p>\r\n<p>Tech Mahindra Limited is a global technology services and consulting company providing digital transformation cloud computing artificial intelligence engineering and business process services. The company serves clients across telecommunications manufacturing banking and financial services. Its business performance depends on technology spending global demand client relationships and the execution of digital transformation projects.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Market trend :</strong></p>\r\n<p>Tech Mahindra reported encouraging second-quarter FY27 results on 15 October 2026. Revenue reached ₹16180 crore marking 15.6% year-on-year growth while consolidated net profit increased 32.7% to ₹1586 crore. Operating margin improved to 14.8% and new deal wins reached USD 1023 million. These figures indicate improved operating performance and business momentum.</p>\r\n<p>The stock gained approximately 8% on 16 October 2026 following the earnings announcement and stronger deal wins. The broader IT sector also rebounded as investors reassessed demand prospects and AI-related opportunities. Further market direction may depend on quarterly results revenue growth margin sustainability and global technology spending. Despite recent strength short-term volatility remains possible.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Risk fector :</strong></p>\r\n<p>Key risks include weaker global technology spending currency fluctuations rising competition and delays in client projects. Rapid AI adoption may disrupt traditional service models and require continued investment. Margin improvement and future growth depend on deal execution client demand and global economic conditions.</p>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Overall Assessment : Neutral and Observation-Based. No target price or Buy / Sell or Hold recommendation is assigned.</span></p>\r\n<p>This report is intended exclusively for educational and journalism purposes. It does not constitute personalised investment advice or a securities recommendation. Technical levels are subject to change. Investments in securities markets are subject to market risks.</p>','technical-analysis/gvpqPWPpBAzIR03tvhQHLwgYGeRj2dIf7m7XrrIM.jpg','active','2026-10-16','2026-10-16 12:22:00','2026-10-17 12:04:17'),
(15,'Infosys Technical Analysis : Trend , Support & Resistance',NULL,'1164',NULL,NULL,'Report Date : 16 October 2026 NSE Symbol : INFY | BSE Code : 500209 Sector : Information Technology – IT Services Recommendation : Neutral Editorial Assessment – No Buy / Sell Recommendation Infosys Limited is a global i...','<p><strong>Report Date :</strong> 16 October 2026</p>\r\n<p><strong>NSE Symbol :</strong> INFY | <strong>BSE Code :</strong> 500209</p>\r\n<p><strong>Sector :</strong> Information Technology &ndash; IT Services</p>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Recommendation : Neutral Editorial Assessment &ndash; No Buy / Sell Recommendation</span></p>\r\n<p>Infosys Limited is a global information technology services and consulting company headquartered in Bengaluru. It provides digital transformation services including artificial intelligence cloud computing software development cybersecurity and business consulting. Its business performance depends on global technology spending client demand operational efficiency and its ability to deliver emerging technology solutions across international markets.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Market trend :</strong></p>\r\n<p>Infosys reported first-quarter FY27 revenue of ₹49195 crore representing 13.6% year-on-year growth. Consolidated net profit reached ₹11028 crore increasing 12.3% year-on-year although it declined 8.6% sequentially. Market participants are monitoring revenue growth operating margins and management commentary ahead of the second-quarter results scheduled for 23 October 2026.</p>\r\n<p>On 16 October 2026 Infosys shares advanced alongside other major Indian IT stocks amid a broader sector recovery. The Nifty IT index recorded strong weekly gains as investors reassessed technology demand and artificial intelligence-related developments. Future movement may depend on quarterly earnings guidance deal momentum global client spending and currency movements. Market volatility remains possible despite recent gains.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Risk fector :</strong></p>\r\n<p>Key risks include weaker international technology spending currency fluctuations rising competition and pricing pressure. Artificial intelligence may disrupt traditional outsourcing models and require additional investment. Revenue growth and profitability remain sensitive to client budgets project execution and global economic conditions.</p>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Overall Assessment: Neutral and Observation-Based. No target price or Buy / Sell or Hold recommendation is assigned.</span></p>\r\n<p>This report is intended exclusively for educational and journalism purposes. It does not constitute personalised investment advice or a securities recommendation. Technical levels are subject to change. Investments in securities markets are subject to market risks.</p>','technical-analysis/XOeJsbnwglZPpW0WpgrSZdTefQUUBvq2UUNiKvCf.jpg','active','2026-10-16','2026-10-16 12:27:26','2026-10-17 12:03:54'),
(16,'State Bank of India Technical Analysis : Trend , Support & Resistance',NULL,'962',NULL,NULL,'Report Date : 16 October 2026 NSE Symbol : SBIN | BSE Code : 500112 Sector : Banking – Public Sector Bank Recommendation : Neutral Editorial Assessment – No Buy / Sell Recommendation. State Bank of India is India\'s large...','<p><strong>Report Date :</strong> 16 October 2026</p>\r\n<p><strong>NSE Symbol :</strong> SBIN | <strong>BSE Code :</strong> 500112</p>\r\n<p><strong>Sector :</strong> Banking &ndash; Public Sector Bank</p>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Recommendation : Neutral Editorial Assessment &ndash; No Buy / Sell Recommendation.</span></p>\r\n<p>State Bank of India is India\'s largest public sector banking institution providing retail banking corporate banking loans deposits treasury services digital banking and financial products. Its business performance depends on credit growth deposit mobilisation interest rate movements asset quality and economic activity. The bank serves individuals businesses and government institutions across India and international markets.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Market trend :</strong></p>\r\n<p>State Bank of India shares closed at approximately ₹961.70 on 16 October 2026 registering a marginal daily gain. The movement occurred during a broadly positive market session. However the stock remained below its February 2026 high of ₹1234.80. Investors continue to monitor banking sector performance interest rate expectations and quarterly financial disclosures.</p>\r\n<p>The near-term outlook depends on loan growth deposit costs net interest margins and asset quality trends. Strong credit demand may support operating performance while rising funding costs or slower economic activity could pressure profitability. Broader market sentiment and institutional investment flows may also influence price fluctuations. These factors warrant continued observation without assuming a particular price direction.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Risk fector :</strong></p>\r\n<p>Key risks include rising deposit costs credit defaults pressure on net interest margins and regulatory changes. Economic slowdown may affect loan demand and repayment capacity. Market volatility and changes in interest rates could also influence profitability and investor sentiment.</p>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Overall Assessment : Neutral and Observation-Based. No target price or Buy / Sell or Hold recommendation is assigned.</span></p>\r\n<p>This report is intended exclusively for educational and journalism purposes. It does not constitute personalised investment advice or a securities recommendation. Technical levels are subject to change. Investments in securities markets are subject to market risks.</p>','technical-analysis/esutxYWx303tAA4PSeZoX6epTpbDPzOkzeO0tMLO.jpg','active','2026-10-16','2026-10-16 12:34:50','2026-10-17 12:03:39'),
(18,'HDFC Bank Technical Analysis : Trend Support & Resistance',NULL,'730',NULL,NULL,'Report Date : 17 October 2026 NSE Symbol : HDFCBANK | BSE Code : 500180 Sector : Banking – Private Sector Bank HDFC Bank Limited is a leading Indian private sector bank offering retail banking corporate banking loans dep...','<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Report Date :</strong> 17 October 2026</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>NSE Symbol :</strong> HDFCBANK | <strong>BSE Code :</strong> 500180</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Sector :</strong> Banking &ndash; Private Sector Bank</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">HDFC Bank Limited is a leading Indian private sector bank offering retail banking corporate banking loans deposits credit cards and digital financial services. Its performance depends on credit growth deposit mobilisation interest margins asset quality and operating efficiency. The bank serves individuals businesses and institutions through its extensive branch network and digital platforms.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Market trend :</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">HDFC Bank closed at ₹728.85 on 16 October 2026 with a gain of ₹2.00. The share traded above its 20-day and 50-day moving averages while remaining below its 100-day and 200-day averages. The 14-day RSI stood near 55.3 indicating moderate positive momentum. These indicators present a mixed medium-term technical picture.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Risk fector :</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Key risks include rising deposit costs pressure on net interest margins deterioration in asset quality and slower credit growth. Regulatory changes and competition may affect profitability. Interest rate movements and broader market volatility can influence share prices. Technical support and resistance levels are not guaranteed and may fail during sharp market movements.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Recommendation : Neutral Editorial Assessment &ndash; No Buy / Sell Recommendation.</span></p>','technical-analysis/j4oCCfUqVg0mgLgyzeTm8pLF5rOCUfgjEeMK8xQV.jpg','active','2026-10-17','2026-10-17 08:12:05','2026-10-22 13:31:37'),
(20,'Adani Energy Solutions Technical Analysis : Trend Support & Resistance',NULL,'1260',NULL,NULL,'Name : Adani Energy Solutions Limited NSE Symbol : ADANIENSOL | BSE Code : 539254 Sector : Power Transmission and Distribution Dear Investors, Adani Energy Solutions Limited operates in electricity transmission and distr...','<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Name :</strong> Adani Energy Solutions Limited</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>NSE Symbol :</strong> ADANIENSOL | <strong>BSE Code :</strong> 539254</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Sector :</strong> Power Transmission and Distribution</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Dear Investors,</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Adani Energy Solutions Limited operates in electricity transmission and distribution and smart metering infrastructure. The company develops and manages power networks and provides related energy infrastructure services. Its business performance depends on infrastructure expansion regulatory approvals project execution electricity demand and capital investment.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Financial Performance :</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Over the five financial years from FY2022 to FY2026 consolidated sales increased from ₹11258 crore to ₹27588 crore. Revenue rose to ₹13293 crore in FY2023 and ₹16607 crore in FY2024 before reaching ₹23767 crore in FY2025. This reflects sustained business expansion alongside infrastructure development and smart metering growth.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Net profit stood at ₹1236 crore in FY2022 and ₹1281 crore in FY2023. It declined to ₹1196 crore in FY2024 and ₹922 crore in FY2025 before recovering to ₹2393 crore in FY2026. Operating profit increased from ₹4206 crore in FY2022 to ₹8005 crore in FY2026. Despite revenue growth investors should monitor debt levels financing costs cash flow and the sustainability of profit improvement.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Market trend :</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">On 26 October 2026 the share traded at ₹1241.80 gaining 1.80% during the morning session. The stock opened at ₹1221 and moved between ₹1207.50 and ₹1260.80. This rebound followed declines in the preceding sessions. The share remains below its 52-week high of ₹1789 indicating a significant retreat from its peak.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The immediate trend remains volatile. Traders may monitor the ₹1200 region as a nearby reference area while movement above the intraday high could indicate improving momentum. These are observational levels rather than confirmed technical signals. Fresh price action and trading volume remain important.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Risk fector :</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Key risks include high capital requirements debt servicing costs regulatory changes and delays in infrastructure projects. Changes in transmission tariffs and smart meter execution may affect earnings. Interest rate movements and refinancing needs can influence profitability. Project concentration and cash flow pressures also warrant attention. Short-term share price volatility may continue as investors reassess valuation and earnings expectations.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Recommendation : Neutral Editorial Assessment &ndash; No Buy / Sell Recommendation.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Report Date :</strong> 26 October 2026 | Monday</p>','technical-analysis/3oai8FniHUu7vWDPzowYAv4aub4CkMM9gADDEHle.jpg','active','2026-10-26','2026-10-26 11:05:04','2026-10-26 11:10:11'),
(21,'Godrej Properties Technical Analysis : Trend Support & Resistance',NULL,'1522',NULL,NULL,'Name : Godrej Properties Limited NSE Symbol : GODREJPROP | BSE Code : 533150 Sector : Real Estate – Property Development Dear Investors, Godrej Properties Limited is a real estate development company within the Godrej Gr...','<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Name :</strong> Godrej Properties Limited</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>NSE Symbol :</strong> GODREJPROP | <strong>BSE Code :</strong> 533150</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Sector :</strong> Real Estate &ndash; Property Development</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Dear Investors,</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Godrej Properties Limited is a real estate development company within the Godrej Group. It develops residential and commercial properties across major Indian cities. Its business performance depends on property demand sales bookings project execution land acquisition construction costs and prevailing interest rates.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Financial Performance :</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">During FY2022 to FY2026 consolidated sales increased from ₹1825 crore in FY2022 to ₹5131 crore in FY2026. Revenue rose to ₹2252 crore in FY2023 and ₹3036 crore in FY2024 before reaching ₹4923 crore in FY2025. This reflects expansion in reported revenue over the five-year period.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Net profit increased from ₹351 crore in FY2022 to ₹621 crore in FY2023 and ₹747 crore in FY2024. It rose further to ₹1389 crore in FY2025 and ₹1841 crore in FY2026. The growth indicates stronger reported earnings. Future performance will depend on project deliveries cash flow and the sustainability of property demand.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Market trend :</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">On 26 October 2026 Godrej Properties traded around ₹1518.60 after opening at ₹1500.00. The share moved between ₹1475.60 and ₹1547.20 during the session and gained approximately 1.48% against its previous close of ₹1496.50. Despite the daily recovery the share remains substantially below its 52-week high of ₹2352.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The near-term trend remains sensitive to trading volume broader market sentiment and real estate sector performance. Investors may monitor price stability around recent trading lows and the ability to sustain a recovery. These observations do not establish a confirmed breakout or reversal.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Risk fector :</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Key risks include slower property sales rising construction costs project delays and changes in borrowing rates. Real estate demand can weaken during economic uncertainty. Land acquisition and regulatory approvals may affect delivery schedules. Cash flow requirements and competition may influence profitability. Share prices can also react sharply to quarterly results and changes in investor sentiment.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Recommendation : Neutral Editorial Assessment &ndash; No Buy / Sell Recommendation.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Report Date :</strong> 26 October 2026 | Monday</p>','technical-analysis/OGlnQtm6HD77Kr20Gandkj111QMdhpUbjGw5v76y.jpg','active','2026-10-26','2026-10-26 11:10:00','2026-10-26 11:10:00'),
(22,'Godrej Consumer Products Technical Analysis : Trend Support & Resistance',NULL,'936',NULL,NULL,'Name : Godrej Consumer Products Limited NSE Symbol : GODREJCP | BSE Code : 532424 Sector : Fast-Moving Consumer Goods – Household and Personal Care Dear Investors, Godrej Consumer Products Limited is a consumer goods com...','<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Name :</strong> Godrej Consumer Products Limited</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>NSE Symbol :</strong> GODREJCP | <strong>BSE Code :</strong> 532424</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Sector :</strong> Fast-Moving Consumer Goods &ndash; Household and Personal Care</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Dear Investors,</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Godrej Consumer Products Limited is a consumer goods company manufacturing household insecticides personal care products soaps hair colours and air care products. Its business operates across India and international markets. Performance depends on consumer demand product innovation distribution strength input costs and overseas market conditions.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Financial Performance :</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">From FY2022 to FY2026 consolidated sales increased from ₹12276 crore to ₹15178 crore. Revenue reached ₹13316 crore in FY2023 and ₹14096 crore in FY2024 before moderating to ₹13997 crore in FY2025 and recovering in FY2026.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Net profit stood at ₹1783 crore in FY2022 and ₹1702 crore in FY2023. It declined to a loss of ₹561 crore in FY2024 before recovering to ₹1852 crore in FY2025 and ₹1861 crore in FY2026. Operating profit increased from ₹2409 crore to ₹3169 crore across the period. The FY2024 loss reflected an exceptional impact and highlights the importance of assessing underlying profitability.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Market trend :</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">On 26 October 2026 the share traded near ₹830.50 declining around 2.47% during the session. The price approached its reported 52-week low of ₹827 indicating continued selling pressure and weak short-term sentiment.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Investors may monitor trading volume consumer demand and upcoming quarterly results. A sustained recovery would require evidence of price stabilisation and improved market participation. Technical levels remain dynamic and should be interpreted alongside fresh exchange data.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Risk fector :</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Key risks include rising raw material costs weak consumer demand currency fluctuations and intense competition. International operations expose the company to regional economic uncertainty. Changes in product preferences and pricing pressures may affect margins. Exceptional expenses can distort reported earnings. Share price volatility may continue if quarterly performance or market expectations disappoint.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Recommendation : Neutral Editorial Assessment &ndash; No Buy / Sell Recommendation.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Report Date :</strong> 26 October 2026 | Monday</p>\r\n</div>','technical-analysis/MKMVyObbhvxdN4trpVgrBRbEHUPZdg6Aelx3lv1U.jpg','active','2026-10-26','2026-10-26 11:17:48','2026-10-26 11:17:48'),
(23,'ICICI Bank Technical Analysis : Trend Support & Resistance',NULL,'1396',NULL,NULL,'Name : ICICI Bank Limited NSE Symbol : ICICIBANK | BSE Code : 532174 Sector : Banking – Private Sector Bank Dear Investors, ICICI Bank Limited is a leading Indian private sector bank providing retail banking corporate ba...','<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Name :</strong> ICICI Bank Limited</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>NSE Symbol :</strong> ICICIBANK | <strong>BSE Code :</strong> 532174</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Sector :</strong> Banking &ndash; Private Sector Bank</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Dear Investors,</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">ICICI Bank Limited is a leading Indian private sector bank providing retail banking corporate banking loans deposits credit cards and digital financial services. Its performance depends on credit growth deposit mobilisation interest margins asset quality and economic conditions.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Financial Performance :</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">During FY2022 to FY2026 consolidated revenue increased from ₹95407 crore to ₹195218 crore. Revenue rose to ₹121067 crore in FY2023 and ₹159516 crore in FY2024 before reaching ₹186331 crore in FY2025. This reflects sustained expansion in business operations.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Net profit increased from ₹26538 crore in FY2022 to ₹35461 crore in FY2023 and ₹46081 crore in FY2024. It advanced to ₹54569 crore in FY2025 and ₹57936 crore in FY2026. Despite earnings growth investors should monitor deposit costs credit quality and net interest margins as these factors influence future profitability.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Market trend :</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">ICICI Bank shares experienced selling pressure during the early session on 26 October 2026 declining to an intraday low of ₹1378.70 from an opening price of ₹1394.20. The decline reflected short-term weakness although the share subsequently recovered towards ₹1402. The stock remains below its 52-week high of ₹1480 indicating scope for continued price fluctuations.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Immediate support may emerge near ₹1380 while resistance is observed around ₹1406 and ₹1419. A sustained move below support could indicate further weakness whereas a recovery above resistance may improve momentum. These levels are indicative and can change with market conditions.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Risk fector :</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Key risks include rising deposit costs pressure on net interest margins deterioration in asset quality and slower credit growth. Regulatory changes and competition may affect profitability. Economic uncertainty can weaken loan demand and repayment capacity. Short-term price volatility may continue amid changing market sentiment. Technical levels are not guaranteed and should be reassessed using updated exchange data.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Recommendation : Neutral Editorial Assessment &ndash; No Buy / Sell Recommendation.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Report Date :</strong> 26 October 2026 | Monday</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>','technical-analysis/x7raUnySWcPiYK4WXDN5l1IIDRrxZb0CTZOWHS83.jpg','active','2026-10-26','2026-10-26 11:23:36','2026-10-26 11:23:36');
