  \nClosed price : 1906\n\n·      \nStrong Support : 1934 /\n1940 / 1955\n\n·      \nResistance price : 1884 /\n1870\n\nReasons for Recommended –\nHdfc Bank Ltd. is exhibiting bearish signals across\nmultiple technical indicators.\n\n The RSI indicates that the stock is in\noversold conditions, which could lead to a potential reversal or consolidation.\n\n\nHowever, the\nMACD\'s position suggests ongoing bearish momentum. The moderate ADX value\nreflects a somewhat defined trend.\n\n The stock\'s position below both the 50-day and\n200-day SMAs points to potential short- to medium-term bearishness.\n​( 17 ) INFOSYS -\n\n·      \nClosed price : 1426\n\n·      \nStrong Support : 1447 /\n1460\n\n·      \nResistance price : 1397 /\n1390\n\nReasons for Recommended – The technical indicators for Infosys Ltd.\nsuggest a strong bearish trend. The stock is in oversold territory, indicating\npotential for a short-term rebound; however, the prevailing trend remains\ndownward. ( 18 ) RELIANCE -\n\n·      \nClosed price : 1271\n\n·      \nStrong Support : 1303 /\n1323 / 1330\n\n·      \nResistance price : 1255 /\n1230\n\nReasons for Recommended –\nThe stock\'s position below both the 50-day\nand 200-day SMAs points to potential short- to medium-term bearishness.\n​INVESTMENT STOCKS -\n\n( 19 )  SBFC FIN. -\n\n·      \nClosed price : 90\n\n·      \nStrong Support : 83\n\n·      \nResistance price : 103 /\n113 \n\nReasons for Recommended –\nSBFC Finance Ltd (NSE: SBFC) presents a\npromising long-term investment opportunity, particularly for investors with a\n3–5 year horizon. The company\'s robust growth trajectory, sound financials, and\nfavorable projections underscore its potential.\n\nRevenue &\nProfit Growth: SBFC Finance is projected to achieve annual revenue growth of\napproximately 21.6% and earnings growth of 21.5% over the next few years.\nEarnings per share (EPS) are expected to grow by 21.2% annually, with a\nforecasted return on equity (ROE) of 14.7% within three years. \n\nProfitability\nMetrics: The company reported a net income of ₹2.5 billion on revenues of ₹9.3 billion, resulting in a\nnet margin of 26.9%. Its profitability score stands at 49/100, indicating\nmoderate profitability with room\nfor improvement.\n\nSBFC Finance\nLtd demonstrates solid fundamentals and growth potential, making it a viable\noption for long-term investors.\n\n( 20 )  NHPC LTD -\n\n·      \nClosed price : 80\n\n·      \nStrong Support : 73\n\n·      \nResistance price : 93 /\n97 \n\nReasons for Recommended – NHPC Ltd \npresents a compelling long-term investment opportunity, particularly for\ninvestors interested in the renewable energy sector. The company\'s stable\nfinancials, government backing, and strategic focus on hydropower position it\nwell for sustained growth.\n\nRevenue Growth:\nIn FY2024, NHPC reported a total revenue of approximately ₹8,396.50 crore, marking a\nsignificant milestone in the company\'s financial performance. ​\n\nProfitability:\nThe company maintains a healthy net profit margin of 27.4%, indicating\nefficient operations. ​\n\nDebt Profile:\nNHPC has a debt-to-equity ratio of 0.79, reflecting a moderate debt level that\nis manageable given its stable cash flows.\n\nRenewable\nEnergy Focus: NHPC is actively expanding its renewable energy portfolio,\naligning with India\'s push for clean energy and favorable government policies.\n\nNHPC Ltd stands\nout as a stable and promising long-term investment, especially for those\nlooking to capitalize on the growth of renewable energy in India.\n\n ( 21 )  GATWAY DISTRIPARKS -\n\n·      \nClosed price : 58\n\n·      \nStrong Support : 53 / 48\n\n·      \nResistance price : 67 /\n75\n\nReasons for Recommended –\nGateway Distriparks Ltd presents a mixed\noutlook for long-term investors. While the company demonstrates financial\nstability and holds a significant position in India\'s logistics sector.\n\n Financial Overview (FY 2023–24) : Revenue: ₹1,536.13 crore,EBITDA: ₹396.68 crore & Net\nProfit (PAT): ₹258.27 crore, EBITDA Margin:\n26%.\n\nThese figures\nindicate a solid financial foundation with moderate leverage, suggesting the\ncompany is well-positioned to manage its obligations and invest in growth\nopportunities. \n\nGateway\nDistriparks Ltd exhibits financial stability and holds a strategic position in\nIndia\'s logistics industry. However, recent stock performance and moderate\ngrowth projections suggest that investors should approach with caution.\n\n( 22 )  IDFC FIRST BANK -\n\n·      \nClosed price : 57\n\n·      \nStrong Support : 50\n\n·      \nResistance price : 64 /\n70 / 77\n\nReasons for Recommended –\nIDFC First Bank Ltd exhibits a mixed\ntechnical outlook for long-term investors. While certain indicators suggest\nbullish momentum.\n\nMoving\nAverages: The stock is trading above its 50-day and 200-day Simple Moving\nAverages (SMAs), indicating a bullish trend.\n\nMACD (Moving\nAverage Convergence Divergence): The MACD indicator shows a value of 1.6, which\nis a bullish signal, indicating upward momentum.\n\nADX (Average\nDirectional Index): With an ADX value of 45.59, the trend strength is strong,\nsupporting the current bullish trend. IDFC First Bank Ltd presents a compelling\ncase for long-term investment.','active',NULL,'2026-09-25 07:23:03','2026-09-25 07:23:03'),
